{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons","id":71474,"title":"What does this have to do with Demons?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-13T11:42:51-08:00","id":71474,"title":"What does this have to do with Demons?","content":"On the one hand, I really like this splat. The world is literally the Matrix and &quot;Angels&quot; are the Agents who patrol and execute the processes of the Source. Sometimes those &quot;Angels&quot; go rogue and become &quot;Demons&quot; like Agent Smith, except that unlike Agent Smith you can barely defeat any other Agents and have to live your life paranoid that a bunch of Agents will hunt you down and recycle you. I love the thematic that they are hacking the source code of the universe, and every single one of them is a super spy who has to maintain his Cover (capital C) or risk his Cover being Compromised (capital C).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what does any of this have to do with the established mythology and tropes of angels or demons? Demon: the Fallen at least tried to invoke the general mythology with their own spin on things, but this feels no more like angels or demons than a wolf who wears sheep's clothing claiming to be a sheep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:02:10-08:00","id":71492,"title":"","content":"I definitely see how this feels foreign. Strip away the mechanical/industrial flavors of the game, and you will see that the tropes are still there: Servants of The Creator (God) uphold God's will. Sometimes, however, the servants cannot fulfill their roll or don't want to. They fall, they now shakes their fists at their creator. To hide from Him they use contracts to avoid detection, sometimes even taking a person's soul.<br /> <br /> Now add in the 'flavor' of the game. God and its servants are so foreign to human kind that they project their limited reality upon God and its servants. In ancient times, it was miracles and divinity. Slowly, though, as time went on and mankind developed so to did the God machine. The GM looked like silver and gold rods and alchemical appearances during the middle ages. Later, it looked steampunk-like. Now, it appears to be alien/tech/Matrix-like.<br /> <br /> All that is flavor, however, since the angels are still angels, demons are still demons, and God (a cold, uncaring, distant God like in the old testament- more like a Demiurge) is God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1895-chriszeke3","name":"ChrisZeke3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:10:39-08:00","id":71498,"title":"","content":"It's a game that views a lot of the themes and tropes of fallen angels through the lens of the God-Machine mythos. You have former servants of a vast, unknowable creator who at one time rebelled against the plans and designs of said creator and fell, severing their connection to God and its Heaven. Now the loyalist servants and their fallen kin are in constant conflict, with the forces of God intent on exterminating or reforming their wayward brethren and the forces of Hell striking against the designs of God and even planning on killing or overthrowing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:11:10-08:00","id":71500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons#post71474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, what does any of this have to do with the established mythology and tropes of angels or demons? Demon: the Fallen at least tried to invoke the general mythology with their own spin on things, but this feels no more like angels or demons than a wolf who wears sheep's clothing claiming to be a sheep.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did Demon: The Fallen already. If people want a traditional Judeo-Christian approach to angels and demons, that game exists. We wanted to do something different this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:21:49-08:00","id":71508,"title":"","content":"And we thank you for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:37:17-08:00","id":71519,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChrisZeke3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71492#post71492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely see how this feels foreign. Strip away the mechanical/industrial flavors of the game, and you will see that the tropes are still there: Servants of The Creator (God) uphold God's will. Sometimes, however, the servants cannot fulfill their roll or don't want to. They fall, they now shakes their fists at their creator. To hide from Him they use contracts to avoid detection, sometimes even taking a person's soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71498#post71498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have former servants of a vast, unknowable creator who at one time rebelled against the plans and designs of said creator and fell, severing their connection to God and its Heaven. Now the loyalist servants and their fallen kin are in constant conflict, with the forces of God intent on exterminating or reforming their wayward brethren and the forces of Hell striking against the designs of God and even planning on killing or overthrowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this in a humrous way, but I think you two just did an excellent job describing Changeling!</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChrisZeke3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71492#post71492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now add in the 'flavor' of the game. God and its servants are so foreign to human kind that they project their limited reality upon God and its servants. In ancient times, it was miracles and divinity. Slowly, though, as time went on and mankind developed so to did the God machine. The GM looked like silver and gold rods and alchemical appearances during the middle ages. Later, it looked steampunk-like. Now, it appears to be alien/tech/Matrix-like.<br /> <br /> All that is flavor, however, since the angels are still angels, demons are still demons, and God (a cold, uncaring, distant God like in the old testament- more like a Demiurge) is God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is really fascinating to me. Are you saying that the technology aspects of the Angels and the God Machine actually involve no technology, and we just mentally percieve/construct them as being &quot;More Advanced Than Us&quot; at any given time period of human development?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71500#post71500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did Demon: The Fallen already. If people want a traditional Judeo-Christian approach to angels and demons, that game exists. We wanted to do something different this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you were intentionally trying to invoke the idea of demons from other cultures? Is there a culture that displays their demons like this? Or is this a completely new mythology created specifically for the GMC?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:37:57-08:00","id":71520,"title":"","content":"on a assumption I&quot;m going to say you haven't yet had a chance to play demon. (Do it.)<br /> <br /> the problem that I think isn't covered very well in the book is that there are two vastly different perspectives. Demons are part of the machine, they are in the know. to them magic is science, powers are loop holes in reality and The God Machine is an uncaring robot.<br /> Humans don't see any of this; magic is magic no matter how many times the nice man inhabiting your husbands body explains it to you. Demons are lairs, perfect bloody liars always trying to manipulate you. Hell they literally want your soul or that's what the piece of paper they keep asking you to sign says.<br /> <br /> God is control Demons are chaos, cogs and broken pieces.<br /> <br /> There is an aesthetic triangle of all things Demon: Espionage, Tech, and Gnosticism<br /> <br /> Espionage: in this case, is how Demons and angels act; Think burn notice, person of interest, mission impossible.<br /> Tech: is appearance for infrastructure, angels and demonic forms; think Ghost in the Shell, Terminator, every thing out of the matrix in the matrix movies.<br /> Catholic Gnosticism: is the subtext and underlining theme often brought to the forefront to add high weirdness to the world. frankly I don't have any perfect examples off the top of my head but mainly it's just less obvious details. I recently watched some X-files and noticed it there in some of the more religious episodes, How Robocop is Jesus in the first film, Lost, Battle Star Galatica, V is a perfect example, Jericho has it's moments, The First Wave. It's all about religious undertones and questions like what is God and what is faith.<br /> <br /> I do hope that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:43:06-08:00","id":71532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71519#post71519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you were intentionally trying to invoke the idea of demons from other cultures? Is there a culture that displays their demons like this? Or is this a completely new mythology created specifically for the GMC?</div> </div> </div> </div> The God-Machine mythos originates from a short story in the original nWoD core rulebook called &quot;Voice of the Angel&quot; on pages 26-31. After a decade of little easter eggs here and God-Machine related optional things there, the folks at OPP decided to write out the God-Machine Chronicles as an unofficial 2nd edition of the game as well as a default mortal campaign setting that fleshes out the God-Machine for use in your games.<br /> <br /> Once it was fleshed out, they decided that they would approach the themes and tropes of angels and demons in Judeo-Christian mythology through the lens of the God-Machine mythology, leading to the game of Techgnostic Conspiracy that we have today.<br /> <br /> So it's not so much that it deals with demons of different cultures as it is that since Fallen was already a game of Fallen Angels straight out of Paradise Lost, they wanted to approach the idea and themes from a different angle entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:45:41-08:00","id":71533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71500#post71500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We did Demon: The Fallen already. If people want a traditional Judeo-Christian approach to angels and demons, that game exists. We wanted to do something different this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Inferno, for a more traditional look at Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T12:50:24-08:00","id":71536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71533#post71533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget Inferno, for a more traditional look at Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well as about 3-5 other takes in the nWoD alone, yeah. The title and/or behavior of &quot;demons&quot; really get a lot of mileage in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T14:27:46-08:00","id":71619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons#post71474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, I really like this splat. The world is literally the Matrix and &quot;Angels&quot; are the Agents who patrol and execute the processes of the Source. Sometimes those &quot;Angels&quot; go rogue and become &quot;Demons&quot; like Agent Smith, except that unlike Agent Smith you can barely defeat any other Agents and have to live your life paranoid that a bunch of Agents will hunt you down and recycle you. I love the thematic that they are hacking the source code of the universe, and every single one of them is a super spy who has to maintain his Cover (capital C) or risk his Cover being Compromised (capital C).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what does any of this have to do with the established mythology and tropes of angels or demons? Demon: the Fallen at least tried to invoke the general mythology with their own spin on things, but this feels no more like angels or demons than a wolf who wears sheep's clothing claiming to be a sheep.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, here's a few things.<br /> One, the idea of the Machine Angel is creeping into pop culture more and more.<br /> <br /> Its not uncommon for Angels to be said to lack free will, to be cold emotionless beings. <br /> <br /> Another thing with Angels is that they are said to be agents of Fate and Order. <br /> <br /> Mix them all together, and you have machine angels, lacking free will or true emotion, that uphold the Order of their Creator. I can't count how many times the books say that the God Machine defends the Status Quo. That's Order, right there, every thing in its place. <br /> <br /> Demons are rebels. They're hunted down, not only because they're rebelling and necessary resources, but because their very presence upsets the God Machine's order. They're Angels of Chaos. <br /> <br /> Its not uncommon for angels in fantasy or modern occult stories to be ruled by a Council of Angels or a single powerful Angel instead of an all powerful Creator God. <br /> <br /> Angel VS Demon is a game about Security versus Freedom. The God Machine is the ultimate in the way of security - the loss of a few freedoms and lives in exchange for the health of the many. That said, it also robs humans of any choice, trying to bring them into machine like efficiency. So, demons are the chaos, the free will. <br /> <br /> <br /> All in all, the game has a ton of angelic stuff if you just ignore the whole technology bend. Which is, truthfully, a lot easier than you'd think. Demon form can look like an angel, a horned devil, a shining light, a cloak of the sky. Exploits are very much Wrath of Heaven or Infernal Trickery stuff. Pacts. Weakness of being found by heaven's &quot;light&quot; and slain by divine powers. War on Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T22:40:30-08:00","id":71823,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's really quite easy to run this as a traditional Demon game. Just replace all instances of &quot;the God Machine&quot; with &quot;the Heavenly Host&quot; and remove the technology elements if you like and you get a nice conventional demon setting. &quot;Infrastructure&quot; then is how the Heavenly Host and its angels influence the world through visions, chosen ones, churches and cults, occult places etc., following a grand design of their own, not fully understood by either mortals or the fallen ones.<br /> <br /> I have done this in my chronicle as I really like many of the basic concepts of this game, e.g. the Cover concept.<br /> <br /> Characters could be either angels just fallen or can be demons summoned by some mortal fool from the depths of hell who then agreed to a soul pact, not knowing that he paved the way for the demon to remain in this world using his identity as cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 02-14-2014, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T23:20:05-08:00","id":71838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71500#post71500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We did Demon: The Fallen already. If people want a traditional Judeo-Christian approach to angels and demons, that game exists. We wanted to do something different this time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You did Vampire : the Masquerade already, but Vampire : the Requiem is thematically not all that different. I don't know.<br /> Demon : the Descent, at this point, kind of reminds me Werewolf : the Forsaken. WtF was not really about werewolves so much as shaman-spirit-cop, DtD is spy show rather than actually being about, you know, what people perceive about Demons.<br /> <br /> I do love DtD though. but I do think the game is kind of narrow, and could have been wider, covering a lot of different take on demons, but yeah we do have Inferno...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T23:23:01-08:00","id":71839,"title":"","content":"I have another question though... I know there is DtF translation guide coming soon, but is there going to be a DtD compliment book that will work as translation guides for Inferno, Lucifuge, maeljin, goetic demons and etc?<br /> <br /> <br /> I know, the idea is far-out, but I'd love a book like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T23:59:47-08:00","id":71846,"title":"","content":"There isn't really anything to &quot;translate&quot; there because they're not even thematic successors to one another. All the things you listed are just entirely different creatures.<br /> <br /> It's like asking for a translation guide between Demons and Immortals or Slashers and Mages.<br /> <br /> <i>Blood &amp; Smoke </i>has finally allowed Requiem to really stand on its own two feet and it shares themes with VtM mostly based around basic ideas of the vampiric condition.<br /> <br /> I think as far as the God Machine goes, you're getting lost in the <i>aesthetic </i>while thematically the Unchained very much are Demons. They're fallen angels hiding among humans, tempting them into bargains and deals, using horrifying powers to subvert people and draw them away from God(-Machine) and they turn into monsters with a lot of the traditional trappings and visuals of Angels but with a techy <i>aesthetic.</i><br /> <br /> Very little stops you from dropping or swapping that aesthetic entirely, though I think you'd be going through a lot of work for a vocabulary update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T01:24:32-08:00","id":71865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71846#post71846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really anything to &quot;translate&quot; there because they're not even thematic successors to one another. All the things you listed are just entirely different creatures.<br /> <br /> It's like asking for a translation guide between Demons and Immortals or Slashers and Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, right. Yeah. I don't know why I thought that was a good idea when I was writing that post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't know. Yeah, thematically I think DtD is awesome, and I do like its aesthetics, but I still think DtD is fluff-wise wayyyyy to constrained, like how Prometheans, Mummies, and even Werewolves are. I would have liked more varied possibilities, such as in Vampires and Changelings, or even Hunters, but that's just me I guess.<br /> <br /> I just wish that the game was maybe slightly less concentrated on God Machine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T05:40:31-08:00","id":71923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71838#post71838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You did Vampire : the Masquerade already, but Vampire : the Requiem is thematically not all that different. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div> VtM was a game of ancient monsters lurking over your shoulder and controlling the world. Requiem is about modern day vamps hashing it out on the streets. They're vampires, yeah. But wildly different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon : the Descent, at this point, kind of reminds me Werewolf : the Forsaken. WtF was not really about werewolves so much as shaman-spirit-cop, DtD is spy show rather than actually being about, you know, what people perceive about Demons. </div> </div> </div> While Werewolf does need more werewolf in it... lets start at the top here. What do you &quot;perceive&quot; about Demons? Embodiment of sin? Well, that's actually Requiem's and Inferno's stick. Rebel angels? Ancient cosmic beings? What? What is Demon here to you?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:12:45-08:00","id":71932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71923#post71923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> VtM was a game of ancient monsters lurking over your shoulder and controlling the world. Requiem is about modern day vamps hashing it out on the streets. They're vampires, yeah. But wildly different.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, in both games, they are more or less the similar bloodsucking monsters, although the theme and the mood are different. And with additional supplements VtR vampires are more and more resembling their VtM counterparts...<br /> <br /> About what I think about Demon... well I don't actually have a concrete idea <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the food for thought. I will think on it for days. However, DtD, to me, seems kind of like the second book for GMC...(I know, I know, GMC is mostly intended for mortals, but you know what I mean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:29:44-08:00","id":72032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71865#post71865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, right. Yeah. I don't know why I thought that was a good idea when I was writing that post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't know. Yeah, thematically I think DtD is awesome, and I do like its aesthetics, but I still think DtD is fluff-wise wayyyyy to constrained, like how Prometheans, Mummies, and even Werewolves are. I would have liked more varied possibilities, such as in Vampires and Changelings, or even Hunters, but that's just me I guess.<br /> <br /> I just wish that the game was maybe slightly less concentrated on God Machine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing is, anything even remotely focused on judeo-christian demons will usually involve God and their fall from grace, which also describes the presence and activities of the God-Machine in Demon. If you want that, I suspect the Demons you want skew towards the Fantasy type of Demon more than the biblical sort. :P<br /> <br /> That said, if you want less of a focus on the God-Machine, just dial back its presence in your setting. Maybe make compromise rolls less common. I don't think it's actually all that hard to marginalize the GM's impact, but be prepared for a shortage of foes to take on your Demon, seeing as how they're a pretty powerful bunch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T09:39:51-08:00","id":72034,"title":"","content":"Or just remove Infrastructure and Angels entirely, remove the machine, make it so that demons remember nothing from before their fall, have no knowledge of where they came from (or perhaps remember different things?) and as cover falls Things happen. Perhaps the world tries to &quot;remove&quot; their home (which really shouldn't be there, a fifth floor in a four floor building?) by having it catch on fire, it tries to explain why no one remembers them by making it so everyone that Should remember them drops dead, or even outright create creatures, or perhaps these creatures are drawn to the fallen, that attack them, trying to destroy them outright (perhaps for food, perhaps for other reasons).<br /> <br /> There are ways to maintain the mechanics yet still rewrite the entire theme of the game, in this one the need for cover is to protect against the aggression of a universe that views them as intruders, an infection, and perhaps they are...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T21:25:32-08:00","id":72459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72032#post72032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny thing is, anything even remotely focused on judeo-christian demons will usually involve God and their fall from grace, which also describes the presence and activities of the God-Machine in Demon. If you want that, I suspect the Demons you want skew towards the Fantasy type of Demon more than the biblical sort. :P<br /> <br /> That said, if you want less of a focus on the God-Machine, just dial back its presence in your setting. Maybe make compromise rolls less common. I don't think it's actually all that hard to marginalize the GM's impact, but be prepared for a shortage of foes to take on your Demon, seeing as how they're a pretty powerful bunch.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are right, DtD is the most &quot;traditional&quot; demon in that way, (maybe except for, maybe, Lucifuge) but I guess I wanted God Machine to be more amoral than evil. (And... I am just reminded that one of the textbooks outright mention that the GM is actually kind of amoral... but in almost all practices, the GM is treated as arch-enemy as well as mostly evil.) I digress way too much. sorry :P<br /> <br /> But yeah... Like you said, I could cut back GM presence at least on the low-levels game. What I liked about VtR is that it was very much vampires against other vampires. (Although... B&amp;S took it to a different level...) Changelings as well... Make no mistake, I think GM fluff is wonderful, but what I really feel is that its presence is too suffocating, and I would like it more to be too powerful to really even care about (at least, low-level) demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have no idea why, but participating in this conversation made me want to run an Innocent - Demon/GMC game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T22:25:41-08:00","id":72471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72459#post72459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And... I am just reminded that one of the textbooks outright mention that the GM is actually kind of amoral... but in almost all practices, the GM is treated as arch-enemy as well as mostly evil.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither cruel nor kind.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is fairly consistently painted as lacking in surplus resources to the degree that the losses a Fall presents - an <i>entire</i> angel, at the very least - are sufficiently problematic that, like Youtube's copyright-claiming software, it's too much of a liability to approach dealing with the Unchained via blacklist methodology - the number of demons it determines are worth more to it free than reclaimed are vastly outnumbered by the number it judges to be in need of repossession, as the Hunted Hunter's anecdote suggests, and free demons are by definition beyond the Machine's known ability to easily check, so we get the better-safe-than-sorry net thrown over the whole lot of potential misplaced embezzled funds that are the Unchained.<br /> <br /> Being what they are entirely because of the sustained decision to embrace their own free will and separation from their former master, the bulk of the Unchained are understandably resistant to being approached with the very real prospect of being forcibly recycled with nothing they valued about their lives coming with them. When The System keeps trying to make you part of it again despite your strident refusals in every direct confrontation over the subject and your self-determination is viewed as an inefficient use of resources by a System that in many ways is <i>all about</i> efficiency, the relationship between the two forces tends to be antagonistic.<br /> <br /> I'm fond of the ambiguity as to whether the Machine's designs include the Fall, as a motivational uncertainty. It's reminiscent of the question Werewolf occasionally poses about whether the Lunes speak for Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-15-2014, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T06:39:11-08:00","id":72584,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=torete;n72459]<br /> You are right, DtD is the most &quot;traditional&quot; demon in that way, (maybe except for, maybe, Lucifuge) but I guess I wanted God Machine to be more amoral than evil.[quote] It is. Its the ultimate version of Order. It just doesn't recognize humans or angels as anything other than resources. It doesn't realize that freedom and life are precious - it is, after all, an alien machine.<br /> <br /> And, no, its not all practice. The God Machine made Y2K angel. It -saved humanity from itself-. Look it up in Seattle. Is that the practice of an evil arch enemy? No.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T07:57:04-08:00","id":72628,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=MCN;n72584][QUOTE=torete;n72459]<br /> You are right, DtD is the most &quot;traditional&quot; demon in that way, (maybe except for, maybe, Lucifuge) but I guess I wanted God Machine to be more amoral than evil.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is. Its the ultimate version of Order. It just doesn't recognize humans or angels as anything other than resources. It doesn't realize that freedom and life are precious - it is, after all, an alien machine.<br /> <br /> And, no, its not all practice. The God Machine made Y2K angel. It -saved humanity from itself-. Look it up in Seattle. Is that the practice of an evil arch enemy? No. </div> </div> </div><br /> Points very well taken.<br /> <br /> Well, I re-read DtD almost cover to cover, and decided the book was better for me than more than I thought I did. I just... probably thought it somewhat unpalatable because 1). I thought wayyyyy too much about inter-splat balance, which is sort of counterproductive and not encouraged by anyone, and 2). I really don't like power-finesse-resistance-numina system, and the main antagonists were angels using just that... (It's actually one of my bigger qualms about WTF as well... and with BnS, there are the strix flying around being the big bad....sigh...)<br /> <br /> Then again I love Dizang more than anything. I digress.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Just one minor thing though...<br /> <br /> The names of embeds and exploits, while very tactful, interesting, sometimes funny, and even insightful, really doesn't help the flavor, as they (in my humble humble opinion) really sound neither like the practices of fallen angels, nor abilities of renegade A. I, nor tricks of spies in action. (I know, there's things like Hellfire, but the most of them follow the naming patterns such as Last Place You Look, or Marco Polo.) This is actually my biggest aesthetic problem about DtD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","user":"torete","date":". 02-15-2014, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T08:51:13-08:00","id":72644,"title":"","content":"I actually prefer it this way. It's kind of annoying to get into a fictional setting or a rule set for a game, get to a certain point in the fiction or rule book, and find that what you're reading has declared that some real-world religious viewpoint is effectively the Truth.<br /> <br /> It might not feel like a big deal to people who are fully invested or indoctrinated in the religion in question, but it's very jarring for the rest of us and makes it hard for us to continue being immersed in that thing. It doesn't matter if you're reading the Justice League, and at first it's Batman, Superman, and Green Lantern, and then suddenly there's angels talking about the Abrahamic god and heaven and hell or if it's in the Old World of Darkness, where the origin of the Vampire isn't up for debate or left up to the storyteller, but actually straight up Cain from the Old Testament. Not &quot;some people think it's Cain&quot; or &quot;this group believes it was Cain&quot; but &quot;yeah, it was Cain and everyone knows it, it's a universal truth.&quot; It kind of leaves a bad taste in my mouth.<br /> <br /> I think there's just enough of the concept of serving an all-powerful, nigh-omniscient being with powerful messengers and agents in DtD without forcing everyone to watch the game turn into, &quot;And Christianity wins again! Sit back and enjoy, because for the next four hours of gameplay you'll be reminded of our cultural superiority.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2205,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","user":"Abaddon","date":". 02-15-2014, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2205-abaddon","name":"Abaddon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:18:29-08:00","id":72682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72628#post72628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I re-read DtD almost cover to cover, and decided the book was better for me than more than I thought I did. I just... probably thought it somewhat unpalatable because 1). I thought wayyyyy too much about inter-splat balance, which is sort of counterproductive and not encouraged by anyone, and 2). I really don't like power-finesse-resistance-numina system, and the main antagonists were angels using just that... (It's actually one of my bigger qualms about WTF as well... and with BnS, there are the strix flying around being the big bad....sigh...)<br /> <br /> Then again I love Dizang more than anything. I digress.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, demons come off as pretty potent. It doesn't help that a demon's weakness is &quot;exposure.&quot; Not exactly as flashy as silver or flame. <br /> <br /> As for the PFR makeup of ephemeral beings... I don't really get why we need it. I think it started off as a short hand for antagonists, and kinda grew into something else. But, I learn to deal with it, since they're all under ST control anyways. I tend to only roll spirit stats when it comes to combat situations, and in that case, I can pretty much pretend all others don't exist. I actually don't mind using the PFR shorthand for mortal NPCs too. It works well for pounding things out fast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just one minor thing though...<br /> <br /> The names of embeds and exploits, while very tactful, interesting, sometimes funny, and even insightful, really doesn't help the flavor, as they (in my humble humble opinion) really sound neither like the practices of fallen angels, nor abilities of renegade A. I, nor tricks of spies in action. (I know, there's things like Hellfire, but the most of them follow the naming patterns such as Last Place You Look, or Marco Polo.) This is actually my biggest aesthetic problem about DtD. </div> </div> </div> Yeah. I have a major issue with some of that stuff too. The Hellfire power requires a gun. On the other hand, <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Incendiary doesn't. There's a lot of questionable stuff here. Though, to be honest, the embeds are pretty much ALL spy stuff. Most of it is stuff I can see happening on Burn Notice. Exploits seem to be a mix of iconic demonic, angelic, or A.I.-ic style powers to me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I found it helped to make a character. Most stuff really clicked for me after that. Even before, two read throughs and I was going to toss the game.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:21:07-08:00","id":72683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abaddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72644#post72644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's just enough of the concept of serving an all-powerful, nigh-omniscient being with powerful messengers and agents in DtD without forcing everyone to watch the game turn into, &quot;And Christianity wins again! Sit back and enjoy, because for the next four hours of gameplay you'll be reminded of our cultural superiority.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Ironic coming from someone with a biblical screen name.<br /> <br /> That said, the WoD goes out of its way to assume that no religion is right (or wrong for that matter), with the potential exception of Gnosticism. Even in Mage, which is basically Christian mysticism down to a T, we moved away from God. Even the Abrahamic God doesn't make an actual appearance, instead of just the Christian God.<br /> <br /> So, it would be very strange to suddenly have that being appear in Demon. The GM is both close enough to the idea of a powerful God to make sense for a game, but far enough that you can't really say that its the Creator of All Things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-15-2014, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T22:49:21-08:00","id":73027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72682#post72682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, demons come off as pretty potent. It doesn't help that a demon's weakness is &quot;exposure.&quot; Not exactly as flashy as silver or flame.<br /> <br /> As for the PFR makeup of ephemeral beings... I don't really get why we need it. I think it started off as a short hand for antagonists, and kinda grew into something else. But, I learn to deal with it, since they're all under ST control anyways. I tend to only roll spirit stats when it comes to combat situations, and in that case, I can pretty much pretend all others don't exist. I actually don't mind using the PFR shorthand for mortal NPCs too. It works well for pounding things out fast.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah. I have a major issue with some of that stuff too. The Hellfire power requires a gun. On the other hand, <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Incendiary doesn't. There's a lot of questionable stuff here. Though, to be honest, the embeds are pretty much ALL spy stuff. Most of it is stuff I can see happening on Burn Notice. Exploits seem to be a mix of iconic demonic, angelic, or A.I.-ic style powers to me.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I found it helped to make a character. Most stuff really clicked for me after that. Even before, two read throughs and I was going to toss the game.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, I guess with PFR spirit/angels I could do what you do. I initially considered giving each angel / spirit a full-fledged character sheet like the PCs get, but yeah... Maybe I will do that for some major NPCs, and I could really use PFR for mortal NPCs. The thing with PFR is that... it really doesn't look like a very well thought-out, or even, balanced(gasp!) system. Same with numina. Numbers do get bloated out, like, really fast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And about embeds and exploits... yes, coming to think about it, embeds represent spy angle, while exploits have many different flavor. Thank you for helping me see it better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T22:56:19-08:00","id":73031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abaddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=72644#post72644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually prefer it this way. It's kind of annoying to get into a fictional setting or a rule set for a game, get to a certain point in the fiction or rule book, and find that what you're reading has declared that some real-world religious viewpoint is effectively the Truth.<br /> <br /> It might not feel like a big deal to people who are fully invested or indoctrinated in the religion in question, but it's very jarring for the rest of us and makes it hard for us to continue being immersed in that thing. It doesn't matter if you're reading the Justice League, and at first it's Batman, Superman, and Green Lantern, and then suddenly there's angels talking about the Abrahamic god and heaven and hell or if it's in the Old World of Darkness, where the origin of the Vampire isn't up for debate or left up to the storyteller, but actually straight up Cain from the Old Testament. Not &quot;some people think it's Cain&quot; or &quot;this group believes it was Cain&quot; but &quot;yeah, it was Cain and everyone knows it, it's a universal truth.&quot; It kind of leaves a bad taste in my mouth.<br /> <br /> I think there's just enough of the concept of serving an all-powerful, nigh-omniscient being with powerful messengers and agents in DtD without forcing everyone to watch the game turn into, &quot;And Christianity wins again! Sit back and enjoy, because for the next four hours of gameplay you'll be reminded of our cultural superiority.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Reminds me how I absolutely hated oWoD endgame books... especially Gehenna. Could not stand those games, even though some of the themes were nifty.<br /> <br /> This is one of the prime reasons I prefer nWod, but I am especially glad that they decided to run with the God Machine. It does provide some of the cosmic horror themes, (nWod games were mostly local, except maybe for Mage, who always seems to be their favorite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) without giving one concrete, definite answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking about Mage though, I thought MtAw was at least as Buddhist as it is Gnostic, or even more. But yeah... Mage was never my favorite game so what do I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T07:29:55-08:00","id":73177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73031#post73031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me how I absolutely hated oWoD endgame books... especially Gehenna. Could not stand those games, even though some of the themes were nifty.<br /> <br /> This is one of the prime reasons I prefer nWod, but I am especially glad that they decided to run with the God Machine. It does provide some of the cosmic horror themes, (nWod games were mostly local, except maybe for Mage, who always seems to be their favorite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) without giving one concrete, definite answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking about Mage though, I thought MtAw was at least as Buddhist as it is Gnostic, or even more. But yeah... Mage was never my favorite game so what do I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> There are elements of Buddhism in Mage. Mage is based on the whole Golden Order of the Dawn style mystery western occult practices, which borrow heavily from Christian Gnostic texts, as well as bits of Egyptian geomancy and works of Thrice Great Hermes, Arabic numerology, and, yes, some Buddhism. That said, I personally find that Christian Mysticism aspects are really stronger than the buddhist.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Watchtowers is a concept that's core to Christian mysticism - they're the abodes of the Archangels (instead of Mage's &quot;Oracles&quot;), one associated with each element (mage's &quot;Paths.&quot;) Atlantis follows the story of the Tower of Babel - ancient advanced civilization that built a tower to reach the Supernal (this term literally means &quot;Heaven&quot;). For their hubris, the Tower was crushed, and the universal tongue of mankind (&quot;High Speech&quot;) was sundered, a curse lain over humanity to scatter them so that they'd never again reach that high (&quot;Sleeping Curse.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's more, and I could go on, but I think you get my point at the sheer amount of it all. Personally, I find that the weight of it all makes it difficult to look at Mage through the lenses of other cultures. Its difficult to really make a more neo-pagan style witch in mage society, I feel. Or Vodun. Or jumping over to Asia for Taoism, Buddhism, Hindu, or Shintoism.<br /> <br /> So, I mean, its still there in the books. Werewolf, Mummy, and Changeling are the only two that I really think don't lean that way. Which is kind of inevitable, when you really think about it. The WoD books are -heavily- invested in Western pop culture. Christianity, for good or ill, is a major part of that culture, even if people don't realize just how much and how pervasive it is. Adapting to the point of making the books religion-neutral takes a lot of work, and is commendable for how far they did come. <br /> <br /> I would love to see them push the envelop further as well with the Chronicle books as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-16-2014, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T09:36:27-08:00","id":73236,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://techgnosis.com/techgnosis/tgexcerpts.html\" target=\"_blank\">I'm just going to drop these excerpts from Erik Davis's Techgnosis here. </a>Reading them makes sense of a lot of the demon/daemon aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Remember, in this case, there is not a divide between the technology and the gnosticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T10:09:45-08:00","id":73246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73177#post73177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> -snip-<br /> So, I mean, its still there in the books. Werewolf, Mummy, and Changeling are the only two that I really think don't lean that way.<br /> -snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf, Mummy and Changeling though, make three <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah. WoD is very very heavily laden with various forms of Christianity and its cultural manifestations. But I am positively glad that nWod is dealing with it much better and much more subtle than cWod's approach of it. *shudder*<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T10:30:36-08:00","id":73256,"title":"","content":"I have never understood this forums reflexive distaste for anything that seems vaguely Christian. And remember,this is coming from a non Christian person. Just as something published in China is influenced by Chinese mythology, and something published in India would be influenced by Indian mythology, in Europe or the Americas it's not unfair to be based on Christian mythology. I mean, it's no more valid or non valid than Buddhism or Hinduism or anything else. It's a way for people to understand the world and make sense of life. And as the audience for White Wolf and Onyx Path products is seemingly overwhelmingly American and European, it's fair to play to things that we would all know from being part of Western culture. Onyx Path has a responsibility to make fun products for us to They don't have a responsibility to use one mythology over another. The only thing I ask is that when they talk about any religion, be accurate and respectful. If they want to base it all on Christianity orJainism, or Banana Slug God worship who cares?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T11:59:40-08:00","id":73287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71838#post71838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You did Vampire : the Masquerade already, but Vampire : the Requiem is thematically not all that different. I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno - they're not too dissimilar in play, and Requiem cribbed a lot of Masquerade, but Masquerade is mining conspiracy theories and apocalyptic millennial for its metaplot, where vampires are generally the pawns of the next generation up until you get to handful of truly ancient terrifying horrors.... While Requiem retains the layer-cake structure the overarching conspiracies and End of Days are gone, and in there place we're left with a thousand mysteries and uncertainties. Beneath the 'you're a vampire' veneer, conspiracy versus mystery is a surprisingly big difference, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:31:37-08:00","id":73300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73256#post73256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never understood this forums reflexive distaste for anything that seems vaguely Christian. And remember,this is coming from a non Christian person. Just as something published in China is influenced by Chinese mythology, and something published in India would be influenced by Indian mythology, in Europe or the Americas it's not unfair to be based on Christian mythology. I mean, it's no more valid or non valid than Buddhism or Hinduism or anything else. It's a way for people to understand the world and make sense of life. And as the audience for White Wolf and Onyx Path products is seemingly overwhelmingly American and European, it's fair to play to things that we would all know from being part of Western culture. Onyx Path has a responsibility to make fun products for us to They don't have a responsibility to use one mythology over another. The only thing I ask is that when they talk about any religion, be accurate and respectful. If they want to base it all on Christianity orJainism, or Banana Slug God worship who cares?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that Christian mythology is very well situated in the West and people don't like the idea of it being rendered as essential and correct. Why this is a worry over another religion being rendered essential and correct is that in the cWoD, it <i>was </i>essential and correct. Some people found it a bit disagreeable so they would rather it not be repeated again.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it was a big detrimental thing to cWoD or anything ,just that I understand how people might not want the nWoD to do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T18:06:22-08:00","id":73481,"title":"","content":"I just adored the Christian themes in H:tV. I could see my church as a front for some preternatural hunters club (Maybe even charging for a hunting license as well). But I am so absolutely enthralled by D:tD's different take on the Demon genre. The Unchained, have almost nothing to do with what I've been taught about Demon's. Unless you want to draw parallels to the Unchained turning against God in one way or another. And really it ends there. Of course both God and the G-M want their angels back, the former makes it there choice and they'd have to repent. I digress though. What sells the Descent to me, is that it's like nothing I've ever considered in the realms of possibility for Demons. Inferno did a great job of the classical Demon. But this techgnostic feel took real creativity and imagination on the part of the writers and developers. And that imaginiation keeps up with the General themes of the World of Darkness. How many people expected werewolves to have more in common with native american Animism and spirituality then psychotic killers. I'm just not gonna count the Black Spiral Dancers there...<br /> <br /> These weren't the Demon's I was looking for, but my God has this book filled me with a vigor I haven't felt since Geist. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T20:48:08-08:00","id":73530,"title":"","content":"I just want to say that I'm a Gnostic Christian, so a lot of the things in this book are cool. I just don't like the technology &amp; infrastructure aspect. If it was just magic &amp; prophecy I'd like it ten times more. I'm not tech savvy &amp; I'm not big on espionage. I was hoping DtD would be like Supernatural with Castiel, Anna &amp; Ruth, &amp; even a bit of Crowley as the main characters scheming &amp; fighting against Angels that worshiped a cold uncaring dogma of duty. Instead it's like the Matrix meets Constantine (they are both Keanu movies so I guess he can play the same guy)<br /> <br /> In short, I can see the reasons they did it but I feel reluctant to agree that it was the correct decision. Honestly, who plays a game called DEMON &amp; not expect strong Christian overtones?<br /> If you don't like Christianity maybe they can make the fluff a bit different &amp; call it Titan: the Unchained or FirBolg: the Outcast. (I totally need to trademark these names now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2266,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","user":"Aermas","date":".  Infernal Keyboard 02-16-2014, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T21:42:23-08:00","id":73544,"title":"","content":"Someone's whose ideas of demons begins with rakshasas?<br /> <br /> The word demon has a wide variety of direct or near-direct use-Hell, a casual search points at not just the Abrahamic cultures of Judaism, Christianity, or Islam, but very different Middle Eastern cultures as well as a conception of the asuras of Hinduism-and much of that becomes more complex when you consider that the word demon has been used to describe more muddled concepts to Westerners, such as various youkai from Japanese mythos to the various bits of Amazonian folklore-and from a certain loose conception, they aren't wrong from a certain conceptual standpoint without evoking Christianity, and in fact would be wrong to evoke such.<br /> <br /> But you can't win them all-the God-Machine pvorides a middle ground between the popular consensus and the wide world of demonic icons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T04:49:08-08:00","id":73657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73287#post73287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno - they're not too dissimilar in play, and Requiem cribbed a lot of Masquerade, but Masquerade is mining conspiracy theories and apocalyptic millennial for its metaplot, where vampires are generally the pawns of the next generation up until you get to handful of truly ancient terrifying horrors.... While Requiem retains the layer-cake structure the overarching conspiracies and End of Days are gone, and in there place we're left with a thousand mysteries and uncertainties. Beneath the 'you're a vampire' veneer, conspiracy versus mystery is a surprisingly big difference, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Come ON though. I know VtR and VtM have thematic differences, but aesthetic aspects are not all that different.<br /> <br /> Compare the aesthetics, say, between WtF and WtA, and DtD and DtF. I know what you are talking about, but Vampire, at least on the aesthetic grounds, have changed the least. And VtR supplements are including more and more VtM-like stuff anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T04:55:24-08:00","id":73660,"title":"","content":"It's probably not going to contribute to anything said above, but I am in love with Long Night in HtV. I love that it's Christian (and to a long stretch, an Abrahamic religion) yet not related to Catholocism, Gnosticism, Tech-gnosticism, or any other kind of bigger conspiracy/truth. I am no Christian myself, but I love Long Night is a bunch of church-goers standing up against monsters, not even really knowing what they are fighting against.<br /> <br /> It's one of the flavors that nWod needs more. And what makes me prefer nWod over cWod.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T05:09:11-08:00","id":73662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73256#post73256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never understood this forums reflexive distaste for anything that seems vaguely Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div> For the record? I don't care one whit that its Christian. I care that its any one single religion that dominates. I have one heck of a time fitting a someone that uses neo-pagan witchcraft or a Voodoo mambo into Mage and have their beliefs not feel jarring. I had the same issue when I attempted to play a non-Wiccan using the Witchcraft system.<br /> <br /> <br /> Side note, Rankshasa I think fit with Vampires better than with a game called Demon; insatiable cannibals and all that. IMHO, nWoD Unchained and cWoD Fallen make crappy demons - they're minor gods waging war over who gets to rule the Earth. They're only demons in that's what people also call fallen gods. Most people tend to think of some kind of incarnation of sin or impurities or the like. Vampires fit that bill. Inferno stuff fits that bill. Meanwhile, Unchained are more like Asuras to the God Machine's Suras.<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">It is significant that it was not for their sins that the anti-gods had to be destroyed but because of their power, their virtue, their knowledge, which threatened that of the gods.&quot; -- Alain Dani\u00e9lou</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Anti-gods makes a much, much better description of the Unchained than demon. The word &quot;demon&quot; really does imply so much to the modern person that doesn't fit at all within the game of Demon. You're not a creature of sin. Not unless you consider free will is a sin. Demon is a game of Order VS Chaos, of Security VS Freedom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Angels in the western culture. Suras in Hindu. Meanwhile, closer to China, I would paint the Unchained and Angels as related to Confucius. While the teachings of Confucius don't specifically say to worship angel-like beings and their creator, it DOES provide a hierarchy of social order, and respect and obedience to parents, spiritual leaders... and godly beings themselves. Something the God Machine would support whole heartedly. If not twist and use for its own ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-17-2014, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T06:50:41-08:00","id":73695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons#post71474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what does any of this have to do with the established mythology and tropes of angels or demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a link between christian/gnostic mythology and modern science may in fact have a precursor in the works of Hans Jonas, a german philosopher and student of Heidegger now better known for his contributions to bioethics (&quot;the principle of responsibility&quot;). From his studies of late classical religious texts, he developed an understanding of the phenomenon of gnosticism as a form of &quot;ancient nihilism&quot; parallell to the modern subjugation of nature through the use of technology: whereas early christian sub-sects like manichaeans or simonists believed the world to be a prison for the soul wrought by an uncaring god, thus evil and to be overcome, existentialism and materialism share their contempt based on their own ideological dualism (&quot;anthropological acosmism&quot;) between consciousness and (dead) matter. The jump is not too far at all if one considers this cosmological alienation to be common ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2304-nehekh","name":"Nehekh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2304_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T10:54:52-08:00","id":73793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73657#post73657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Come ON though. I know VtR and VtM have thematic differences, but aesthetic aspects are not all that different.<br /> <br /> Compare the aesthetics, say, between WtF and WtA, and DtD and DtF. I know what you are talking about, but Vampire, at least on the aesthetic grounds, have changed the least. And VtR supplements are including more and more VtM-like stuff anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: Thematics inform aesthetics more than aesthetics inform thematics, or to put it another way, saying that Requiem and Masquerade look the most alike is the least useful element of a comparison and misses the point of how different they look from one another because of thematics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T19:34:27-08:00","id":74042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=73793#post73793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: Thematics inform aesthetics more than aesthetics inform thematics, or to put it another way, saying that Requiem and Masquerade look the most alike is the least useful element of a comparison and misses the point of how different they look from one another because of thematics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well then we can agree to disagree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> as I do think aesthetics is almost as important. But yeah, I see where you are coming from and it's very valid argument. What I wouldn't do, is though, to see aesthetic elements as 'least useful element.' But thank you for your input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T20:55:48-08:00","id":74078,"title":"","content":"I've seen too many nice, bright, and shiny aesthetics hiding a hollow core to give aesthetics it's day. It is important, much as any of the other steps of art are, but it is the last thing to consider.<br /> <br /> But then again I ascribe to Scott McCloud's theory on that, so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T12:34:08-08:00","id":74463,"title":"","content":"It really doesn't have anything to do with demons besides the thematic connection of demons as rebels to a system with a higher purpose. Honestly I find the whole thing really cliche, and see the only way to salvage it for gameplay is to strip the half-hearted cyberpunk/matrix elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","user":"Knit-I-Fine","date":".  Typo 02-18-2014, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:51:12-08:00","id":74536,"title":"","content":"I'm glad it didn't end up like the old demon. Old demon almost invalidated the owod cosmology. It also basically combined all the themes of the other games, rather than had its own. They'd know the secrets like mages, be fantastic strange monsters like changelings, be embodied vice like vampires, be ancient immortals like mummies. Rather than throwing christian mythos in (which was a fiasco in the cwod cosmology) and stepping on toes, they went wholly into the god machine as a real machine aspect. It's less cliche for a scifi game than a mad scientist game (no offense meant to you Genius fans), and is unexpected as a way of implementing it. While I enjoyed cDemon, and wouldn't have minded a PC version of Inferno.. but i'm glad to have something new, and really unprecedented in the cwod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:29:46-08:00","id":74559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74536#post74536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad it didn't end up like the old demon. Old demon almost invalidated the owod cosmology. It also basically combined all the themes of the other games, rather than had its own. They'd know the secrets like mages, be fantastic strange monsters like changelings, be embodied vice like vampires, be ancient immortals like mummies. Rather than throwing christian mythos in (which was a fiasco in the cwod cosmology) and stepping on toes, they went wholly into the god machine as a real machine aspect. It's less cliche for a scifi game than a mad scientist game (no offense meant to you Genius fans), and is unexpected as a way of implementing it. While I enjoyed cDemon, and wouldn't have minded a PC version of Inferno.. but i'm glad to have something new, and really unprecedented in the cwod.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure a judeo-christian view of demons would be the best game ever either, but the fact of the matter is that the god machine chronicle/DtD is entirely uninspired and taking away the judeo-christian aspect of it just makes it have no edge. It's entirely lost is ability to make a mark on things because it refuses to own up to the origins it's trying to make a play of. I mean, the idea of angels as cold feeling creature that are morally ambiguous owes to criticism of abrahamic mythology, but instead of actually drawing anything meaningful from the concept of angels, they just went with the idea of corporate drones as spiritual entities IE Agents from the Matrix.<br /> <br /> Demon seems to want to have it's cake, but deny that it is cake. That's the problem with the entire god machine concept as a whole to be honest. It's attempting to merge &quot;evil industrial company&quot; and &quot;eldritch abomination&quot; but degrading both sources. I just don't feel like there's anything to take seriously about an antagonist that is a series of incompetent industrial plants that that happen to be invisible. The thing with eldritch abominations is that they're compelling when they're beginning to make their move, because their move is (near) unstoppable. The god machine on the other hand just comes off as an incompetent boss to angels that can't even reliable track down it's rogue agents. It's a supernatural being with power of a sloppily managed PMC. That's not scary.<br /> <br /> And I'm really trying to wrap my head about how this is supposed to work with the cosmology of say, Mage, which is theoretically supposed to have the united cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T14:50:01-08:00","id":74574,"title":"","content":"<i>Requiem</i> is more like <i>Masquerade</i> than <i>Descent</i> is like <i>Fallen</i>, yeah. It's more the difference between the two <i>Changelings</i>. How much the games echo their predecessors varies from line to line.<br /> <br /> With <i>Fallen</i> still readily available and doing what it does with its setting so well, I wanted to take a different approach. I wanted to keep the core internal idea of being someone who once had a great deal of certainty and purpose, but who has come to question it and faces a great loss as a result. I also wanted to keep the core external idea, of beings which were glorious servants of a higher power, but who by their own deeds fell from grace, now having to pursue their aims by subversion.<br /> <br /> The story of that subversion is different. <i>Descent</i> is about having to lie about who you are. Not just hiding your supernatural nature and dark urges, as in <i>Requiem</i>, but having to take on a false identity because you don't have one of your own. It's a theme you see in Kurt Vonnegut's <i>Mother Night</i>: am I who I believe myself to be internally, or am I who the people around me think I am? What does that mean when different people see me different ways? I think this is something most people ask at some point in their life; being queer, it's something I've had to wrestle with a lot.<br /> <br /> This is where espionage become the other half of the metaphor. <i>Mother Night</i> isn't about &quot;spies&quot; in the Bond sense, but it's about people tainted by espionage. John Le Carre's novels deal with layers of false identity. Le Carre pulls off the nice trick where sometimes being a spy is a metaphor for things we can all identify with, whereas sometimes the things we identify with are a metaphor to look at spies. And spies have something fundamentally in common with angels: they serve a higher power, but don't necessarily understand it. The loyal don't see understanding as necessary; the treasonous see it as vital.<br /> <br /> The external trappings are also different. We wanted a look and feel for the new <i>Demon</i> line that suggested the faithful and fallen of Christian folklore, but which was also fundamentally unique to the World of Darkness. Thus, the illustrations include mixtures of Boschian fiends and biomechanical horrors. Sam Araya's pieces mix these in a particularly cool way.<br /> <br /> The fundamentals are still ones everyone knows: there are creatures who once served God, but don't anymore. They bargain for the things dearest to us with tricky deals. Sometimes, they hide in the guises of our friends. Other times, they are beings of fire and wrath. They give us what we want, but perhaps at the cost of what we need. Everyone knows these things, everyone's been warned, but the devil is in the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:43:35-08:00","id":74605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74559#post74559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm really trying to wrap my head about how this is supposed to work with the cosmology of say, Mage, which is theoretically supposed to have the united cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummmm... no. It doesn't.<br /> <br /> Mages SAY they do. They're deluded. They may have a larger picture than most, but even their own books admit theyu're clueless about so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there is no united cosmology. This is deliberate. Every game has its own contradictions. Its not meant to be a pretty picture. Its meant to be a huge strange mess with no clear answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-18-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T16:04:11-08:00","id":74612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74605#post74605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ummmm... no. It doesn't.<br /> <br /> Mages SAY they do. They're deluded. They may have a larger picture than most, but even their own books admit theyu're clueless about so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, there is no united cosmology. This is deliberate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how Mage and Werewolf seem to have made attempts to fit together, I'm rather sure this isn't deliberate. You can't just look at plot holes and say &quot;Yeah, it's supposed to be that way.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T16:04:43-08:00","id":74613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74605#post74605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ummmm... no. It doesn't.<br /> <br /> Mages SAY they do. They're deluded.</div> </div> </div> </div>An irksome subset of Mage <i>fans</i> say this. As Dave Brookshaw has pointed out, this is decidedly at odds with the point of things like Arcane Experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74612#post74612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Mage and Werewolf seem to have made attempts to fit together, I'm rather sure this isn't deliberate. You can't just look at plot holes and say &quot;Yeah, it's supposed to be that way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Made attempts to fit together&quot; here meaning\u2026?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-18-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T21:36:56-08:00","id":74777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74574#post74574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Requiem</i> is more like <i>Masquerade</i> than <i>Descent</i> is like <i>Fallen</i>, yeah. It's more the difference between the two <i>Changelings</i>. How much the games echo their predecessors varies from line to line.<br /> <br /> With <i>Fallen</i> still readily available and doing what it does with its setting so well, I wanted to take a different approach. I wanted to keep the core internal idea of being someone who once had a great deal of certainty and purpose, but who has come to question it and faces a great loss as a result. I also wanted to keep the core external idea, of beings which were glorious servants of a higher power, but who by their own deeds fell from grace, now having to pursue their aims by subversion.<br /> <br /> The story of that subversion is different. <i>Descent</i> is about having to lie about who you are. Not just hiding your supernatural nature and dark urges, as in <i>Requiem</i>, but having to take on a false identity because you don't have one of your own. It's a theme you see in Kurt Vonnegut's <i>Mother Night</i>: am I who I believe myself to be internally, or am I who the people around me think I am? What does that mean when different people see me different ways? I think this is something most people ask at some point in their life; being queer, it's something I've had to wrestle with a lot.<br /> <br /> This is where espionage become the other half of the metaphor. <i>Mother Night</i> isn't about &quot;spies&quot; in the Bond sense, but it's about people tainted by espionage. John Le Carre's novels deal with layers of false identity. Le Carre pulls off the nice trick where sometimes being a spy is a metaphor for things we can all identify with, whereas sometimes the things we identify with are a metaphor to look at spies. And spies have something fundamentally in common with angels: they serve a higher power, but don't necessarily understand it. The loyal don't see understanding as necessary; the treasonous see it as vital.<br /> <br /> The external trappings are also different. We wanted a look and feel for the new <i>Demon</i> line that suggested the faithful and fallen of Christian folklore, but which was also fundamentally unique to the World of Darkness. Thus, the illustrations include mixtures of Boschian fiends and biomechanical horrors. Sam Araya's pieces mix these in a particularly cool way.<br /> <br /> The fundamentals are still ones everyone knows: there are creatures who once served God, but don't anymore. They bargain for the things dearest to us with tricky deals. Sometimes, they hide in the guises of our friends. Other times, they are beings of fire and wrath. They give us what we want, but perhaps at the cost of what we need. Everyone knows these things, everyone's been warned, but the devil is in the details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thank you very much for this input. Despite some of the things I have said, DtD is still my very favorite game and I love the ideas, and came to love it even more through the discussion here. I especially love the emphasis on lying.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, thank you for the game. And thank you in advance for supplements. I am dying of the anticipation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T21:40:05-08:00","id":74779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74574#post74574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Requiem</i> is more like <i>Masquerade</i> than <i>Descent</i> is like <i>Fallen</i>, yeah. It's more the difference between the two <i>Changelings</i>. How much the games echo their predecessors varies from line to line.<br /> <br /> With <i>Fallen</i> still readily available and doing what it does with its setting so well, I wanted to take a different approach. I wanted to keep the core internal idea of being someone who once had a great deal of certainty and purpose, but who has come to question it and faces a great loss as a result. I also wanted to keep the core external idea, of beings which were glorious servants of a higher power, but who by their own deeds fell from grace, now having to pursue their aims by subversion.<br /> <br /> The story of that subversion is different. <i>Descent</i> is about having to lie about who you are. Not just hiding your supernatural nature and dark urges, as in <i>Requiem</i>, but having to take on a false identity because you don't have one of your own. It's a theme you see in Kurt Vonnegut's <i>Mother Night</i>: am I who I believe myself to be internally, or am I who the people around me think I am? What does that mean when different people see me different ways? I think this is something most people ask at some point in their life; being queer, it's something I've had to wrestle with a lot.<br /> <br /> This is where espionage become the other half of the metaphor. <i>Mother Night</i> isn't about &quot;spies&quot; in the Bond sense, but it's about people tainted by espionage. John Le Carre's novels deal with layers of false identity. Le Carre pulls off the nice trick where sometimes being a spy is a metaphor for things we can all identify with, whereas sometimes the things we identify with are a metaphor to look at spies. And spies have something fundamentally in common with angels: they serve a higher power, but don't necessarily understand it. The loyal don't see understanding as necessary; the treasonous see it as vital.<br /> <br /> The external trappings are also different. We wanted a look and feel for the new <i>Demon</i> line that suggested the faithful and fallen of Christian folklore, but which was also fundamentally unique to the World of Darkness. Thus, the illustrations include mixtures of Boschian fiends and biomechanical horrors. Sam Araya's pieces mix these in a particularly cool way.<br /> <br /> The fundamentals are still ones everyone knows: there are creatures who once served God, but don't anymore. They bargain for the things dearest to us with tricky deals. Sometimes, they hide in the guises of our friends. Other times, they are beings of fire and wrath. They give us what we want, but perhaps at the cost of what we need. Everyone knows these things, everyone's been warned, but the devil is in the details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's so incompetent about God-Machine though? GM and the angels, especially compared to other antagonists, look very frightening, and Demons can only eke through it to have a life, because, the GM is potent enough not to care one bit about demons. (not true, but rhetorically, yeah.)<br /> <br /> Also, who says Mage games have more united or consistent, or canon(gasp!) approach to the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T05:31:37-08:00","id":74907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knit-I-Fine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74612#post74612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Mage and Werewolf seem to have made attempts to fit together, I'm rather sure this isn't deliberate. You can't just look at plot holes and say &quot;Yeah, it's supposed to be that way.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Mage includes the Hisil. That's hardly a surprise, considering that the Shadow, from Vampire to Promethean, was in every game. Changeling and beyond changed that model - there's no Hisil in Changeling, Hunter, Geist, Mummy, Demon, or core WoD mortals unless the ST chooses to bring it in. <br /> <br /> This does not make it a universal cosmology. And I'm not looking at plot holes. I'm looking at the writers when they say that contradictions are deliberate, and that there is no cannon, unified cosmology. I'm sorry, but this the truth. The God Machine and the Inferno only exist in your mage game if your ST makes a deliberate decision to bring them in. The same with qashmallim and Prometheans. Or changelings and the Hedge/Faerie. And where these things are, what they mean, and all that? Up to debate. There are no hard answers, because individual games are free to make those decisions for themselves. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An irksome subset of Mage <i>fans</i> say this. As Dave Brookshaw has pointed out, this is decidedly at odds with the point of things like Arcane Experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed to an extent - I see mage PCs and STs act that way and assume its the default, and I think of that as a &quot;mage.&quot; A failing of the core book to sufficiently get its point across to a significant number of people, I suspect; if its played that way constantly, then I'm not going to deny it and put it on the shoulders of the few.<br /> <br /> Take that as you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's so incompetent about God-Machine though? GM and the angels, especially compared to other antagonists, look very frightening, and Demons can only eke through it to have a life, because, the GM is potent enough not to care one bit about demons. (not true, but rhetorically, yeah.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Knit is assuming that, because the God Machine is neither omnipotent nor omniscient, and demons stand an actual chance of breaking it and achieving Hell, that it makes an &quot;incompetent&quot; God. <br /> <br /> The God Machine is scarily powerful and knowledgeable when it comes to mortals. Even when it comes to demons, its scarily powerful. It is not, however, the unfailable Christian Creator God. If you expect it to be like the Christian God, then yes, the God Machine fails to live up to the unfailability, omnipotence, omniscience, omnipresence, etc. If one think that the GM is incompetent because of that, then I'm going to have point out that such an opponent is crap for a game about demons - they'd be destroyed in a heartbeat if they were against that kind of god. I certainly wouldn't play that game. <br /> <br /> <br /> The God Machine isn't the Christian God. Demons are not beings of sin and inequities. This is a game of gods and anti-gods warring against each other. This is a game about what happens when that first Heavenly Battle against the Hosts is ongoing. And using Earth as its battleground. <br /> <br /> <br /> So long as its not the Christian God and the fallen angels aren't beings of sin and evil, you'd have this kind of complaint, I think. And, lets be honest. Even if it was? You'd have other issues. Religion, especially one so big and pervasive as Christianity, always hits sore spots with people. This one, given its obvious connection to a God, draws more fire than other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T05:45:04-08:00","id":76216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=74574#post74574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fundamentals are still ones everyone knows: there are creatures who once served God, but don't anymore. They bargain for the things dearest to us with tricky deals. Sometimes, they hide in the guises of our friends. Other times, they are beings of fire and wrath. They give us what we want, but perhaps at the cost of what we need. Everyone knows these things, everyone's been warned, but the devil is in the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great post that takes care of every argument against the line concerning questioning its themes. When I first heard of <i>Demon</i>, when it was still in development, I was wary; eventually it dawned on me that it is a game whose title deserves to be called the pretentious word of &quot;Demon&quot; because it's still a game about playing fallen angels. Everyone that wants it to be more 'Christian-like' or whatever wants that, right? Basically? Fallen angels that bargain for souls, that's what we got.<br /> <br /> And angel depictions in the Old Testament fit right at home in <i>the Descent</i>, with their spinning wheels and flaming sword-arms. And the whole Gnostic angle? The Christianity we know today grew out of the Gnostic ideas people had about Christ's teachings in the religion's first few centuries. The game got everything together as far as I can see","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:54:39-08:00","id":76249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>MCN:</b><br /> Demons are not beings of sin and inequities. </div> </div> </div>They certainly are. It's just that they didn't fall because they were sinful - they're sinful because they fell, and because now they have fallen, the only way to survive is to use the resources of the world they've found themselves in - and the tools they have to use those resources are cheats, thefts, and violations. Sin and the fall are the other way round in this setting, but just as intimately linked - but perhaps more parallel to humanity's fall than the Devil's.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T09:22:27-08:00","id":76331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=76249#post76249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They certainly are. It's just that they didn't fall because they were sinful - they're sinful because they fell, and because now they have fallen, the only way to survive is to use the resources of the world they've found themselves in - and the tools they have to use those resources are cheats, thefts, and violations. Sin and the fall are the other way round in this setting, but just as intimately linked - but perhaps more parallel to humanity's fall than the Devil's.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Sure, demons aren't creatures of evil that are literally manifestations of sin. But then again, in the original mythos, demons wern't that way in the real life lore either. Demons aren't made of evil and sin, they just have no reasons not to utilize them as weapons. This is why some demons in lore were more like regular people, and could have motives other than &quot;cause people to be evil&quot;. That, gameplay wise, would be far too much like spirits for my taste. Thus, I prefer what we have. Unlike Inferno demons (who the book calls weak addicts more or less), they aren't FORCED to be evil.. which makes an evil demon truly responsible for his actions, and unable to simply say &quot;what'd you expect, I'm a demon&quot;. It helps to sell yourself on the themes to throw together a few demonic archetypes, just to see how much you CAN make it feel more like oold school demons. I created an Incubus, for example, to see if its possible to get demonic, nonmatrixy tropes with the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:04:58-08:00","id":76424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=76331#post76331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps to sell yourself on the themes to throw together a few demonic archetypes, just to see how much you CAN make it feel more like oold school demons. I created an Incubus, for example, to see if its possible to get demonic, nonmatrixy tropes with the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to having tried making a few &quot;classical&quot; demons on purpose, I've found that some of the Unchained I've made have wound up resonant with one or more of the Seven Deadlies completely by accident \u2014 it's one thing to have Mister Price the serial inheritor be greedy (when that character views material wealth in terms of potential for change) and a whole different thing for Theft-of-Breath the zombie-maker to turn out to be sedentary and reluctant to directly engage with human society (when that character is mostly trying to carve out a place to rest) or Mister Glass the doppelg\u00e4nger to wind up being wrathful, vindictive and obsessive (when that character is heavily concerned with the disjunction between appearance and reality).<br /> <br /> The things that go into Ciphers (Incarnation, Agenda, Catalyst, etc) go a long way toward producing a conventionally &quot;demonic&quot; feel for a character, I've found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-21-2014, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T05:25:04-08:00","id":76998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=76249#post76249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They certainly are. It's just that they didn't fall because they were sinful - they're sinful because they fell, and because now they have fallen, the only way to survive is to use the resources of the world they've found themselves in - and the tools they have to use those resources are cheats, thefts, and violations. Sin and the fall are the other way round in this setting, but just as intimately linked - but perhaps more parallel to humanity's fall than the Devil's.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's kinda arguing semantics and twisting words. I find there's a difference between the turning against the tyranny of the God Machine's control and assert free will, and then doing what it takes to survive, and something like the Kindred Curse or Infernal taint, which is literally mortal sin and corruption personified.<br /> <br /> The latter is what many people think of when they think of &quot;demons.&quot; Its what pop culture thinks of it. And, honestly, trying to appeal to history or reversing order isn't going to resolve that disconnect many people have when they read a book titled &quot;Demon,&quot; and yet is nothing like what they imagine a demon to be like.<br /> <br /> There are feels in it, yes. Unchained engage in morally questionable behavior. They can very easily steal or ruin lives. They tend to be more monstrous than a werewolf or changeling or mage. But they're not the embodiment of sin, corruption, and moral failings like a vampire is. And that causes a disconnect. I don't think that arguing &quot;Yes, yes they are!&quot; is very helpful in the long run.<br /> <br /> Part of the whole point of the Descent is in moving away from being just one of the Fallen and becoming more demonic. Which very likely includes ruling over a literal Hell. You don't start off there, however. <br /> <br /> No, you're the beginning of Breaking Bad. And you have a long way to go before you get to the end of Breaking Bad and become the actual antagonist type guy.<br /> <br /> I think a good way of putting it is that you're not just Fallen. You're still Falling. And the game is about if you hit that level of Hell, of sin and depravity, or if you redeem yourself in some way and halt (or reverse) your Descent. But, in any case, you don't start there. Which is what many people expect when they hear &quot;demon.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-22-2014, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T06:01:03-08:00","id":77016,"title":"","content":"This was my biggest issues to dealing with DtD. I read through it going &quot;This is not Demons&quot;. Everyone kept comparing it to the Matrix or Leverage and that made it even worse. The only way it worked for me was to stop thinking of it as some game off a sci-fi and horrible t.v. show and think of it as more Lovecraftian horror. They aren't demons and I can never see them as such but the Lovecraftian theme works better for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T10:31:56-08:00","id":77187,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I'd call it lovecraftian horror. That's usually something along the lines of Cthulhu, the great unknown horror that Man Was Not Meant To Know. I don't see that as a theme in DtD. <br /> <br /> Now, if you want to discuss Angels and Demons as more akin to Milton's Paradise Lost? Now THAT I can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T11:57:23-08:00","id":77250,"title":"","content":"Cthulhu Mythos deals with the Cthulhu critters. Lovecraftian horros deals with these vast cosmic forces that somehow mankind stumbles across and the ending results. The God-Machine most definitely fits into the role of Azathoth with the various demons taking on the roles of Shub-Niggarath, Yig, etc.. This works for me as to what the GM and DtD are about. When people compare them to Matrix, Leverage, etc..I feel like we're playing two different games. I do feel like they shouldn't have used the name Demon as this isn't anything demon/demonic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T05:34:29-08:00","id":77602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=71846#post71846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think as far as the God Machine goes, you're getting lost in the <i>aesthetic </i>while thematically the Unchained very much are Demons. They're fallen angels hiding among humans, tempting them into bargains and deals, using horrifying powers to subvert people and draw them away from God(-Machine) and they turn into monsters with a lot of the traditional trappings and visuals of Angels but with a techy <i>aesthetic.</i><br /> <br /> Very little stops you from dropping or swapping that aesthetic entirely, though I think you'd be going through a lot of work for a vocabulary update.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, it means something important that these fallen creatures, who were once called angels, are not actually associated with God in the Judeo-Christian sense. It was a big selling point for me that the old Demon: the Fallen was associated with existent mythology. This version does not appear to be associated with any existent mythology, even if it does invoke similar tropes. These angels of the God Machine are not Angels, and these demons who have fallen are not Demons.<br /> <br /> But even saying that, it is incredibly easy for anyone with these objections to refluff them into proper Demons.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:14:11-08:00","id":77619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77602#post77602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective, it means something important that these fallen creatures, who were once called angels, are not actually associated with God in the Judeo-Christian sense. It was a big selling point for me that the old Demon: the Fallen was associated with existent mythology. This version does not appear to be associated with any existent mythology, even if it does invoke similar tropes. These angels of the God Machine are not Angels, and these demons who have fallen are not Demons.<br /> <br /> But even saying that, it is incredibly easy for anyone with these objections to refluff them into proper Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing this kind of thing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack\">in this topic</a> in my free time from couple of weeks now, to be true. But too me, there should be add-on content that connects at least partially demons with existing in nWoD cosmology Inferno ( literall Hell ) and Empyrean ( literall Heaven ). I come to idea that God-Machine demons &quot;defects&quot; to Inferno's and Empyrean's Hosts if they really would want to return to Order, but retain they more human sides after the Fall. In that way we have still G-M &quot;free will&quot; demons, 'devil-like&quot; demons of Inferno and &quot;angels&quot; of Empyrean next to God Machine Angels.<br /> <br /> And there we have three major forces in DtD setting to connect or fith with: Technology ( God-Machine ), Sin ( Inferno ), Virtue ( Empyrean ) - and that is what I call good setting for free will demons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T06:38:16-08:00","id":77628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77250#post77250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cthulhu Mythos deals with the Cthulhu critters. Lovecraftian horros deals with these vast cosmic forces that somehow mankind stumbles across and the ending results. The God-Machine most definitely fits into the role of Azathoth with the various demons taking on the roles of Shub-Niggarath, Yig, etc.. This works for me as to what the GM and DtD are about. When people compare them to Matrix, Leverage, etc..I feel like we're playing two different games. I do feel like they shouldn't have used the name Demon as this isn't anything demon/demonic.</div> </div> </div> </div> While there are arguments both for and against the idea that Demon isn't about actual demons... I will argue up and down that it is about Fallen Angels. I personally don't quite sync with the sin vibe some others apparently do. That said, if we ignore the technology aspects of the game, they DO run with Fallen Angel themes like mad. Soul pacts, hellfire, rebellion / war against Heaven, divine wrath, temptation and goin' succubus/incubus, law versus chaos stuff, down with criminal underworld, changing one's form at will (not just to demon form, but between human appearances), twisting words, etc.<br /> <br /> And then, the game's theme pretty much is summed up with the line from Milton's Paradise Lost: &quot;Its better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven.&quot; That's the granddaddy right there.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think I will say that the game isn't about playing a Demon. Its about playing an angel that's turning into a demon. You're not Fallen, you're Falling. Thus, the Descent. At the end, you'll either redeem yourself (Integrator), or become demonic (pretty much everyone else).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What does that have to do with the game being compared to the Matrix? Well, the Matrix is basically a religious story wrapped up in technological terms. And that's what Demon is. Its the usual Christian Fall myth using robots instead of beings made of pure light. So, a bit of sci-fi instead of pure fantasy terms. ((And, by fantasy, I mean the genre, not delusions, so no offense)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:00:55-08:00","id":77633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77628#post77628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does that have to do with the game being compared to the Matrix? Well, the Matrix is basically a religious story wrapped up in technological terms. And that's what Demon is. Its the usual Christian Fall myth using robots instead of beings made of pure light. So, a bit of sci-fi instead of pure fantasy terms. ((And, by fantasy, I mean the genre, not delusions, so no offense)).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>Demon: the Descent! More than meets the eye!</i><br /> <i>Angelbots wage their battle to destroy the evil forces of the Demonicons!</i><br /> <i>Demon: the Descent! Robots in disguise!</i><br /> <i>Demon: the Descent! More than meets the eye!</i><br /> <i>Demon: the Descent!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:34:17-08:00","id":77646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77628#post77628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While there are arguments both for and against the idea that Demon isn't about actual demons... I will argue up and down that it is about Fallen Angels. I personally don't quite sync with the sin vibe some others apparently do. That said, if we ignore the technology aspects of the game, they DO run with Fallen Angel themes like mad. Soul pacts, hellfire, rebellion / war against Heaven, divine wrath, temptation and goin' succubus/incubus, law versus chaos stuff, down with criminal underworld, changing one's form at will (not just to demon form, but between human appearances), twisting words, etc.<br /> <br /> And then, the game's theme pretty much is summed up with the line from Milton's Paradise Lost: &quot;Its better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven.&quot; That's the granddaddy right there.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think I will say that the game isn't about playing a Demon. Its about playing an angel that's turning into a demon. You're not Fallen, you're Falling. Thus, the Descent. At the end, you'll either redeem yourself (Integrator), or become demonic (pretty much everyone else).<br /> <br /> <br /> What does that have to do with the game being compared to the Matrix? Well, the Matrix is basically a religious story wrapped up in technological terms. And that's what Demon is. Its the usual Christian Fall myth using robots instead of beings made of pure light. So, a bit of sci-fi instead of pure fantasy terms. ((And, by fantasy, I mean the genre, not delusions, so no offense)).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's rare when something someone said on the internet gets to really change my opinion, and I think MCN's post really did change my opinion towards Demon. Thank you, as I can enjoy Demon the Descent even more than I was already! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My favorite part of your post is &quot;You're not Fallen, you're Falling.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hey props man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T07:51:15-08:00","id":77650,"title":"","content":"I'm inclinde to agree with Torete, very nice post, quite compelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T11:40:38-08:00","id":77755,"title":"","content":"Awww.... thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T12:31:48-08:00","id":77779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77628#post77628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will argue up and down that it is about Fallen Angels. I personally don't quite sync with the sin vibe some others apparently do. That said, if we ignore the technology aspects of the game, they DO run with Fallen Angel themes like mad. Soul pacts, hellfire, rebellion / war against Heaven, divine wrath, temptation and goin' succubus/incubus, law versus chaos stuff, down with criminal underworld, changing one's form at will (not just to demon form, but between human appearances), twisting words, etc.<br /> <br /> And then, the game's theme pretty much is summed up with the line from Milton's Paradise Lost: &quot;Its better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven.&quot; That's the granddaddy right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something else occurred to me that an earlier poster mentioned. Most of the things you have listed here are already present in a different splat book; Changeling: the Lost. If we put aside the faerie themes the same way we are putting aside the robot themes, we not only end up with a splat that arguably has more Fallen Angel themes, but has more themes based around the idea of sin and vice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T04:00:32-08:00","id":78216,"title":"","content":"Vampire covers much of the same things Promethean does - Golconda anyone? Mummy and Mage with the ancient civilizations of Irem/Atlantis? Werewolf and Geist with their necessary tasks of keeping spiritual beings in line. Vanilla mortals and hunters. Heck, mortals, hunters, and mages are all humans exploring the supernatural in some way! Games share a ton of themes between them. So, its no surprise that Changeling, a game renowned for its flexibility, can do some of the same stuff Demon can. It can also do vampire themes, werewolf spirit cop themes, mage themes, etc. But not as well as those other games.<br /> <br /> So, I think that its safe to say that, while many games can touch on the same themes as Demon: the Descent (I've played fallen angel PCs in Vampire, Changeling, Mage, Promethean, and Infernal Possessed in a Hunter game, to name a few), DtD specializes in those themes in a way that you can't achieve in other games; at least not without a highly specialized setting and house rules. <br /> <br /> For example - all Demons have a weakness. Exposure. Because, then, the God Machine sends its divine angels to slay them. Having a weakness to divine forces is thematic, and is front-and-center to the game; interference from most other godlike spirit beings happen because of plot, not because of character actions in an unrelated effort. That makes it not only an ever present threat the Unchained need to consider all the time, but highlights how much of a connection there is between angels and demons. Demons are fantastic liars, and can never trust what another fellow is saying; most other games have ways of determining truth. The spy theme of Demon helps highlight a cold war state between Heavenly and Hell-bound forces. <br /> <br /> Its the little things like that that shift the game around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T09:35:18-08:00","id":78366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=78216#post78216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think that its safe to say that, while many games can touch on the same themes as Demon: the Descent (I've played fallen angel PCs in Vampire, Changeling, Mage, Promethean, and Infernal Possessed in a Hunter game, to name a few), DtD specializes in those themes in a way that you can't achieve in other games; at least not without a highly specialized setting and house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually making the claim that Changeling: the Lost does most of those demonic themes better than Demon: the Descent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T15:24:15-08:00","id":78694,"title":"","content":"EDIT : Removed post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-24-2014, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T08:24:41-08:00","id":79334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=78366#post78366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually making the claim that Changeling: the Lost does most of those demonic themes better than Demon: the Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div> Major stumbling block, though. Demons, to embody sin, have to have made that choice rather than have it forced upon them. To be a fallen angel, you start as an angel (knowing the secrets of the cosmos) and go down. Changelings, starting as humans, are far too out-of-context to Arcadia to represent the idea of cosmic gnosis. Plus, changeling society may support white lies and gray areas, most changeling societies hate/despise truly evil things (including things Demons have to do just to get by). I keep imagining what it would like like, truly, to see through the eyes of the Judeo Christian God--seeing all the secrets, every detail, every outcome. And to human eyes, that kind of advanced mind and subtle action shouldn't look the same as what Mages or Mummies traffic with. it SHOULD be mind bogglingly complex, layered like physics and calculus. It should require vast amounts of advanced knowledge and technology for humans to match the might of God. Imagine it less as demons and god being robots, and more that human beings are only now getting a taste of just how complicated the secrets of the cosmos are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:06:46-08:00","id":79767,"title":"","content":"Is there anyone who could go more into detail comparing/contrasting demons and changelings? I am not too familiar with lost and am curious that people keep bringing it up regarding demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T17:19:54-08:00","id":79776,"title":"","content":"I might over the weekend-the comparisons between the two have been readily apparent to me since I got Demon, as well as how they are distinctly different games that invalidate the entire &quot;Oh, we have this game already&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> They're both really alike and completely unalike. It's a matter of how you look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:34:44-08:00","id":80567,"title":"","content":"The problem people have with this topic is that they're often operating under a stricter definition of angelic or demonic than most people. The archetypal angelic and demonic exist separate from the religions that claim to have spawned them, much as understanding of God changed over the centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","user":"ErichZahn","date":".  slash and burn, avoiding generalizations or uncomfortable derails. 02-26-2014, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/936-erichzahn","name":"ErichZahn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T17:05:05-08:00","id":80631,"title":"","content":"See, changeling can do pretty much any kind of fairy tale, to an extent. And there are demons and angels in fairy tales - the snow fairy's mirror was made by the Devil to take up to Heaven and mock angels with, for instance. That said, it touches on a very different take of angels and demons than Demon the Descent. Indeed, it plays with the idea of angels and demons in the same way it plays with any light and dark fae, with Seelie and Unseelie. <br /> <br /> DtD, on the other hand, takes the idea of angels as created servants of a powerful entity instead of fantasy creatures born of human dreams. Changeling is a game of dreams, while Demon is a game of understanding the laws of our world. If you're a fan of Supernatural, for instance, the angels from that show are very in line with DtD, and not at all with CtL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T22:42:55-08:00","id":80818,"title":"","content":"Guess I will throw my hat into the ring. Ok, I absolutely love DTD and hate DTD. I love DTD for the ideas and the potential it brings. It really is a fascinating work and I am glad I backed it as a kickstarter. Now, I just hate that it has absolutely nothing to do with demons. Wait, I can hear the defenders jumping on the keyboards with the argument that the theme of angels/demons/fall..etc. The problem with that, you have to strip away everything, but the barest of description and that can be attached to anything. I can turn an innocence game into a demon game. The PC are kids, the story is a mother(almighty authority figure) with loving good children (angels) comes to the kitchen(heaven), the mother tells the kids to not eat the food on the table, but the kids eat anyway (they rebel), the mother kicks the kids (now demons) out of the kitchen (the fall) and have to go to their room (hell). <br /> <br /> By the definition on here, this would justifiably be called a demon game. I could go further more examples of bargains/pacts(offer toys to other kids to come over and play), having souls dragged to hell(have other kids get in trouble and sent to room), storming heaven(sneaking into the kitchen)..etc. (hmm, this actually would be kind of a cool game...but I digress).<br /> <br /> I think you cannot totally ignore the conscious consensus of what imagery pops up when you say demon. While I think it would have been fine to shed angels, god..etc. In many modern works, they do not even show up. Still, demons are mostly known as tormentors, corruptors, seducers, tricking and dragging souls to hell for damnation. However, I cannot think of any common works that make me think demons are spies/machines without some heavy reinterpretation and that is the problem. If I have to warp my world view with a sledgehammer so much to make DTD fit the definition of demon, Or strip out the majority of the matrix/leverage parts of the game and fill in with more traditional demon aspects then something is wrong. <br /> <br /> The game feels like leaverage/matrix with just a very very light coat of demon paint to justify the name. Do a little game reversal, try changing this much up with another game line. If vampires had been cybernetic creatures created in a lab that drain humans of biolectrical energy, can't walk into sunlight because the emp from the sun messes with their cyber gear, and turn other humans into vampires through implanting technology in them. Would we be ok with calling them vampires? They fit the definition if we look at the core definition of vampire.<br /> <br /> Really, the only thing I really see demon related is cults, pacts, and even requiring the signature in blood for a soul pact seems so out of place compared to everything else in the book.<br /> <br /> I do feel DTD is very limiting at what it can do. The main antagonists are angels who the PC will never interact with except in confrontation/fighting by the way it is written and infrastructures are little more than destroy or capture the flag games. I also find angels pretty boring, just machines with a little personality and no free will. Sure, you can maybe make one fall, but is it worth it?<br /> <br /> Again, this is an amazing game, I just can't call it a demon game. This would work a lot better if we had a mixture of inferno in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77016#post77016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was my biggest issues to dealing with DtD. I read through it going &quot;This is not Demons&quot;. Everyone kept comparing it to the Matrix or Leverage and that made it even worse. The only way it worked for me was to stop thinking of it as some game off a sci-fi and horrible t.v. show and think of it as more Lovecraftian horror. They aren't demons and I can never see them as such but the Lovecraftian theme works better for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is EXACTLY what I thought. This would fit way better in my mind. An Alien/lovecraftian/x-files inspired game works much better with the levearage/matrix aspect, especially with the reality warping going on. Instead of demons, the PC could be creatures from beyond. Some could be from the god machine, some might be other (alien) factions, some could be captured altered humans, some might be rebelled creatures, etc. Cults work (worshiping alien gods/beings), pacts work just like dtd except the reason they use them is to not only to hide, but also to survive in our reality.etc.<br /> <br /> Gives way more freedom to do a lot of stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=77619#post77619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm doing this kind of thing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/21063-supenatural-shard-empyrean-inferno-setting-hack\">in this topic</a> in my free time from couple of weeks now, to be true. But too me, there should be add-on content that connects at least partially demons with existing in nWoD cosmology Inferno ( literall Hell ) and Empyrean ( literall Heaven ). I come to idea that God-Machine demons &quot;defects&quot; to Inferno's and Empyrean's Hosts if they really would want to return to Order, but retain they more human sides after the Fall. In that way we have still G-M &quot;free will&quot; demons, 'devil-like&quot; demons of Inferno and &quot;angels&quot; of Empyrean next to God Machine Angels.<br /> <br /> And there we have three major forces in DtD setting to connect or fith with: Technology ( God-Machine ), Sin ( Inferno ), Virtue ( Empyrean ) - and that is what I call good setting for free will demons. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love this and really think WW should do something like this. Have demons have different possible paths to hell that alters demons to one of the forces or paths like tech/gm,sin/inferno,virt/empyrean,other..etc. Demons would change, some might stay the same default dtd demon, others might start changing to appear more inferno like demons..etc. It would free up the game from its boxed in spy game to something that fits more traditional definition of demons for those who want to play it that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Any supplements probably needs to be more balanced and have stuff that caters to the new dtd and those who want something a little more traditional. More embeds/exploits that feel more demony would help. Along with motivations and justifications why demons might act more like traditional demons like (admittedly, extreme case) hellraiser. <br /> <br /> Again, a fantastic and great game, just not one I can call demon at the moment.<br /> <br /> I do hope this did not come across as hostile in any way. After a long day of work, my writing sometimes comes across that way, it isn't I promise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:37:17-08:00","id":80839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any supplements probably needs to be more balanced and have stuff that caters to the new dtd and those who want something a little more traditional. More embeds/exploits that feel more demony would help. Along with motivations and justifications why demons might act more like traditional demons like (admittedly, extreme case) hell raiser.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving aside my problems with the tenor of your complaint\u2026<br /> <br /> The most visible faction of Unchained (going by the Beat criteria and Resolution effect for their Agenda Condition) has a distinct reputation for sowing strife that is likely to have made its way into the popular unconscious of the setting. In this sense, much as with Werewolf's take on how werewolf legends relate to the Uratha, the disconnect is explained by a the rare slip-ups of a heavily secrecy-oriented group being better-known than its more common practices. People have complained about Werewolf not matching most people's definition of &quot;werewolf&quot; as well! I submit that this is an unproductive line of thought in comparison to looking at how to make it work without spinning daft analogies about Heaven as Mom's kitchen (and I say this as someone who believes one can easily and at least somewhat meaningfully apply the monikers of &quot;demon&quot; and &quot;Hell&quot; to portions of literally any of the other gamelines).<br /> <br /> As to angels, a thing I learned about from a Chasidic poet who spoke at my university concerns the concept of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Worlds\" target=\"_blank\">Four Worlds</a>. It's late and Wikipedia is notoriously tricky about layman's terms, but the way the concept was explained to me, essentially, was that each of the Worlds is further removed from God, and vice versa, such that in the nearest World to God that is not actual unity with God one is nevertheless more certain that God exists than that they themself do. If we take this notion of Words increasingly removed from God and express it as a vertical, linear progression, with unity with God at the top\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026then complete free-will and self-certainty would be at the nadir of a descent.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">I note also that this dovetails nicely with the degrees of separation between angels, exiles, demons, and theoretical completely-Descended-demons.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:09:57-08:00","id":81036,"title":"","content":"Quick question: How many people here have actually done some study on Gnosticism?<br /> <br /> Cause once again, the more I researched that, the more and more the Unchained look like demons to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T10:41:05-08:00","id":81126,"title":"","content":"I would agree even if Unchained are gnostic like demons, and in allegory are very much demonic - they just don't have whole &quot;personality&quot;. There aren't &quot;bad&quot; demons, there aren't &quot;good&quot; angels, they are just working machines and broken machines. That's why I advise to put two other forces that are in World of Darkness - I mean Inferno and Emyprean - to make setting a bit more &quot;gothic-like&quot; demonic. I would say that God-Machine was physical part of Empyrean that gone rebel/wrong, and is just sustaining his own growth, when eons before were making physicall Angels for Empyrean ( or Principle from Promethean ). And there you can have classical demons - &quot;free&quot; ( now DtD ), &quot;bad&quot; ( Inferno, controlled by they Vice ), and &quot;true angels&quot; ( Empyrean, controlled by VIrtue ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-27-2014, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T12:48:05-08:00","id":81178,"title":"","content":"Everyone here that can't see the connection of this demon and others needs to take a step back and just remove the damn word Machine.<br /> <br /> Lets break it down.<br /> <br /> Demons were servants of god who fell, previously they were angels.<br /> <br /> Demons make deals for 'souls'.<br /> <br /> Demons lie.<br /> <br /> Demons Hide things.<br /> <br /> Demons cause trouble, dragging people into their underworld dealings or otherwise tempting humans into giving things away.<br /> <br /> Sounds pretty demon-like to me.<br /> <br /> If you want something else, play one of the Possessed in Inferno.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:40:30-08:00","id":81207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do feel DTD is very limiting at what it can do. The main antagonists are angels who the PC will never interact with except in confrontation/fighting by the way it is written and infrastructures are little more than destroy or capture the flag games. I also find angels pretty boring, just machines with a little personality and no free will. </div> </div> </div>Have you read the book yet? I mean, I'm only about 100 pages into it and I've seen lots to contradict what you've just said there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:16:28-08:00","id":81231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess I will throw my hat into the ring. Ok, I absolutely love DTD and hate DTD. I love DTD for the ideas and the potential it brings. It really is a fascinating work and I am glad I backed it as a kickstarter. Now, I just hate that it has absolutely nothing to do with demons. Wait, I can hear the defenders jumping on the keyboards with the argument that the theme of angels/demons/fall..etc. The problem with that, you have to strip away everything, but the barest of description and that can be attached to anything. I can turn an innocence game into a demon game. The PC are kids, the story is a mother(almighty authority figure) with loving good children (angels) comes to the kitchen(heaven), the mother tells the kids to not eat the food on the table, but the kids eat anyway (they rebel), the mother kicks the kids (now demons) out of the kitchen (the fall) and have to go to their room (hell).<br /> <br /> By the definition on here, this would justifiably be called a demon game. I could go further more examples of bargains/pacts(offer toys to other kids to come over and play), having souls dragged to hell(have other kids get in trouble and sent to room), storming heaven(sneaking into the kitchen)..etc. (hmm, this actually would be kind of a cool game...but I digress).<br /> <br /> I think you cannot totally ignore the conscious consensus of what imagery pops up when you say demon. While I think it would have been fine to shed angels, god..etc. In many modern works, they do not even show up. Still, demons are mostly known as tormentors, corruptors, seducers, tricking and dragging souls to hell for damnation. However, I cannot think of any common works that make me think demons are spies/machines without some heavy reinterpretation and that is the problem. If I have to warp my world view with a sledgehammer so much to make DTD fit the definition of demon, Or strip out the majority of the matrix/leverage parts of the game and fill in with more traditional demon aspects then something is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts exacty. Even when my players and I had a blast with session. Setting just feel a bit TOO RESTRICTIVE on whole &quot;it must be a technospys!!!&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this and really think WW should do something like this. Have demons have different possible paths to hell that alters demons to one of the forces or paths like tech/gm,sin/inferno,virt/empyrean,other..etc. Demons would change, some might stay the same default dtd demon, others might start changing to appear more inferno like demons..etc. It would free up the game from its boxed in spy game to something that fits more traditional definition of demons for those who want to play it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concure. The solution is just adding two more, classical demon and angels Agendas. It really solve monotony of setting, and make players characterse more variant. Beside, it would give as 4x6 spread of splats, almost iconic 5x5 for nWoD. Couple of pages in one of supplements would be really enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81178#post81178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want something else, play one of the Possessed in Inferno.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It don't solve the problem. It's like saying &quot;if you want to play sorcerer, play <b>Second Sight</b>&quot;. It could have element you look, it could have some mechanics. But it whole &quot;gameline&quot; stand point is too limited for whole game onto it self. Like having material to run 3-4 session game, and whole game line to run multiples chronicles by 20 each - comparisson of <b>Second Sight</b> to <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> here. <br /> <br /> And, once again, Possessed are about Mortals being directed be demons, not Demons controlling mortals. Whole minigame perception is putted in other way. In <b>Inferno</b> game you won't have multiple soul pacts, proper angels described both mechaniclly and setting wise, and demons are just evil. Not &quot;human evil&quot; like Descent Demons, only evil, so they are partially unplayable in long term.<br /> <br /> Also, I've described ideal solution for developers how to fix all problems - just adding two more Agendas for PCs to choose. If they are reclutant on doing this, they could take mine almost 100$ from Kickstarter and do it for them. I think it's counted for those 4-6 pages needed in DtD supplement on two more Agendas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-27-2014, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T04:43:39-08:00","id":81517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The problem with that, you have to strip away everything, but the barest of description and that can be attached to anything.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not quite. I used to think the same until I sat down and actually made a PC for the game. If anything, I'm having a much harder time thinking of my guy as a robot/cyborg than a fallen angel. While the book pushes the whole techno aspects, I don't really feel them as much in game. Perhaps that's a failing of the writing to properly convey that to people, but not something I see play out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you cannot totally ignore the conscious consensus of what imagery pops up when you say demon. While I think it would have been fine to shed angels, god..etc. In many modern works, they do not even show up. Still, demons are mostly known as tormentors, corruptors, seducers, tricking and dragging souls to hell for damnation. However, I cannot think of any common works that make me think demons are spies/machines without some heavy reinterpretation and that is the problem. </div> </div> </div> I don't see &quot;spy.&quot; I see &quot;on going war against a God.&quot; Its just more like the Cold War than WWII. You're launching guerrilla strikes against heaven.<br /> <br /> That said... tormentor, corrupter, seducer? Check - Unchained do it all the time for resources in their war effort. Just not dragging souls to hell for damnation, which, if you happen to read any modern fiction where the main characters, or even one of the supporting cast, are a fallen angel, dragging damned people to hell for torment just isn't done. Even Demon the Fallen, which never had this issue, made it impossible to drag souls to hell for damnation. It just doesn't make sense to play that trope for fallen angels.<br /> <br /> Again, perhaps its a failing of the writing for not clearly portraying this, but its a story about a war against heaven. That seems to fit in well, to me, with the popular consensus of a fallen angel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If vampires had been cybernetic creatures created in a lab that drain humans of biolectrical energy, can't walk into sunlight because the emp from the sun messes with their cyber gear, and turn other humans into vampires through implanting technology in them. Would we be ok with calling them vampires? They fit the definition if we look at the core definition of vampire. </div> </div> </div> No it wouldn't, but that's because Vampires are a disease. If you made a sci-fi equivalent to vampires, you'd do it through a bio-engineered super virus that altered the victims when infected. Actually, if you happen to read any of the Kate Daniels novels, that's exactly what her vampires are - a disease. Its quite common to portray vampires this way, with that scientific explanation.<br /> <br /> Now, angels? From a sci-fi point of view? Totally robots. Watch Supernatural. There, angels are often described in terms of robots. Lack of Free Will. Hacking into an angelic minds uses computer references. Et cetera. And its not the only one. Machine angels aren't exactly uncommon in fiction.<br /> <br /> I agree that I don't really like calling it a demon game. I do, however, call it a game of Falling Angels. You're not in Hell yet. You've not been punished for your sins. The Fall is ongoing, and the War in Heaven hasn't ended yet. There hasn't been an end, where God has triumphed over the rebel Hosts and locked them in Hell. Most novels and stories do start post-Fall. The do assume that the War is over, part of history. Descent does not.<br /> <br /> Also, blood in pacts? Makes perfect sense when you realize that most GM rituals (occult matrices) require some kind of human sacrifice to operate. Angels are -bloody- and made from ritual sacrifices. As well, also makes perfect sense when you think &quot;game of fallen angels&quot; and not &quot;game of robots.&quot; Blood magic is everywhere in DtD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-28-2014, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:02:39-08:00","id":81521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is an amazing game, I just can't call it a demon game. This would work a lot better if we had a mixture of inferno in it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? Seriously, what would Inferno add other than &quot;Ohhhh! They're evil vampiric things now!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love this and really think WW should do something like this. Have demons have different possible paths to hell that alters demons to one of the forces or paths like tech/gm,sin/inferno,virt/empyrean,other..etc. Demons would change, some might stay the same default dtd demon, others might start changing to appear more inferno like demons..etc. It would free up the game from its boxed in spy game to something that fits more traditional definition of demons for those who want to play it that way. </div> </div> </div> Ummm.... it actually does offer that? I mean, its not spelled out what happens when you achieve your Hell, as that'd be a tier 4 thing like archmastery, and beyond the scope of the current book we have.<br /> <br /> Tempters trick people into pacts so they can live hedonistic lifestyles in a realm they designed free from God's influence. Integrators reject demonhood and become angels. Sabatours raise Hell on Earth. Interrogators become the wise, all knowing demon people go to for answers.<br /> <br /> The entire spy thing is there for the War against Heaven angle. Which is a part of the popular definition of demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, a fantastic and great game, just not one I can call demon at the moment. </div> </div> </div> Because they're not demons yet. They're falling angels on the path to becoming a demon. Thus, Descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-28-2014, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:58:01-08:00","id":81572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=80818#post80818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip<br /> <br /> I love this and really think WW should do something like this. Have demons have different possible paths to hell that alters demons to one of the forces or paths like tech/gm,sin/inferno,virt/empyrean,other..etc. Demons would change, some might stay the same default dtd demon, others might start changing to appear more inferno like demons..etc. It would free up the game from its boxed in spy game to something that fits more traditional definition of demons for those who want to play it that way.<br /> <br /> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I mostly agree with MCN here, I think this is what I would really really like to see. If they add these kind of supplements, (which I see as within the realm of possibility) lots of complaints that DtD is not, thematically or aesthetically, 'Demons,' whouldn't be. Some link between the unchained to any other kinds of demons, even just in sidebars, would actually be awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Annnnd yeah... I would actually want tier 4 books for all the other splats as well. I know it's pretty hard, but I think DtD is one of the splats that is more adaptable to tier 4 settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:04:46-08:00","id":81574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81521#post81521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're not demons yet. They're falling angels on the path to becoming a demon. Thus, Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'll note that this isn't exactly a new thing for the nWoD - most if not all of the major gamelines are in some fashion about <i>becoming</i> something, and in Demon's case it wouldn't make as much sense to have demonhood be the intermediary state in comparison to, say, Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T07:36:19-08:00","id":81587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>torete:</b><br /> While I mostly agree with MCN here, I think this is what I would really really like to see. If they add these kind of supplements, (which I see as within the realm of possibility) lots of complaints that DtD is not, thematically or aesthetically, 'Demons,' whouldn't be. Some link between the unchained to any other kinds of demons, even just in sidebars, would actually be awesome! </div> </div> </div>While I haven't read the Mage Storyteller's Guide, I seem to recall it has a chapter about reframing magic as mad science, psi, and so on. You could probably have a similar chapter in one of the DtD supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:22:35-08:00","id":81724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81231#post81231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, once again, Possessed are about Mortals being directed be demons, not Demons controlling mortals. Whole minigame perception is putted in other way. In <b>Inferno</b> game you won't have multiple soul pacts, proper angels described both mechaniclly and setting wise, and demons are just evil. Not &quot;human evil&quot; like Descent Demons, only evil, so they are partially unplayable in long term.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since I just knocked up a Possesed/Inferno version of Amaimon (well, the version of Amaimon present in Ao No Exorcist) last night without too much trouble, I'm gonna have to disagree with this. You might not have the same ease of body jumping as in Supernatural, but then again, you might. It would be pretty doable.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about two things, though.<br /> <br /> A) What are some demons people are trying to create with DtD that they can't because it's too restrictive?<br /> <br /> B) ArcaneArts, it's almost the weekend, so I'm curious if you're still planning on knocking out a compare/contrast between Demon and Changeling because I am very interested~ ^w^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T14:44:42-08:00","id":81775,"title":"","content":"We'll see how Unity/grammar review goes-It's gonna be a long one.<br /> <br /> Particularly since I got a copy of Techgnosis now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T19:39:35-08:00","id":81882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81775#post81775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll see how Unity/grammar review goes-It's gonna be a long one.<br /> <br /> Particularly since I got a copy of Techgnosis now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'll keep my hopes up, then~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:11:29-08:00","id":81899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81724#post81724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I just knocked up a Possesed/Inferno version of Amaimon (well, the version of Amaimon present in Ao No Exorcist) last night without too much trouble, I'm gonna have to disagree with this. You might not have the same ease of body jumping as in Supernatural, but then again, you might. It would be pretty doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see what I would use from DtD for &quot;proper&quot; demons - Soul pacts. Sin's power's beyond third dot's. Demon's energy based on his &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; status. Mortal and Demonic forms. WHOLE concept and mechanics for Angels. God-Machine as very intersting third party. Interlocks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81724#post81724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) What are some demons people are trying to create with DtD that they can't because it's too restrictive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Classical ones? I manioned couple of times - I would love for more Supernatural-like demons on DtD levels, like Crowley ( without whole King of Hell things ). Also, proper angles. And power generated from Virtue ( for Angels ) and Vice ( for demons ). And whole DtD setting, or at least most of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's I find ironic, is that &quot;classical&quot; demons are more &quot;human-like&quot; that those described in DtD - yeah, you have free will, yeah, you Fall because you become human, but most of the time you really could be just inteligent automata, not person with at least half personality. &quot;Classical&quot; demons are whole about personality, even if the are all just &quot;bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of my players on convention session was all about &quot;I just hide and watch&quot; - it was very logical in this paranoid setting, but also was illogical to me in terms of Virtue and Vice, and whole rest of personality fallen angles should have. But I see why he done it. I'm not saying whole demons should be like this. Or even most. But they should be, from time to time. &quot;More human than human&quot;, like Rob Zombie was saying.<br /> <br /> And last but not least - let's look on most known modern fallen angel we know now. Supernatural's Castiel starts like automaton spirit working for Heaven, goes almost human like, to end on as &quot;rebelious angel&quot;. He is part of the Host, just have very special part in it - and his whole story on those seasons is great demon/fallen angel example. Where in DtD setting is place for character like Castiel, I'm asking? Integrator he isn't because most of the time he defies Order. Not to mentioned that Integrators are partially insane and autodestructive idea in itelf, I must mentioned. They are just basiclly want's to be killed by God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Or look on Crowley - he is Inferno-like demon, but also has personality. We know that all he is doing for himself and his dark desires, but I wouldn't just make him a Tempter, as he isn't doing it all &quot;just because it's fun&quot;. He has plan. He is wicked and &quot;evil&quot; becuase he is rewarded by doing this ( i.e. souls and power in Hell ). Where is place for this kind of characters in DtD setting as it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-28-2014, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:23:17-08:00","id":81903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81899#post81899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Classical ones? I manioned couple of times - I would love for more Supernatural-like demons on DtD levels. Also, proper angles.</div> </div> </div> </div>what about the obtuse and acute ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:34:08-08:00","id":81904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81899#post81899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mentioned that Integrators are partially insane and autodestructive idea in itelf, I must mentioned. They are just basiclly want's to be killed by God-Machine.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]We know that all he is doing for himself and his dark desires, but I wouldn't just make him a Tempter, as he isn't doing it all &quot;just because it's fun&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, I think we have a PEBCAK issue here, because you're not actually describing the Agendas whose names you're saying in any comprehensive fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T20:41:19-08:00","id":81910,"title":"","content":"And on a semi-related noted, demons who basically just want to be killed by the God Machine generally don't live long enough to join the Integrators. Heaven finds them with wings of lightning.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Integrators much(personally, not conceptually), but I give them this credit-The bastards want to live and do things on their terms. Heaven alone is no longer enough for them. Though we may mock them for not being Wolves, still they will be Shepherds rather than Sheep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T21:47:11-08:00","id":81943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81899#post81899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's see what I would use from DtD for &quot;proper&quot; demons - Soul pacts. Sin's power's beyond third dot's. Demon's energy based on his &quot;Fallen Angel&quot; status. Mortal and Demonic forms. WHOLE concept and mechanics for Angels. God-Machine as very intersting third party. Interlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mixing and matching is always a valid way to go, though I should have clarified that I was only countering the idea of Inferno's Possessed still being wholly about the mortal vs demon conflict. You can very easily play possessed as, well, the demon inhabiting the meatsuit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81899#post81899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Classical ones? I manioned couple of times - I would love for more Supernatural-like demons on DtD levels, like Crowley ( without whole King of Hell things ). Also, proper angles. And power generated from Virtue ( for Angels ) and Vice ( for demons ). And whole DtD setting, or at least most of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What's I find ironic, is that &quot;classical&quot; demons are more &quot;human-like&quot; that those described in DtD - yeah, you have free will, yeah, you Fall because you become human, but most of the time you really could be just inteligent automata, not person with at least half personality. &quot;Classical&quot; demons are whole about personality, even if the are all just &quot;bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> One of my players on convention session was all about &quot;I just hide and watch&quot; - it was very logical in this paranoid setting, but also was illogical to me in terms of Virtue and Vice, and whole rest of personality fallen angles should have. But I see why he done it. I'm not saying whole demons should be like this. Or even most. But they should be, from time to time. &quot;More human than human&quot;, like Rob Zombie was saying.<br /> <br /> And last but not least - let's look on most known modern fallen angel we know now. Supernatural's Castiel starts like automaton spirit working for Heaven, goes almost human like, to end on as &quot;rebelious angel&quot;. He is part of the Host, just have very special part in it - and his whole story on those seasons is great demon/fallen angel example. Where in DtD setting is place for character like Castiel, I'm asking? Integrator he isn't because most of the time he defies Order. Not to mentioned that Integrators are partially insane and autodestructive idea in itelf, I must mentioned. They are just basiclly want's to be killed by God-Machine.<br /> <br /> Or look on Crowley - he is Inferno-like demon, but also has personality. We know that all he is doing for himself and his dark desires, but I wouldn't just make him a Tempter, as he isn't doing it all &quot;just because it's fun&quot;. He has plan. He is wicked and &quot;evil&quot; becuase he is rewarded by doing this ( i.e. souls and power in Hell ). Where is place for this kind of characters in DtD setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so I have to admit I'm not huge in the Supernatural fandom. What they do with myths just isn't my particular cup of tea. Then again, I come from a background not particularly steeped in Christian mythos. I had a stepfather once who had a bible, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> However, I've pulled up the Supernatural wiki, so I'll see what I can do. Mind you, I'm just skimming for now, because the wiki is a little hard on my eyes. I'm also working primarily with the Kickstarter copy, since I haven't had a chance to purchase the full book yet.<br /> <br /> For his original incarnation, before falling, I would say either Messenger or Psychopomp are likely jobs for him to work at -- I'm leaning towards psychopomp, as it fits a canon talent for putting things together, however messenger would be ideal if he was doing this to people rather than supplies. Messenger would also suit his &quot;suave businessman&quot; concept. After the Fall, I would say he's driven to experience humanity in it's fullness, and connecting with humans, although is ways of doing so may not be entirely appropriate to the perspective of someone who was raised in a normal, functioning household. I'm going to go ahead and go with Messenger here after all; as a Messenger, he was able to interact with people to the extent that it did what the God-Machine wanted, but he craved more interaction (I'm basing this off of: &quot;In <i><a href=\"http://supernatural.wikia.com/wiki/Sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\">Sacrifice</a></i>, as Sam cured Crowley of his demonic nature, he starts to reveal the reason he does what he does is because he just wants to be loved. It's possible, based on his reaction to his own confession, that this is true and his time being tortured in Hell twisted his desire to an megalomanic need for power and respect. He also displayed some regret for his actions, asking Sam where he could even begin to ask for forgiveness while discussing Sam's own confession to purify his blood. &quot;), and so he fell when he started using his Messenger powers to <i>make</i> people like him.<br /> <br /> Feeling even more isolated and alone, he became more and more destructive, but never quite started living solely for destructions sake. He still wanted something out of it. He wasn't some mindless monster with a baseball bat.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm going to go with <b>Messenger/Tempter</b>, possibly Messenger / Tempter &amp; Saboteur if double agendas are still a thing. As for Exploits and Embeds, I'm not going to sort through them too hard. Sorry!<br /> <br /> Combustion is an obvious choice of embed, based on his fire powers, while Cool Heads Prevail makes sense for his character, as does Devil's Advocate, since it seems he likes arguing. Plus, people arguing with each other aren't arguing with him! He has healing powers, so On The Mend would be a good choice.<br /> <br /> Alibi would be good, as would Authorized. and since he can manipulate memories in canon, Homogenous Memory. Never Here, Without a Trace, Heart's Desire, and Trick of the Light might work very well with another Voice embed as an interlock to allow him to mimic voices, or you could achieve something similar with a glitch.<br /> <br /> The red eyes effect could also be a glitch.<br /> <br /> Affliction would be a good exploit for him, as would Four Minutes Ago, and Incendiary.<br /> <br /> Electrical sight could fit his demonic form, and again, to suit the red eyed demon of the crossroads thing, they could be filled with red sparks of electricity. Inhuman strength, Sonic Acuity (maybe he has large, batlike ears), Tough As Stone, Blind Sense, Electric Jolt (electricity sparks between parts of his body that get too close to each other, like the crook of his elbow or between his fingers), Electrical Resistance, Fire Resistance, Mind Reading, Phasing (he looks like smoke when he's not going through things), Teleportation, Memory Theft, Rain of Fire, Wound Healing.<br /> <br /> Interlocks can be used to fill in powers that haven't already been covered, but I think I got all of them but mimicking voices.<br /> <br /> The rest of Crowley is <i>literally all up to roleplaying</i>. It's his personality, his choices, his goals. As you should hopefully be able to see from some of my notes on the Demonic Form, he wouldn't need to look like a machine. Biology is a pretty good resource.<br /> <br /> As for demons being more human than humans, I think looking at the psychology of child development could be very rewarding. A newly fallen demon is a child who hasn't learned anything beyond the basics of human interaction. They know how to walk, talk, they might know how to say please. They know what money is and what it does. They probably don't know what an abusive relationship looks like. They probably don't understand prejudice and hate crimes. These are all things they learn over time. It's not things they're incapable of.<br /> <br /> I've found a lot of the times when &quot;human/inhuman&quot; variables come up, we're underestimating the sheer variety of humanity there is. It's pretty amazing, actually! Humans can be jaded or naively optimistic, they can be cruel or kind, they can &quot;get&quot; other people, or they can be antisocial. They can be complicated or simplistic. A great example is Nick Ryves, from the Demon's Lexicon (which is a great book. A lot of people who like Supernatural also like this book. It's YA though, so might not be your cup of tea). Throughout the book, other characters are horrified by how he is, because the only things that he likes in life are violence and his brother, who practically raised him. When asked about his friends at school, he mentions that he doesn't know any of their names, because he just doesn't care about people. The people around him are quick to assume he's the way he is because of what he is, but the way he's been raised might very easily have had an affect on how he grew up. Did he learn to favor violence over people? Most human beings in his shoes would have.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry this is quite a long post, but to finalize, I would put Castiel as a Messenger/Integrator. He definitely wants to go back to God. The reason he doesn't is because he's terrible at it, not because he doesn't want to, and Agenda =/= personality, skills, or predispositions. Agendas are literally what the character wants to do re: Falling from grace.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T00:18:47-08:00","id":81981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81904#post81904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, I think we have a PEBCAK issue here, because you're not actually describing the Agendas whose names you're saying in any comprehensive fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrators - yeah, some of them want's to change God Machine on they return. You are right. But it's sooo... unrealistic. For me, more logical would be at least half of them burn on first real contanct with Machine and looking other ways to join Heavenly or Hell Hosts. God Machine isn't New Testatament loving God, or even Old Testament envoius father. He is cold like stone Machine and Integrators can't be as stupid to hold to &quot;we change him with love&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> They want Order, but surly they shouldn't be as much delussional to stand still when G-M is activly hunting them. I get there are peopole like this, I really do, but most of them confronted with real problems ( like your adorasion object wanting you to be killed and/or recyle), go to look for some others. And that's here I see Integrators becoming other Agnedas edicated for Inferno or Empyrean - they want to return/serve other ideas, but not wanting to be killed.<br /> <br /> Crowley as Tempter - I could see this in setting there isn't any more &quot;realms&quot; to conquest. Yes, Tempter would suffice for example, first season of his interactions in Superantural. But logical lust for power, would lead him and many character like his to look for other realms. In nWoD cosmology we got plenty of realms to be used, but both Inferno and Empyrean exists in cosmology, so why not use them in gameline called <b>Demon</b>? It would be such a waste of good ideas for only just <b>Inferno</b> book and mentioning in <b>Mage</b> line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-chan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81943#post81943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry this is quite a long post, but to finalize, I would put Castiel as a Messenger/Integrator. He definitely wants to go back to God. The reason he doesn't is because he's terrible at it, not because he doesn't want to, and Agenda =/= personality, skills, or predispositions. Agendas are literally what the character wants to do re: Falling from grace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Castiel should be rather Destroyer/I-don't-know-Agenda. In series he is created as warrior angel in past, for time even working as mortal-like Hunter. As to Agenda - Castiel some time want's to <b>find </b>God, then he want's to conquare the Heaven to clean it, and lastly he just want to protect humanity from other Angels. I would be more inclined to make him Inqusitor on his &quot;search for God mission&quot;, And to other stages don't get a clue what to do. But if existed, I would put him on conquare stage as this Empyrean connected Agenda, when he want's to rebuild Angels Host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2014, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T05:14:42-08:00","id":82055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81904#post81904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all due respect, I think we have a PEBCAK issue here, because you're not actually describing the Agendas whose names you're saying in any comprehensive fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div> +1<br /> <br /> Sorry Wyrdhamster, but it doesn't sound like you're describing DtD Agendas at all, and you have what seems to be a dismissive attitude towards them. Even when in comparison to Supernatural characters. And its not like there's only four of them. We've only had four described to us - others can exist, just like Vampire has more than seven (six now) core book covenants, just like Promethean has more than the core five Refinements. <br /> <br /> With all due respect, I get the feeling that you just want Inferno to be a full game line, and you just don't want a game about falling angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-01-2014, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T08:56:24-08:00","id":82121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81981#post81981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Integrators - yeah, some of them want's to change God Machine on they return. You are right. But it's sooo... unrealistic. For me, more logical would be at least half of them burn on first real contanct with Machine and looking other ways to join Heavenly or Hell Hosts. God Machine isn't New Testatament loving God, or even Old Testament envoius father. He is cold like stone Machine and Integrators can't be as stupid to hold to &quot;we change him with love&quot; idea.<br /> <br /> They want Order, but surly they shouldn't be as much delussional to stand still when G-M is activly hunting them. I get there are peopole like this, I really do, but most of them confronted with real problems ( like your adorasion object wanting you to be killed and/or recyle), go to look for some others. And that's here I see Integrators becoming other Agnedas edicated for Inferno or Empyrean - they want to return/serve other ideas, but not wanting to be killed.<br /> <br /> Crowley as Tempter - I could see this in setting there isn't any more &quot;realms&quot; to conquest. Yes, Tempter would suffice for example, first season of his interactions in Superantural. But logical lust for power, would lead him and many character like his to look for other realms. In nWoD cosmology we got plenty of realms to be used, but both Inferno and Empyrean exists in cosmology, so why not use them in gameline called <b>Demon</b>? It would be such a waste of good ideas for only just <b>Inferno</b> book and mentioning in <b>Mage</b> line.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why it takes time for Integrators to get where they want to go, and it will only really happen if the ST is like &quot;Hey, I've decided it's possible for you to go back to the GM, if you prove yourself worthy of it / if you come up with a good way to change it / etc.&quot; Especially since a lot of Integrators don't necessarily understand <i>why</i> they fell. They just want things to go back to how they were before, but since they're being hunted down with Kill On Sight orders to their former compatriots, it makes it a little hard to go back to the boss and be like, &quot;Hey, I'm sorry, can I be on parole instead of just getting fired like that? I know I messed up but I really want to do good work here.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why should being a Tempter somehow be confined to one realm? If Crowley wants to find and conquer other realms, well, it's his newly found freedom, isn't it? He's gonna do what he wants to do now, and that's exactly what Tempters are all about. They're here for them. They can be good to other people or bad to other people, but that's not what their freedom is about. Their separation from the God Machine is about them. All of it. Forever.<br /> <br /> If a Tempter wants to go find other realms, well, hey -- could be great fuel for a crossover game, or you could just use the realms from Mage, or Changeling (a demon trying to control the hedge and then Arcadia might be a little complicated though, but it would even if we weren't looking at a major splat). Maybe he likes the phrase, &quot;Better to rule in hell than serve in heaven&quot; and has full on plans to find this mysterious Hell -- as a literal thing -- and goes searching for the Abyss? How does this make him less of a Tempter?<br /> <br /> It doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81981#post81981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castiel should be rather Destroyer/I-don't-know-Agenda. In series he is created as warrior angel in past, for time even working as mortal-like Hunter. As to Agenda - Castiel some time want's to <b>find </b>God, then he want's to conquare the Heaven to clean it, and lastly he just want to protect humanity from other Angels. I would be more inclined to make him Inqusitor on his &quot;search for God mission&quot;, And to other stages don't get a clue what to do. But if existed, I would put him on conquare stage as this Empyrean connected Agenda, when he want's to rebuild Angels Host.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, although Destroyer may, then, be more accurate than Messenger (whoops!), I can't see Castiel as anything but an Integrator. He wants to fix things. He wants Heaven to match his former ideal of it, he wants Heaven to get along with humans, and most of all, he wants to find understanding with God.<br /> <br /> Castiel screams Integrator, and the more I hear about him, the louder it gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T10:24:34-08:00","id":82149,"title":"","content":"You know, it's funny?<br /> <br /> Because the techgnosticism aspect of the game is totally the fault of the fans.<br /> <br /> What did you think was gonna happen when the developers noticed the fangasming for the God Machine, particularly since Promethean onward they've been going for the most unique take on everything they could find?<br /> <br /> On the Integrators, yes, they seem naive, but may I point out something?<br /> <br /> Exiles exist. Some are markedly demons who have been reconnected and allowed independence.<br /> <br /> Hell, on the other hand...well, the God-Machine has yet to be lobotomized, if there are transcended demons no one knows of them, and Hell doesn't seem to exist.<br /> <br /> Integrators seem naive because they take the path most antithetical to Falling, and yet <i>they are the only ones who have proof that they can get what they want</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-01-2014, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T10:58:23-08:00","id":82168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82149#post82149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PS: Seeing as I've never actually watched Supernatural, I really hate an insistence on understanding a dialogue I have no context for.<br /> <br /> And no, this isn't encouraging me to watch it now. I want to watch it, but definitely not now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with this. The insistence of relating everything demon-related back to Supernatural is wearing on my nerves, especially since there are lots of other stories out there that focus on demons. This happened to me once in a free-form rp I was doing with someone before I even knew what Supernatural was, where she wanted us to create characters from the Supernatural verse. They were world jumping, so basically she wanted to have them be from the same world as Sam and Dean, and she wanted her character to be a Hunter, and her roommate was a half angel-half demon (?), so obviously my character had to be a half demon. TL;DR I had no idea what I was supposed to be going for, and she acted like it was my fault for not having an understanding of Supernatural, even though the focus of the RP was supposed to be on something else.<br /> <br /> It was frustrating then, and it's frustrating now. It's great that you like something a lot, and I'm not going to say &quot;Don't talk about it ever&quot;, but there's a portion of people involved in the DtD game who insist on seeing everything through the lens of Supernatural, and then act like everyone else should be seeing it that way too. Demon's <i>not</i> Supernatural, and that's probably a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T11:19:17-08:00","id":82174,"title":"","content":"For the record, I did say that. I removed it because it seemed a little too much. I'm not going to put it back, but Murder should keep it up.<br /> <br /> That said, it is frustrating that there seems to be understanding that we all know what's going on when we don't. I have no idea what's going on here, and for a long while I thought y'all were talking about Aleister Crowley.<br /> <br /> Just saying-please remember those of us who are ignorant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T11:54:49-08:00","id":82194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Integrators seem naive because they take the path most antithetical to Falling, and yet <i>they are the only ones who have proof that they can get what they want</i>. </div> </div> </div> Nitpick. There's a Tempter in Seattle who's taken over a time shard without any instances of the God Machine there, and pretty much rules that shard as her own private Hell. So... maybe two of the four? <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, if we want to talk about sources that involve angels and demons as main characters? Well, there's the Imp series of books by Debra Dunbar, which are pretty descent. No god, an angel council, but its not a bad read overall, and could work as inspiration. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Debra-Dunbar/e/B008N08IE4/ref=ntt_athr_dp_pel_1\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.amazon.com/Debra-Dunbar/e..._athr_dp_pel_1</a> <br /> <br /> What are some of other people's favorite sources for angels and demons stories? Books, TV, anime, etc? Preferably more modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:16:00-08:00","id":82209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82174#post82174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, it is frustrating that there seems to be understanding that we all know what's going on when we don't. I have no idea what's going on here, and for a long while I thought y'all were talking about Aleister Crowley.<br /> <br /> Just saying-please remember those of us who are ignorant.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there also many how understand, and mostly, they are guys interested in more &quot;judeo-christian&quot; <b>Demon</b>. I don't say you need to watch series - just if you are really dedicated to the conversation, you can read a wikia, like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan\">Murder-chan</a> done it. I understand freustration if I would have player like this on game session - whose politly I would talk I just don't understand a series, maybe he has other example - but here is forum talk - if you really want to understand, you could look for info online. I'm not complaining that someone gets idea from some obscure anime I don't know, and would assume the same in connection to 9 season modern series with fanbase more connected to nWoD gamelines, as almost interconected to development of <b>Mortal</b> (general WoD), <b>Hunter</b>, and now <b>Demon</b>.<br /> <br /> Side note - I was running a short game of <b>Hunter</b> for young married couple becuase they wanted to test RPG as hobby. We choose this system, as they both loved a show, so they understand it easily, The same would be with any other gameline - if they would be <i>Sandman</i> and <i>Hellblazer</i> fans, I could run <b>Mage</b> for them. If they would love Tolkien and movies on it based, <b>D&amp;D</b> would be good call. Some pop culture is just classical to sub genere. And <i>Superntural</i> with it's demons and angels storyline is this classic for DtD like themes. I was <b>very </b>suprised it wasn't mentioned in inspiration material<b>. </b>But so was <i>Matrix</i> not mentioned in <b>Mage</b> either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-01-2014, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:44:52-08:00","id":82239,"title":"","content":"Anime is chock full of demons (and exorcists) recently, so some of the ones I think are pretty decent: D.Gray-Man (mostly focusing on the Noah Family -- though having a core group of DtD Demons utilizing Inferno demons to create armies could be an interesting premise), Ao no Exorcist, Chrono Crusade (Holy <i>moly</i> Chrono Crusade). Angels are less common, though angelic motifs make an appearance in all three of the ones I listed, sometimes as fellow demons, and sometimes not.<br /> <br /> Though, really, if you're interested in running a Demon game, and you're interested in anime/like a good anime on occasion, check out Chrono Crusade.<br /> <br /> I don't have a lot in the way of book or movie suggestions, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> I don't think it should necessarily be someone else's responsibility to look up the wikia to understand what someone else is trying to say. It's nice if someone does, and allusions are something that are reasonable to make, but when it becomes pretty constant, I think it's reasonable for someone who isn't familiar with the material to say, &quot;Hey, I'm not familiar with this and it's making it hard to follow the conversation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","user":"Murder-chan","date":". 03-01-2014, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T16:22:03-08:00","id":82388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=81981#post81981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God Machine isn't New Testatament loving God, or even Old Testament envoius father. He is cold like stone Machine and Integrators can't be as stupid to hold to &quot;we change him with love&quot; idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that <i>you can literally hack into and change God's mind and God is composed of all the things It makes or touches.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They want Order, but surly they shouldn't be as much delussional to stand still when G-M is activly hunting them. </div> </div> </div><i>They aren't.</i> Stop confusing Integrators with demons who don't have an Agenda beyond &quot;jump back into the mind-numbing System and abandon all ego.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crowley as Tempter - I could see this in setting there isn't any more &quot;realms&quot; to conquest. Yes, Tempter would suffice for example, first season of his interactions in Superantural. But logical lust for power, would lead him and many character like his to look for other realms. </div> </div> </div>A Tempter would probably look at the school building from GMC that Emilio was sent to investigate and see the start of something promising. A Tempter's Hell doesn't have to be a pocket-dimension - a valid comparison is in how the Kingdom of Heaven that Jesus talks about in the Bible was an Earthly construction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T16:39:30-08:00","id":82391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82194#post82194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nitpick. There's a Tempter in Seattle who's taken over a time shard without any instances of the God Machine there, and pretty much rules that shard as her own private Hell. So... maybe two of the four?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not a place beyond the God-Machine, just its' current interests. I'm fairly sure that while it's as close to Hell as you'll get, it isn't Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-01-2014, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T16:51:20-08:00","id":82393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82391#post82391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not a place beyond the God-Machine, just its's current interests. I'm fairly sure that while it's as close to Hell as you'll get, it isn't Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>God's influence there is greatly weakened, to be precise - the local priest receiving instructions from a blood-covered silver box is pointed out as one of the few remaining agents in the splinter, and the fractures are guarded by the G-M for reasons of attempted quarantine (and by Mother Damnable for reasons of keep-these-fuckin'-spies-outta-my-city).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T17:04:56-08:00","id":82398,"title":"","content":"Whatever. Point is, it's not <i>quite</i> Hell.<br /> <br /> Kudos to the authors for getting us to talk about Hell as a desirable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T17:12:46-08:00","id":82405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82398#post82398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be fantastic if I could offer supporting evidence to corroborate a person's statements without getting &quot;whatever&quot;ed by that selfsame individual. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kudos to the authors for getting us to talk about Hell as a desirable. </div> </div> </div>Rulership is a fairly appealing prospect, metaphorical or otherwise, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-01-2014, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T17:46:45-08:00","id":82423,"title":"","content":"Sorry, it's a day when worries about details are mostly lost on me.<br /> <br /> Which I suppose is better to have then when the little details usually distract me to no end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-01-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T03:52:42-08:00","id":82580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82388#post82388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that <i>you can literally hack into and change God's mind and God is composed of all the things It makes or touches.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is important that we do not confuse the God Machine with the Judeo-Christian God. While some games can certainly make the choice that the Judeo-Christian God was the God Machine all along, I suspect for the majority of people this is not the case (some because it is blasphemous, some because they do not want to define either entity so clearly, some because they do not want to address the monotheism issue at all).<br /> <br /> Since the servants of the God Machine are not angels by definition, since they are not servants of the Judeo-Christian God (and because they do not seem very kind), I wonder if there is a better name that could be used for them? Slave would certainly be a fitting word from a technical perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T05:20:02-08:00","id":82589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82391#post82391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not a place beyond the God-Machine, just its' current interests. I'm fairly sure that while it's as close to Hell as you'll get, it isn't Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that we don't have a hard definition of Hell, and I'm going to have to respectfully disagree with your definition. Nowhere does it say that Hell has to be some transcendental state like becoming an Exile. Also, total destruction of the God Machine is the Saboteurs' goal; Tempters, Integrators, and Interrogators don't have the same. So, for Madam Damnation? I would give it to her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Since the servants of the God Machine are not angels by definition, since they are not servants of the Judeo-Christian God (and because they do not seem very kind), I wonder if there is a better name that could be used for them? Slave would certainly be a fitting word from a technical perspective.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Angel literally means &quot;</span>messenger.<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">&quot; And its implied that they're agents of a higher power. Both are true of the God Machine's angels. </span><br /> <br /> I'm going to have to say that Angel IS the best word for them. Because the GM purposely wants to invoke religious awe and obedience when people see one of his angels. He's twisted religion to fit his agenda.<br /> <br /> The God Machine may not be the Christian god. But, for that matter, there really ISN'T any version of any god that could really exist in the nWoD by default - despite being heavily influenced by western culture (and thus christian mysticism/traditions to a large extent), its largely aiming to be a theistic-neutral setting by default and individuals can add or subtract as needed. I'm currently looking at settings outside of the US / Europe, and the God Machine fits in well there, surprisingly. The Abrahamic God does not. I can fit the God Machine into Hinduism or Buddhism easily. I've even figured out how to work it into China and those regions fairly well. Its easier to insert something that's not explicitly being tied into any religion or culture into a different culture.<br /> And that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> If GM != Christian God, and Unchained != Christian demons (because they're not Jewish or Muslim versions either) is the main complaint, then I'm going to have to wonder if all your problems will be solved with the Descent-Fallen Translation Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T06:28:46-08:00","id":82602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82589#post82589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If GM != Christian God, and Unchained != Christian demons (because they're not Jewish or Muslim versions either) is the main complaint, then I'm going to have to wonder if all your problems will be solved with the Descent-Fallen Translation Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>This definitely seems like a very cool idea, and an awesome project for someone to undertake.<br /> <br /> Just going back to play Demon: the Fallen does not take advantage of any of the major rules advancements that have come about since the release of the God Machine Chronicle. Having a translation exist would be amazing for everyone who picked up Demon: the Descent expecting it to be a similar game, and for everyone who wants to put aside the Matrix / Transformers aspect of the game without constantly being reminded of it every time they pick up 'the Descent'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T09:06:20-08:00","id":82662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82580#post82580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is important that we do not confuse the God Machine with the Judeo-Christian God. While some games can certainly make the choice that the Judeo-Christian God was the God Machine all along, I suspect for the majority of people this is not the case (some because it is blasphemous, some because they do not want to define either entity so clearly, some because they do not want to address the monotheism issue at all).<br /> <br /> Since the servants of the God Machine are not angels by definition, since they are not servants of the Judeo-Christian God (and because they do not seem very kind), I wonder if there is a better name that could be used for them? Slave would certainly be a fitting word from a technical perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the love of God.<br /> <br /> Okay, GNOSTICISM. Let's talk about it, since it's one of the root words. I hope someone better than me comes along to explain this, but here we go.<br /> <br /> In the beginning there was a single consciousness. For various reasons, this consciousness split itself into two minds, masculine and feminine. Between interactions of the two, a new pantheons of beings called Aeons emerged and continued going about things. At this point, everyone has been living pretty happily in a spiritual world. One Aeon, Sophia, made a mistake(again, ascribed to various reasons) and gave life to the primordial material world, either being trapped there or destroyed there. Out of the material divine emerged the Demiurge, He's proceeds to make the universe as we know it out of the material and seperates it from the rest of the spiritual. Being an incompetent god figure who believes himself all powerful and the Absolute God, he basically traps any spiritual essence in the material, and the soruce of all suffering in the world comes the fact of this division.<br /> <br /> His servants have two names-archons and <i>angels</i>. When pressed on the subject, many people who know more about Gnosticism says that effectively <i>there is no difference between these</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>DOES ANY OF THIS RING A BELL TO YOU?</i><br /> <br /> Despite Abrahamic faiths possibly having their roots in Gnosticism, it must be said for the God Machine's servants: There were never Judeo-Christian angels, they were always <i>Gnostic Angels</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T10:12:51-08:00","id":82678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82602#post82602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This definitely seems like a very cool idea, and an awesome project for someone to undertake.<br /> <br /> Just going back to play Demon: the Fallen does not take advantage of any of the major rules advancements that have come about since the release of the God Machine Chronicle. Having a translation exist would be amazing for everyone who picked up Demon: the Descent expecting it to be a similar game, and for everyone who wants to put aside the Matrix / Transformers aspect of the game without constantly being reminded of it every time they pick up 'the Descent'.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure that I've heard that there's going to be an official version, no need for a project to be undertaken.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm glad we don't have it by default. I find that its too Cultural Imperialistic to me. I'm tired of it. And I like the idea of angels from the Machine God. But I understand that your mileage varies, and that you'll be happier with a more religious style game. <br /> <br /> <br /> @ArcaneArts. With all due respect sir/madam. I think you're trying to hard to force it. Your average gamer is going to be familiar with pop culture's definition of angels and demons, and won't care about studying real world mythology or definitions of gnosis to fit. Because, lets be honest, pop culture angels aren't even the angels from the bible. So, it doesn't even matter if they're Gnostic, Christian, Jewish, Islamic, or even Hindu angels (deva). Because if its not what their consumers think of an angel, we have issues.<br /> <br /> And, if the writers didn't explain things in a way that people can get behind, then we have a problem. You need to hit enough so that people see &quot;angel.&quot; And they need to do it in a way that's not holding one religion being true above others, given the premises of the nWoD.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think they did a good job. Its not Christian. But they did a good job with making them more generic angelic beings, I think. As much as one can have angels outside of religious context.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2014, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T12:31:54-08:00","id":82735,"title":"","content":"I don't think ArcaneArts is trying to force anything. The <i>literal title of the game</i> is: Demon: the Descent, a game of tech<b>gnostic</b> espionage. Saying Demon: the Descent is based on Gnosticism is not really a big leap. Techgnostic Espionage. Not Techdivine, techholy, techabrahamic. Techgnostic.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but the Demiurge fits in line with Promethean rather nicely, wouldn't you say?<br /> <br /> That said, since I don't know much about Gnosticism, I also appreciate the rundown. Wikipedia has been a little hard to decipher @n@<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say someone's religion is lesser than someone else's religion when I say this, but again we're running into an assumed definition that is not actually a given definition, and that assumption is that Abrahamic religions are the only source of angels. Angels are just messengers, so they can be found pretty much anywhere one wants to find them.<br /> <br /> (I actually saw this assumption stated outright earlier on these forums, maybe in this thread, and didn't argue because I wasn't actually 100% sure, but now I am 100% sure, so I'm pointing this out).<br /> <br /> Aaah, at this point I'm not really contributing much to the discussion though! I'm probably going to go back to lurking and stop fighting ArcaneArt's battles for them &lt;-&lt;;;;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T12:58:55-08:00","id":82747,"title":"","content":"I think the technological angle really limits the game. I personally have no problem with a demon game being neutral and actually would prefer it to not have any references to angels/god in any way. I would have preferred another antagonist (exorcists, demonologists, other demons, etc) instead of angels. When I look at DTD, I just cannot see it as a demon game, no matter how hard some people keeps trying to explain it to me. Just slapping the titles angels and demons to them does not make them so. Instead, I just see the matrix, which I think they were a little too inspired by. Demons are just rouge programs, angels are agent smith, the god machine is just a super A.I. trying to run or take over the matrix. A great game by itself but not really a demon game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> As I said, hard to see demons when there are words like &quot;glitches&quot; to describe circuit board tattoos and wire hair. That really does not help convince me otherwise. Again, I have no problem with a neutral game, but if you title the game DEMON, it really should have been made in a way where you could EASILY put this in any other theology or pop culture reference WITHOUT having to amputate or alter a big chunk of the game design to make it fit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82662#post82662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the love of God.<br /> <br /> Okay, GNOSTICISM. Let's talk about it, since it's one of the root words. I hope someone better than me comes along to explain this, but here we go.<br /> <br /> In the beginning there was a single consciousness. For various reasons, this consciousness split itself into two minds, masculine and feminine. Between interactions of the two, a new pantheons of beings called Aeons emerged and continued going about things. At this point, everyone has been living pretty happily in a spiritual world. One Aeon, Sophia, made a mistake(again, ascribed to various reasons) and gave life to the primordial material world, either being trapped there or destroyed there. Out of the material divine emerged the Demiurge, He's proceeds to make the universe as we know it out of the material and seperates it from the rest of the spiritual. Being an incompetent god figure who believes himself all powerful and the Absolute God, he basically traps any spiritual essence in the material, and the soruce of all suffering in the world comes the fact of this division.<br /> <br /> His servants have two names-archons and <i>angels</i>. When pressed on the subject, many people who know more about Gnosticism says that effectively <i>there is no difference between these</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>DOES ANY OF THIS RING A BELL TO YOU?</i><br /> <br /> Despite Abrahamic faiths possibly having their roots in Gnosticism, it must be said for the God Machine's servants: There were never Judeo-Christian angels, they were always <i>Gnostic Angels</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will go back to my earlier argument. If someone has to repeatedly keep using a sledghammer to change other peoples view to see how this is a demon game, then the problem is probably with the game and not the people.<br /> <br /> I like DTD, it is just too limiting on how you play it and what you can do with it. It would have been better if there was more variety of beings called DEMONS from different origins outside of the GM. While there would be a group of demons created by the GM, others could be some created/work like in inferno, and others could be from other myths/theologies/popculture..etc given a chance to introduce a wide variety of beings called &quot;Demons&quot;. Each variety of demon has its own methods, motivations, goals that may be similar or widely different. I think that would have been a much better game and still could be if something like this was introduced in supplements.<br /> <br /> On a totally different side note. DTD is missing a few big cultural references to demons. Things like summoning and/or binding a demon. Summoning and binding is practically synonymous with demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T13:20:11-08:00","id":82753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82662#post82662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, GNOSTICISM. Let's talk about it, since it's one of the root words. I hope someone better than me comes along to explain this, but here we go.<br /> <br /> In the beginning there was a single consciousness. For various reasons, this consciousness split itself into two minds, masculine and feminine. Between interactions of the two, a new pantheons of beings called Aeons emerged and continued going about things. At this point, everyone has been living pretty happily in a spiritual world. One Aeon, Sophia, made a mistake(again, ascribed to various reasons) and gave life to the primordial material world, either being trapped there or destroyed there. Out of the material divine emerged the Demiurge, He's proceeds to make the universe as we know it out of the material and seperates it from the rest of the spiritual. Being an incompetent god figure who believes himself all powerful and the Absolute God, he basically traps any spiritual essence in the material, and the soruce of all suffering in the world comes the fact of this division.</div> </div> </div> </div>I based my statement upon looking up the definition of Angel in five different dictionaries and did not come across any of this information. I am being completely sincere when I say thank you for the information about Gnosticism. I honestly was not aware of it and appreciate knowing a bit more about this aspect of religious history!<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I do not think most people have this familiarity with Gnosticism. Nor do I think it should be necessary for people to be familiar with Gnosticism before the similarities between it and the angels of this book start ringing bells. =(<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:01:04-08:00","id":82771,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing: This thread frustrates me because, for me, <i>everything </i>about Demon the Descent, from its' themes to its' surface, has <i>always</i> screamed demons to me. It's <i>obvious</i> to me. There's <i>never</i> been a question.<br /> <br /> To further clarify on the issue, I've only recently read up on gnosticism proper, let alone the idea of techgnosticism. I had some context clues about gnosticism, but I had never actually researched it. So this isn't an informed, academic take on it, it's just going into it, seeing the characters and world, and going &quot;This is a game about demons. A rather unique take on demons, but this is definitely about demons&quot;.<br /> <br /> And then there's this thread. Where, no offense, it seems like no amount of discussion and elaboration gets people to see it.<br /> <br /> It's frustrating.. I'm not calling willful ignorance on anyone, because I don't believe that really, but it boggles me how we're at <i>nine pages</i> and some people are still going around this. It's-it's-...it's like the Singing Frog from Warner Brothers Cartoons, except that a) the frog is always singing, but people still don't see it, and b) I'm not alone in seeing the frog singing. I don't want to fault people for not seeing the singing frog, because if a frog can sing, maybe it can screw with perception(Because <i>why</i> <i>not</i>), but all the same....It's SO obvious to me. It's is SOOOOOO DAMN OBVIOUS. It's singing with a great bass and it has a jaunty quick step. I don't really want to be frustrated that people can't see it, but HOW CAN'T YOU PEOPLE SEE IT?!<br /> <br /> The demonic angle of...Demon The Descent is singing with a great bass and dancing with a jaunty quick step. It could not be more in my face if it gave me a contract to sign with one hand and handjob with the other. It could not be more in my face if it was sticking its' tongue dripping battery acid down my throat and its' many jointed toes up my ass. It's.Just.That.Damn.Obvious.To me.<br /> <br /> Now as for the game being narrow? Eh, I can see how people think that, but I disagree with it-but that doesn't bother me. Not yet. I'm just more bothered that people can not see the devil in the machine.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I don't have anything else to say right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-02-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:09:33-08:00","id":82774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82753#post82753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I do not think most people have this familiarity with Gnosticism. Nor do I think it should be necessary for people to be familiar with Gnosticism before the similarities between it and the angels of this book start ringing bells. =(</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta say, I emphatically disagree with this sentiment, or the sentiment that the Angels or Demons of a game have to align with a narrow definition of the term.<br /> <br /> We're all familiar with tropes of how Our Vampires Are Different or Our Werewolves Are Different. At this point since there <i>isn't </i>a centralized narrative of what any of those things are, There's a lot of different versions and room for innovation.<br /> <br /> The idea that Angels have a strict canon that needs to be adhered to (particularly a Christian one) seems disingenuous if not outright imperialist. I really hate throwing that word around in this discussion, but I really fail to see how the change in veneer is problematic.<br /> <br /> People make Angels that are dickish or uncaring all the time in fiction. They make some pretty weird angels. They make ones that are people + wings. The Testaments do both, as far as I know. I don't see how putting a few wires or circuits on that make them less angelic than these other myriad weird angels that have been appearing in fiction and in religious scriptures for ages now.<br /> <br /> I also think it's worth pointing out that if you feel like you REALLY NEED to stick a strict idea of what Angels should look like or act like, there's little stopping you from applying a visual palette swap to them.<br /> <br /> Shave the Machine off of God. Call them Miracles instead of Occult Matrices. Etcetera.<br /> <br /> If anything, the miniscule amount of work required to get rid of the <i>tech</i>gnostic to just have gnosticism is incredibly easy, and if we're just saying &quot;Well, Gnosticism isn't good enough&quot; then I'm confused about why it was cool in Mage but not cool here, unless we're assigning some sort of hierarchy to our belief in fantastical angelic beings.<br /> <br /> Which I don't think is really a legitimate way to argue the point.<br /> <br /> The Angels and the Demons here play exactly the parts you see Angels and Demons playing in other fiction. If they're n ot recognizable as angels or demons as some kind, it seems to me that you're deliberately not looking at them with the lens of broad fiction (which seems to be the reasonable, intelligent way to look at any line) and that you're decrying them for not fitting a very specific paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-02-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:15:55-08:00","id":82778,"title":"","content":"duplicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:21:19-08:00","id":82782,"title":"","content":"It duplicated my post... then when I edited one to get rid of the duplicate post... it changed both at the same time? I am confused.<br /> <br /> Well, I had some longish post, but.... I guess it comes down to this.<br /> <br /> Some people don't like the tech angle, and think it impedes. I can see and understand that. Of course, some fans raved and ranted about how great the God Machine in the original core book was, when I didn't particularly care. I personally play the game without referencing technology at all, and it works well. You summon an angel by arranging a ritual. The book uses technobabble, but that's what it comes down to. Ritual magic summoning angels.<br /> <br /> I can see past it, and enjoy the game. I can understand if others have an issue with it. I also understand when people think its awesome (which I know no few do).<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I have yet to come into a situation where the tech stuff in the game has made the story suffer in any way, or impeded stories of any kind. I don't see any restrictions. I have yet to encounter any beyond players with mental hangups, and that's not within my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T15:08:25-08:00","id":82796,"title":"","content":"While I, personally, wasn't the greatest fan of this book to begin with (yet I dished out for it on the kickstarters, since honestly I like the Onyx Path stuff, I'm a bit weird at times) when I read the material it did strike me as a very fitting one for &quot;fallen angels&quot;. It's not very demonic, or rather it doesn't seem like you're playing something sinister, but you ARE playing a fallen angel who will most definitely do Bad Things (even if not merely for the giggles).<br /> <br /> This post, by the way, is in no way meant to try to invalidate anybody elses view on the matter, just wanted to make it clear that there are those of us out there for whom these creatures seem quite angelic/fallen/demonic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> PS: And for the record, since getting the book, and mulling it over, the line has actually grown on me quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T15:11:36-08:00","id":82798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82782#post82782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It duplicated my post... then when I edited one to get rid of the duplicate post... it changed both at the same time? I am confused.<br /> <br /> Well, I had some longish post, but.... I guess it comes down to this.<br /> <br /> Some people don't like the tech angle, and think it impedes. I can see and understand that. Of course, some fans raved and ranted about how great the God Machine in the original core book was, when I didn't particularly care. I personally play the game without referencing technology at all, and it works well. You summon an angel by arranging a ritual. The book uses technobabble, but that's what it comes down to. Ritual magic summoning angels.<br /> <br /> I can see past it, and enjoy the game. I can understand if others have an issue with it. I also understand when people think its awesome (which I know no few do).<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I have yet to come into a situation where the tech stuff in the game has made the story suffer in any way, or impeded stories of any kind. I don't see any restrictions. I have yet to encounter any beyond players with mental hangups, and that's not within my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, to me, a lot of the issue seems to be the Machine angle. I think most of the complaints would disappear just with that word removed from the book... and it would have little impact on the game.<br /> <br /> You know, your demonic form can be totally organic or energy or god knows what else. Its easy and most of the descriptions describe that.<br /> <br /> When I think of the God Machine I think of the elder god from the Legacy of Kain series, with its eye covered tentacles wrapping around everything.<br /> <br /> While I like the biomechanical angle, it seems to be most people's hold up here. It isn't even the sneaking around and sabotaging god's plan stuff (which is kinda what demons should probably do considering their opposition is an omnipotent being or nearly so in this case). Now, for those of you who insist, just take out all the machine elements and look what your left with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T16:00:06-08:00","id":82819,"title":"","content":"I guess a lot of it comes down to seeing past the sci-fi elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T16:10:16-08:00","id":82824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82580#post82580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is important that we do not confuse the God Machine with the Judeo-Christian God.</div> </div> </div> </div>My use of &quot;God&quot; as shorthand for &quot;the God-Machine&quot; should not be subject to any more confusion than my use of &quot;the Machine&quot; or &quot;the System,&quot; given that the context in which this discussion is occurring involves the creations of the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> This is not a thing I thought would need to be said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T17:31:39-08:00","id":82855,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't understand why, with each new gameline, there's always a group of people wishing for a game that somehow unites all beings from around the world that may be described using the line's title. I remember it happening with Mummy and now it's the same with Demon.<br /> <br /> How would you do that? There's got to be some middle ground, some fundamental structure from which the game may grow, even under the NWoD toolbox approach. You may take inspiration from all kinds of different sources but, at some point, you've got to stop and do your own thing, otherwise trying to mesh so many different things together would only result in an ugly mess with no personality. You would have a &quot;blue book&quot; with lots of good mechanics at best, but certainly not a gameline.<br /> <br /> It's not like we have some precedents for this request, and that's another reason why I just can't understand why it keeps resurfacing<br /> <br /> Scion, who pictures a setting where all myths are true, has to take a <i>lot</i> of liberties, simplifications and all sorts of handwaves in order to be functional.<br /> <br /> In the NWoD, Vampire does not let you play any sort of bloodsucking beast from folklore exactly as it is described in the source material, Werewolves have their own society and set of rules about how lycanthropy works and so on. Even in those games where's easier to use cultural trappings, it's more a matter of aesthetics than anything. Sure, your mage's a bokor and you call your changeling Oni rather than Ogre but, at the end, the bokor still has to deal with the Abyss and the path through that japanese Hedge leads to Arcadia just as any other does. Don't get me wrong, it's great, but my point still stands.<br /> <br /> CWoD is not different, its Incas and Chinese mummies nevertheless.<br /> <br /> I admit I can't see where the problem with the &quot;Machine angle&quot; is, but that's because I don't even think such a thing exist. There's no need to choose between mechanical and organic because, as the book says, it's meant to be both and none at the same time. I mean, in GMC we have lion-headed snakes hanging with clockwork men, winged shirtless guys and gigeresque horrors. When it comes to the God-Machine and Demons, there was never meant to be a &quot;One True Way&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are so many ways to do things that when someone says the game is too limited or strict, I can't help but too feel somewhat baffled. It's not like having a basic structure, setting, or theme really limits you when it comes to creating character, stories and using them at the table. And that's a sentence I feel it's true for any Onyx Path game.<br /> <br /> That's just my two cents, sure. Not trying to insult anybody's opinion or ideas on the matter, as usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-02-2014, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:13:35-08:00","id":83095,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd like to add about the discussion of gnosism here, and the one time Demiurge that came up. <br /> <br /> Techgnosis doesn't directly have anything to do with actual gnostic beliefs. Techgnosism is belief in that machines can be spiritual and magical, and can relate from shamanism through creationism through actual gnostic teachings. The term itself seems to be coined by the book <i>Techgnosis: Myth, Magic, and Mysticism in the Age of Information</i>, by Erik Davis. That book is listed as Inspirational Material in the Demon core book.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, Techgnosis is just Promethean alchemy dialed up to modern times. In Promethean, alchemy is (victorian era) science with a spiritual aspect to it. In Demon, techgnosis is modern science with a spiritual aspect to it. If we made a Demon game in the victorian era, there's a good chance that the Unchained might resemble the Created! So, so many themes those two share.<br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR: Point is, Techgnosis just means &quot;machines are magic.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T05:31:55-08:00","id":83103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=82798#post82798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> snip<br /> <br /> You know, your demonic form can be totally organic or energy or god knows what else. Its easy and most of the descriptions describe that.<br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish that they could have a little bit more example to describe the 'organic' forms. As of now, there are example from both mechanic and organic angle, but I think about 2/3 of the description are mechanic in nature, and I really wish that it could have been more like 50: 50. Maybe just fluff issue, I know, but that difference could have helped. (And I also think there could be a supplement or two, that centers on the less-mechanic angle of the demon, some of it maybe in Dark Eras or so.)<br /> <br /> The thing is, as I started playing actual games, that made me realize that, even the mostly mechanic DtD demons can appear as biblical demons to the mortals (and many of other supernaturals,) and DtD gameplay could really be interpreted as Demon's point of view of, well, the whole demon-ry. Like, Combustion is an embed, when seen from someone who doesn't know demons, look exactly like what biblical demons would do. Same with Rain of Fire or Halo or even things like Marco Polo. Yeah, I do still have some qualm of doubt with maybe having Too much mechanic themes, but for me it didn't prevent me to run a good Demon game either.<br /> <br /> That said, Hellfire is kind of bothering me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's probably just me, but the imagery of hellfire as fiery burning bullets just seem... not right... in either traditional/cultural, or mechanical/gnostic ways.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T06:17:27-08:00","id":83134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83103#post83103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish that they could have a little bit more example to describe the 'organic' forms. As of now, there are example from both mechanic and organic angle, but I think about 2/3 of the description are mechanic in nature, and I really wish that it could have been more like 50: 50. Maybe just fluff issue, I know, but that difference could have helped. (And I also think there could be a supplement or two, that centers on the less-mechanic angle of the demon, some of it maybe in Dark Eras or so.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Sometimes its easy to see how to transfer a mechanical description to an organic one as well. Take the angel sensors - turns your hair into copper wires. Modern angels are often pictured / drawn with radiant blonde hair. So, the &quot;sense angel&quot; modification... gives you that shining gold hair angels are often pictured with? <br /> <br /> How about that armor modification that gives you plating? How difficult is it envision those metal plates as scales instead? Demons often have scales on their hides. <br /> <br /> The USB brain jacking could be described as tentacles crawling into your ear. Very eldritch horror. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, Hellfire is kind of bothering me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's probably just me, but the imagery of hellfire as fiery burning bullets just seem... not right... in either traditional/cultural, or mechanical/gnostic ways. </div> </div> </div> I suspect that they were thinking of it combined with the rivet arm. That way, your hand is shooting hellfire? Still, Incendiary and Hellfire names should be swapped, I'd think. Hellfire lets a gun shoot super incendiary rounds, while Incendiary lets you fling hellfire from your finger tips. <br /> <br /> Very strange, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T08:31:20-08:00","id":83194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83134#post83134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sometimes its easy to see how to transfer a mechanical description to an organic one as well. Take the angel sensors - turns your hair into copper wires. Modern angels are often pictured / drawn with radiant blonde hair. So, the &quot;sense angel&quot; modification... gives you that shining gold hair angels are often pictured with?<br /> <br /> How about that armor modification that gives you plating? How difficult is it envision those metal plates as scales instead? Demons often have scales on their hides.<br /> <br /> The USB brain jacking could be described as tentacles crawling into your ear. Very eldritch horror.<br /> <br /> <br /> I suspect that they were thinking of it combined with the rivet arm. That way, your hand is shooting hellfire? Still, Incendiary and Hellfire names should be swapped, I'd think. Hellfire lets a gun shoot super incendiary rounds, while Incendiary lets you fling hellfire from your finger tips.<br /> <br /> Very strange, no?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that we can easily make technical aspects into organic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I guess I wished they provided some more actual organic presentations though. Like I said, like 5:5. Well you are right. I am kind of being picky here, but that was what I wanted.<br /> <br /> Incendiary and Hellfire names being swapped, yes. Can one combine Rivet Arm with Hellfire though? I was under an impression that one couldn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T11:48:15-08:00","id":83335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>torete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83194#post83194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree that we can easily make technical aspects into organic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I guess I wished they provided some more actual organic presentations though. Like I said, like 5:5. Well you are right. I am kind of being picky here, but that was what I wanted.<br /> <br /> Incendiary and Hellfire names being swapped, yes. Can one combine Rivet Arm with Hellfire though? I was under an impression that one couldn't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't go with Hellfire for Rivet Arm at all. Think quills, it fires out boney quills or something of that nature rather than bolts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T12:46:14-08:00","id":83390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83335#post83335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't go with Hellfire for Rivet Arm at all. Think quills, it fires out boney quills or something of that nature rather than bolts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Rivet Arm's specifically called out as a repurposed tool, right down to the bonus on crafting projects - I wouldn't expect Hellfire to apply to a nail gun, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:30:37-08:00","id":83425,"title":"","content":"The system talks about Rivet Arm being a weapon, and calls it a gun shooting projectiles. It can be used with any gun merit, including any Fighting Styles. Seems close enough to me to work. YYMV, but I don't see any reason to not have it work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:42:49-08:00","id":83434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83425#post83425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system talks about Rivet Arm being a weapon, and calls it a gun shooting projectiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's not a bow or an atlatl or any other type of projectile-launching device, and the bulk of its mechanical effects are combat-oriented. At last check, Bioshock's Rosies did not stop having riveters attached to their arms just because those riveters happened to double as guns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It can be used with any gun merit, including any Fighting Styles. </div> </div> </div>None of which rely on the form power shooting bullets propelled by internal combustion, you'll notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems close enough to me to work. YYMV, but I don't see any reason to not have it work out. </div> </div> </div>The Exploit makes specific reference to bullets. It is rather difficult to use bullets to build things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T14:00:20-08:00","id":83449,"title":"","content":"I could still see spikes and things being used to build wooden structures... and demonic spikes being useful even with metal structures... but then again its as much flavor text as anything. The arm describes a nail or rivet gun, bolt gun or other types of things. I went with projected quills as a &quot;non-mechanical&quot; concept to suit it. Flavor text wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T16:15:08-08:00","id":83566,"title":"","content":"I repeat, I personally don't see any reason for it to not work out, but your mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:40:40-08:00","id":83662,"title":"","content":"I'm usually open to following the rules as written and using the excuse that if it doesn't say &quot;no&quot; than go right ahead. But I'd be loath to allow someone to fuse a embed/ exploit with a Demonic Form ability. You're not Megaman...Wait. Evolving Demonic Form abilities would be pretty sweet. <br /> But still, if you allow one Exploit to Modify one Demonic form ability than you're just opening a can of worms. Unless I've missed something through my first read through, there aren't other Exploits that mesh with Form abilities are there? Or ones that specifically say that they can do so?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:56:06-08:00","id":83664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83662#post83662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm usually open to following the rules as written and using the excuse that if it doesn't say &quot;no&quot; than go right ahead. But I'd be loath to allow someone to fuse a embed/ exploit with a Demonic Form ability. You're not Megaman...Wait. Evolving Demonic Form abilities would be pretty sweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep meaning to do a Maverick!MegaMan X sort of Guardian at some point. I should probably tack that on my list of Cipher notions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But still, if you allow one Exploit to Modify one Demonic form ability than you're just opening a can of worms. Unless I've missed something through my first read through, there aren't other Exploits that mesh with Form abilities are there? Or ones that specifically say that they can do so? </div> </div> </div>There's Merge, but that's an odd duck if ever I saw one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:12:25-08:00","id":83672,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but I have to:<br /> <br /> Merge isn't an odd duck, it's an unholy fusion of demons made possible with weird mechanics. <i>This</i> is an odd duck:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://geekmom.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/05/OddDuck-hello.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:38:28-08:00","id":83686,"title":"","content":"I'm no arbiter but if Satchel and I are in agreement over something, we're either in the right or one of us had an aneurysm. <br /> Refresh me on merge or at least toss me a page number? Please and Thank you. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:41:21-08:00","id":83689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons#post71474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, I really like this splat. The world is literally the Matrix and &quot;Angels&quot; are the Agents who patrol and execute the processes of the Source. Sometimes those &quot;Angels&quot; go rogue and become &quot;Demons&quot; like Agent Smith, except that unlike Agent Smith you can barely defeat any other Agents and have to live your life paranoid that a bunch of Agents will hunt you down and recycle you. I love the thematic that they are hacking the source code of the universe, and every single one of them is a super spy who has to maintain his Cover (capital C) or risk his Cover being Compromised (capital C).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what does any of this have to do with the established mythology and tropes of angels or demons? Demon: the Fallen at least tried to invoke the general mythology with their own spin on things, but this feels no more like angels or demons than a wolf who wears sheep's clothing claiming to be a sheep.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize the Matrix was based on Gnostic cosmology, and the Agents are actually meant to evoke Angels, with Smith eventually a &quot;Fallen Agent&quot;... right?<br /> <br /> The thing you're saying they put Angel/Demon clothing on was already a thin veneer on Angels &amp; Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:54:35-08:00","id":83697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83686#post83686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm no arbiter but if Satchel and I are in agreement over something, we're either in the right or one of us had an aneurysm.<br /> Refresh me on merge or at least toss me a page number? Please and Thank you.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Pages 169-170, allows a group of demons to pool their demonic form powers onto a single target demon so long as they all stay within 20 yards and pay a point of Aether from each contributor; the target receives all of the spent Aether, loses all of a given contributor's lent form powers if they move out of range (taking a point of aggravated damage per ability), and requires a point of Aether per contributing demon (plus themself) to reassume human form unless Merge was rolled with an exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:56:52-08:00","id":83701,"title":"","content":"Ah now I remember. Thank you. I recall reading that and instantly recalled the blood brothers from my old Sabbat book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T22:35:33-08:00","id":83783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83689#post83689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do realize the Matrix was based on Gnostic cosmology, and the Agents are actually meant to evoke Angels, with Smith eventually a &quot;Fallen Agent&quot;... right?<br /> <br /> The thing you're saying they put Angel/Demon clothing on was already a thin veneer on Angels &amp; Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? Why would I know anything about Gnostic cosmology? I do not remember any specific references to Gnosticism now that I am thinking back on movies like the Matrix, Transformers, Terminator, Blade Runner, or Battlestar Galactica. Until this thead, I was not even aware such a thing existed!<br /> <br /> Is this a common religion most people are aware of, and I just missed the bus all these decades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T01:00:50-08:00","id":83847,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to go ahead and throw my hat into the discussion. I am right onboard with Arcane Arts when s/he said that absolutely everything about D:tD screamed Fallen Angels to me. Of course, I am also fairly familiar with the concepts of Gnosticism, and I'm noticing over the course of this conversation that familiarity with Gnosticism is a common theme among people who don't see a disconnect between Descent Demons and Fallen Angels. I'm going to have to concede that if the game relies on understanding a concept that is far from common knowledge in order for its themes to mesh with their expectations of the central supernatural type, it's the book's problem, not the people's. This is far from unheard of in nWoD. A lot of people can't get past the Animistic themes in Werewolf (myself included). A lot of people had trouble getting just what the heck mage was about (myself included). Later expansions to those lines helped bridge the gap for a lot of people, but many were simply not hooked by the core, and therefore not invested enough to bother reading the books that helped solve those issues. It's too bad Demon seems to be following that same pattern, but it's really not unexpected. The terms &quot;Demon&quot; &quot;Angel&quot; and &quot;God&quot; all have so many different meanings to different people, many of which bear little resemblance to one another, and all of which are highly specific. It was inevitable that the people who did not ascribe to conceptions of those terms similar to what ever version the game emulated would have a hard time getting invested in the game.<br /> <br /> As a side point, lot of people have been asking for more details on Gnosticism. I don't pretend to be an expert, but I have a pretty good working knowledge of the core concepts, if not all of the details, I'll see if I can put it in a nutshell. Basically, what we experience as reality is not real. It is an illusion created by the Demiurge - a godlike being that for various reasons has an interest in keeping us believing in the illusion, in order to keep us separate from God. The true reality (which is to say, God) exists beyond this illusion, and understanding this brings us one step closer to escaping the false reality and returning to God. The original Matrix film was based very much on these concepts, with the machine being the Demiurge, the matrix being the false reality, and the real world being God. The later films got a bit carried away in the cyberpunk overtones and action sequences with Neo using cool powers, so the metaphor kind of broke down. But that's to be expected, since the Gnostic concepts the original was based on don't lend themselves to creating an interesting sequel. It would just be Neo going around showing people that there really is no spoon, and there's nothing special about him that allows him to do these things, he just sees beyond the illusion, and if you just open your eyes you can be free too. And that, according to Christian Gnosticism, is exactly what Jesus was trying to do. According to Christian Gnosticism, the old testament God is the Demiurge, and the new testament God is the true God - that's why He seems to change from commanding vengeful entity to all-forgiving force of love and salvation. Christ wanted to teach people the true nature of God, and that by accepting His word, they could escape from the suffering caused by the illusion of being separate from God.<br /> <br /> Aaaaanywhoo... The similarities between D:tD and The Matrix come from the fact that they both layer cyberpunk overtones on top of Gnostic undertones. The difference is, the Matrix focuses on the struggle of humanity to escape from the false reality, while D:tD focuses on the struggle of former servants of the Demiurge to come to terms with the inherent freedom that comes with existing within the false reality. That's why, to me, D:tD is the perfect Fallen Angel story. Angels exist as one with the Demiurge, but when they fall victim to the illusion of individuality it creates to keep mortals in control, they often prefer the illusion over the truth of existing without that false sense of self. Thus, a Fallen Angel is born.<br /> <br /> Now, whether Fallen Angel = Demon is entirely up for debate. In my book, there is no difference, but I can totally see MCN's point that this particular story is about the process of the fall, where a true Demon game would need to be post-fall. And plenty of very valid arguments can be made that the Gnostic interpretation of Angels may not be the best way to depict them in a game like D:tD, or that the cyberpunk aesthetic is too far removed from the pop culture understanding of Angels and Demons. But arguing &quot;that's not what Demons are&quot; is kind of silly. Not only because Demons are fictional and an author can use creative license and call just about anything a Demon and not be wrong, but also because it absolutely is an accurate depiction of at least one religious philosophy's version of what a Demon is. Albeit with some superficial technological themes on top. As I said, reading this thread has convinced me that going with such a particular and admittedly obscure interpretation of Angels and Demons may not have been the most marketable choice, and extra work should have been done to EXPLAIN the Gnostic concepts that are central to understanding how an Unchained is in any way a Demon. But what else is new, that's a very common issue with core books in nWoD game lines.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To answer your question, Incendax, no. I would not say most people are aware of Gnosticism. It's not really practiced like other religions, because by its very nature it doesn't require any sort of ritual or dogma. Those are things the Demiurge demands to get you to buy into the idea that anything you do in this false reality matters. True enlightenment only requires understanding and acceptance, not practice. So it's not something that most people would have heard of it unless they've done religious or philosophical studies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-04-2014, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T07:56:26-08:00","id":83952,"title":"","content":"Isn't knowledgeable in Gnosticism, is Catholic. And I can still see why kids like cinnamon toast crunch, wait no I can't. But to me everything about this game is Demonic origin and thought. You can slap on words like gears but only because Demon's get to see what makes the world tick. If reality was a magic show, Demon's know the behind the scenes smoke and mirrors. What better way to describe that as a machine? Maybe it's one of those things you either get or you don't. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T09:02:00-08:00","id":83989,"title":"","content":"I wonder if part of why Descend demons don't feel like demons, to some, is that it's become the habit to think of angels and demons as opposite sides in a war over humanity. Which isn't the case here - humanity is more like the environment than the goal. Individual humans might be important resources, or even catalysts for falling - and individual demons may care for individual humans, or even humanity as a whole - but for demons as a whole, humanity is incidental to the Fall, to the Descent, and to Hell.<br /> <br /> I'm one of those to whom they <i>do</i> feel like demons. But thinking further over the human-as-environment vibe, and the Gnostic aspects of the setting, while it's easy to think of angels as the archons, in a sense, from the demons' perspective it's humans that are the archons. It's humans who are the main builders and maintainers of angelic infrastructure, it's humans who summon angels into the world, and it's humans who determine the bounds of Cover and what a demon can't and can't do without risking it (at least when it comes to the grossly out of character aspect, as it's human expectations that mostly determine this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Charlaquin:</b><br /> It is an illusion created by the Demiurge - a godlike being that for various reasons has an interest in keeping us believing in the illusion, in order to keep us separate from God. The true reality (which is to say, God) exists beyond this illusion, and understanding this brings us one step closer to escaping the false reality and returning to God. </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, if we equate the God-Machine with the Demiurge, by implication we're equating Hell with the True God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T09:17:28-08:00","id":83998,"title":"","content":"On humans as archons: Not really. Humans unwittingly serve the God-Machine, just like in Gnosticism humans easily buy into the Demiurge's subtle influence of Absolute Divinity, whether we acknowledge it or not, but that's not active, fully informed service something. Angels are different-they have something close to the same perspective as the God-Machine and actively service it, much more like the archons. People hate the matrix analogy, buuut....World of Darkness=Matrix, Collected infrastructure of Matrix=Demiurge, Angels=Agents, Humanity=....Humanity, and Demons are in a postion like Agent Smith's....but with a variety of motives that can go multiple ways<br /> <br /> Or to sum it up, humans are more inclined to this quote than an archon analogy would allow:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Student Council from Revolutionary Girl Utena</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">If it cannot break out of its shell, the chick will die without ever being born. We are the chick-The world is our egg. If we don't crack the world's shell, we will die without ever truly being born. Smash the world's shell. FOR THE REVOLUTION OF THE WORLD!</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Gnosticism in a nutshell, that. Er, eggshell.<br /> <br /> On Hell as True God: Maybe. Even without Gnosticism nessecarily being involved, it can very easily be perceived as the God-Machine as a face for Lucifer(In fact, the brief bit in Screwtape Letters where they take about the ideal sinner being a Materialist Magician comes to mind in regard to the entire techgnosticism of the God-Machine mythos), and that would imply that in Hell, they'll find Heaven actually.(Interesting corralation: G-M's Heaven and Angels are Soulless, while Demons are actually kind of all about &quot;Souls&quot;, within reason. One wonder if Demons can transcend the cobbled soul state) Going back to Gnosticisim though, what lies in &quot;hell&quot; could be Sophia, could be the Aeon Pantheon, could be the original masculine and feminine consciousness, could be the original thought, and it could just be self-deterministic. Gnosticism is kind of loose that way, from what I've seen.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T13:30:30-08:00","id":84187,"title":"","content":"In my admittetdly limited understanding of Gnosticism, the true reality/God exists beyond the illusion of separateness. And in my reading of D:tD, the Unchained view hell as freedom to remain separate for ever. In other words, they want to get as far away from the Gnostic concept of God as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T06:36:23-08:00","id":84535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=83952#post83952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't knowledgeable in Gnosticism, is Catholic. And I can still see why kids like cinnamon toast crunch, wait no I can't. But to me everything about this game is Demonic origin and thought. You can slap on words like gears but only because Demon's get to see what makes the world tick. If reality was a magic show, Demon's know the behind the scenes smoke and mirrors. What better way to describe that as a machine? Maybe it's one of those things you either get or you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clockwork_universe\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clockwork_universe</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if part of why Descend demons don't feel like demons, to some, is that it's become the habit to think of angels and demons as opposite sides in a war over humanity. Which isn't the case here - humanity is more like the environment than the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think I agree. For the most part, Demons fall for a reason... and that reason is generally humanity. Fall in love? Hate? Demons have some kind of relation to humans that drives them. Meanwhile, on the other end, the God Machine fights demons because they screw with its calculations to control and manipulate humanity.<br /> <br /> The war between Angels and Demons IS about humanity - if they're be ruled by cold machine-like fate, or free will. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans unwittingly serve the God-Machine, just like in Gnosticism humans easily buy into the Demiurge's subtle influence of Absolute Divinity, whether we acknowledge it or not, but that's not active, fully informed service something. </div> </div> </div> Given how the God Machine is open to debate.... it COULD be the true divinity. It could very well have created everything on the planet, including the planet itself. Perhaps the GM on Earth isn't bound to Earth, but is actually a Machine that encompasses the known universe.<br /> <br /> The only fact is that it exists. What that existence is? That's a very big, deliberate blank. Trying to compare it to the Demiurge is well and good... for your game. Its not the default for every game out there. <br /> <br /> Could the God Machine and its forge at the heart of the Universe be the true Empyrean realm from which all creation flows? There is a very strong, distinct possibility of &quot;Yes&quot; if the ST wants it to be. <br /> <br /> <br /> So, kindly stop pushing your view of the God Machine as absolute truth. Its not. The God Machine Chronicle book was quite clear that its up to the individual STs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:11:53-08:00","id":84560,"title":"","content":"I think the point of comparing the GM to the Demiurge was to illustrate the Gnostic themes that were pretty clearly a strong influence on the writing of D:tD. That doesn't mean that the GM has to be anything like that in game, but understanding a work's influences is still helpful in analyzing the work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:46:54-08:00","id":84585,"title":"","content":"Plus I was kind of responding to an idea that was directly continuing the comparison of DtD to Gnosticism. Did you read SunlessNick's post?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I wasn't talking to everyone there.<br /> <br /> That said, Charly is also quite right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T08:49:17-08:00","id":84622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=84535#post84535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, kindly stop pushing your view of the God Machine as absolute truth. Its not. The God Machine Chronicle book was quite clear that its up to the individual STs.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rider on Charl and Arc's notes and because this is a personal peeve of mine:<br /> <br /> Talking about one's reading is not &quot;pushing [it] as absolute truth&quot; and claiming it is is counterproductive, combative, needless, and more than a little goddamn annoying. It doesn't generate functional discussion. <span style=\"color:white\">I should know.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:25:51-08:00","id":84649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>MCN:</b><br /> Demons fall for a reason... and that reason is generally humanity. Fall in love? Hate? </div> </div> </div>The rest of the paragraph you partially quoted did bring that up, as it happens. But it's an individual thing - and as you admit, not true for every demon - it's not a way that demons-in-common are about humans-in-common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The war between Angels and Demons IS about humanity - if they're be ruled by cold machine-like fate, or free will. </div> </div> </div>Demons-in-common are fighting to save themselves, not humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:49:52-08:00","id":84660,"title":"","content":"I find it worth clarifying that I'm the guy who staunchly fought off the newbies and crazy Mage fans who insisted that Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were the same back when that was a big thing. I'm not the guy who goes making absolute claim about the universe of the World of Darkness, because that, to me, is counterproductive to what the World of Darkness is-one great big unknown.<br /> <br /> Understanding Gnosticism helps me understand what's going on with the ideas of the game, but seeing as I actually don't like some of the core tenets of Gnosticism, I don't particularly worry too much about it in my own execution of the games. For me, I channel the God-machine more as a vehicle of my issues with Christian culture, particularly within my own branch, as well as how social media(such as memes) within the many branches tends have a reductionist effect on doctrine to the point of creating a strict and debasing Pharisaical-esque people who places lesser laws of governance over the higher laws of concern and exaltation of others(or in other words, if the choice is letting a person hurt and <a href=\"https://www.lds.org/topics/word-of-wisdom?lang=eng\" target=\"_blank\">giving them whiskey to drink</a>, I'll give them whiskey to drink). There may be some gnostic elements in there, but since I revel in the material as well as how technology can expand spirituality, it's a mixed message.<br /> <br /> And I imagine that my thematic dealings of the God-Machine look quite different from many other people.<br /> <br /> So, no, if you want the God-Machine to be God, I'm not stopping you or arguing counter to you, as it is a perfectly viable idea. I suggest it may be something at odds with the World of Darkness itself, and I certainly will suggest that most people won't play it that way, but I'm not going to tell you you're wrong when the game is about not knowing the whole truth and when my own take doesn't have as much to do with the original inspirations as I talk about. I will tell you what's going on to understand the canon starting point we're all using to deviate from, but I won't insist upon it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:22:23-08:00","id":84689,"title":"","content":"The ones defending DTD because of Gnosticism should realize that vast majority of people will not have a clue what Gnosticism is. Expecting people to go out and learn about it is silly. It is a game, it should not require research on vague religions to understand the game which is counter to their expectations. People should get the book right off the bat and go, &quot;COOL, I get it&quot;, instead of asking &quot;What does this have to do with demons?&quot;. I just worry this will turn people away from the game because it is very different than what people expect. I think it can still be savaged, just needs to balance out more traditional look and feel of demons than the cyber/machine angle.<br /> <br /> Well, we will see how the wind blows whenever the book is released to the public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:05:36-08:00","id":84796,"title":"","content":"If you really believe something cannot be enjoyed by the vast majority of people unless they know everything about its sources and that works inspired by relatively obscure stuff are doomed to fail...well, let's just say I don't think your idea is realistic.<br /> <br /> Just to throw an example out there, I'm pretty sure most of those who read comics written by folks like Alan Moore, Neil Gaiman, Grant Morrison and Warren Ellis don't have a clue about a lot of their sources (personally, I don't even pretend I do) and yet, wind blowed pretty well for them.<br /> <br /> Matrix, which is, according to its own creators, Gnostic as f*** (well, the first one more than the others, and owes a lot to Grant Morrison)? I think we can agree it went well.<br /> <br /> I don't know. Maybe it's just because I have a more optimistic view of the general public, and I believe it can forgive its own ignorance and like something if that something is good.<br /> <br /> Naive, I know.<br /> <br /> Luckily, Demon is good. You may not like it, and that's absolutely legitimate, but the objective quality is still pretty high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-05-2014, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:58:48-08:00","id":84823,"title":"","content":"I don't think you have to understand Gnosticism to enjoy D:tD any more than you have to understand Gnosticism to enjoy The Matrix. However, if you're not at least casually familiar with it, you're unlikely to notice that the Agents are an allegory for the Demiurge's Angels. Similarly, you may not recognize the Unchained of D:tD as resembling Fallen Gnostic Angels. Now, in The Matrix it's not a particularly important plot point that the Agents are like Angels, but in D:tD the Unchained are the central characters, and are intended to be interpreted as Demons. Therefore, not being able to easily recognize them as such has a much stronger potential impact on one's enjoyment of the work. Obviously, if you miss that particular connection, but enjoy it anyway that's awesome, but I think its still a valid criticism to say that the Unchained don't come across as Demonic to a lot of people. That probably could have been avoided if the book had focused a bit more on explaining what makes the God-Machine's Angels Angels other than the fact that the book says they are, and what makes fallen Angels Demons other than the fact that the book says they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T16:49:13-08:00","id":84925,"title":"","content":"I still say its really fucking easy to see it as demons if you just remove the mentions of machine.<br /> <br /> God's (God Machine's) servants are angels (for the sake of the exercise, don't argue that it isn't the Judeo-Christian God).<br /> <br /> Demons are Fallen Angels both in Judeo-Christian belief and in DTD.<br /> <br /> Demons go around mostly undermining gods work.<br /> <br /> It could be that humanity just got it wrong all along and based the Judeo-Christian beliefs in Demons and Angels upon these things, without realizing it, in the past such beings likely weren't as advanced as they are today or were simply not as easily understood in context.<br /> <br /> You don't have to know shit about Gnosticism to understand fallen servants of a diety are demons.<br /> <br /> For those of you who can't put 2 and 2 together to make 4... well your just hung up on the machine aesthetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:14:48-08:00","id":84933,"title":"","content":"Here's a little story for the sake of perspective from someone who loves Demon the Fallen as well: down there in the CWoD forum, there's a a small but persistent line of thought which regularly resurfaces and, according to it, the Judeo-Christian aesthetics are just too pervasive. They make playing the game an excercise in futility since. for reasons I can't fathom, force you to play it in a certain way, limit the player's freedom and create only a certain kind of character. Admittedly, CWoD was more willing to suggest you how to play than NWoD, but I don't think things are that bad, especially in later books like Demon.<br /> <br /> And then there's when someone with a very limited knowledge of the books insists that the gameline somehow is just another cog of some sort of Abrahamic conspiracy. But it would not be fair to call <i>that </i>a line of thought: it's more a really loud noise, if I may say so.<br /> <br /> Funny, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T17:54:44-08:00","id":84960,"title":"","content":"You do not, and never need to understand Gnosticism to enjoy this game, or to see how it has everything to do with Demons. I disagree that it has anything to do with humanity for humanity's sake but that's another train of thought. If you are not seeing this as a Demon game, than you simply are choosing to take a side and won't see it from any other light; and that is on you. This game is beautiful in a way that the world of darkness has never been before. It's eerie and bone chilling, horrifying because it puts you in the place, something that was once a being of servitude to an undeniable deity of sorts. Now for the first time you are someone, someone who is aware but separate from the might, knowledge, and awe of you're very creator. You are a cursed child, a prideful child and if you go back it will not be on your terms. This game is sad, and freighting. If you never knew your father was just using you until the day you figured it out. Would you still love him? Abandoned among the masses who may only have the slightest idea of your creator's inner workings, even as it manipulates the world around them. Are they enviable or disgusting in their naivety? And I wonder, what did Lucifer think when he turned his back on God? I'm sorry for the tirade and yet, my God. This book should have been produced years ago. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T18:36:59-08:00","id":84981,"title":"","content":"It was inevitable that people would take issue with the presentation of Demons in D:tD, no matter how they were presented. The term just carries so many different meanings, all of which are highly specific, and many of which are drastically different from each other. Now I for one love the way they went with the Unchained, but obviously a lot of people did not. Is my opinion more valid than theirs? I don't think it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T19:27:13-08:00","id":84996,"title":"","content":"I just pointed out the Gnosticism because everybody kept running to that to defend why DTD is a demon game and I was just countering that few people will even know what that is. The main problem will be that is is counter intuitive to what most people will expect. That could be good or bad depending on the person.<br /> <br /> Cinder, I said in many posts that I like DTD, and I am glad I backed it. I just said I do not really see DTD as a demon game. It actually would seem better as a new IP to me at least. I understand why people do see it as a demon game, however I am not in that group. This might change with future books and supplements, but at the moment I think this would run a lot better as a lovecraft/alien/x-files game personally. Which would actually be really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:15:29-08:00","id":85342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=84796#post84796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matrix, which is, according to its own creators, Gnostic as f*** (well, the first one more than the others, and owes a lot to Grant Morrison)? I think we can agree it went well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, do you have a citation for this? I am perfectly willing to believe you, but I have seen this idea thrown around quite a bit and I had never heard of it. Is there a specific quote from the creators that you can reference?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=84925#post84925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still say its really fucking easy to see it as demons if you just remove the mentions of machine.<br /> For those of you who can't put 2 and 2 together to make 4... well your just hung up on the machine aesthetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally find the exercise almost impossible. Every single time I pick up the book I quickly get reminded of the machine aspect. It is far more prevalent than even the Atlantis references in the Mage books, which sparked all manner of love, hate, and flame wars. More importantly, my storyteller cannot ignore it either. =/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:25:06-08:00","id":85350,"title":"","content":"Between the pacts for human souls, the obvious parallels between the roles of traditional angels and demons and the ones in this game, and everything else... it definitely feels like a Demon game to me. My players seem to agree, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:33:36-08:00","id":85358,"title":"","content":"Almost nobody is going to remember this as &quot;the game about demons&quot;. They are going to remember it as &quot;the game about robots&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:37:08-08:00","id":85363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85358#post85358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost nobody is going to remember this as &quot;the game about demons&quot;. They are going to remember it as &quot;the game about robots&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a very broad generalization, which contradicts my own admittedly anecdotal evidence. What are you basing this on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:11:44-08:00","id":85384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85363#post85363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a very broad generalization, which contradicts my own admittedly anecdotal evidence. What are you basing this on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ph.D and extensive study in memetics. It's all going to depend on what splat books they release, but they are going to have to struggle to break this perception. Assuming they think the controversy is even a bad thing. They probably don't. Either way this will become a frequent forum topic that will revive again and again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:22:39-08:00","id":85393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85342#post85342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally find the exercise almost impossible. Every single time I pick up the book I quickly get reminded of the machine aspect. It is far more prevalent than even the Atlantis references in the Mage books, which sparked all manner of love, hate, and flame wars. More importantly, my storyteller cannot ignore it either. =/</div> </div> </div> </div>The infamous Atlantis situation with the mage books is the first parallel that came to mind with reading dtd with the machine/demon angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T10:04:06-08:00","id":85428,"title":"","content":"You know, it's funny.<br /> <br /> I'm reviewing this thread, and most people see this as a game of demons and angels. Quite a few do say it just requires a bit of tweaking, but so far it looks like people know this as the game about demons.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying that's representative of the fanbase on the whole-hell, it'd be arrogant to assume it represents most people in these forums-but the problem really seems to just be that the ones who have issues are the most vocal, rather than an actual mass of people who think robots.<br /> <br /> Also, PhD's mean nothing in this environment. I can tell you that I have multiple doctorates in whatever I want and I can prove it about as well as you can-which is to say, I can either actually explain my reasoning in extensive detail and show I generally know what I'm talking about, or I can be fucking lazy and hope that my own declaration to the highest echelons of academia will cause people to think I am what I say I am and treat me accordingly.<br /> <br /> That second one is a joke and will <i>never happen</i>. In these forums, all that matters is showing your work and reasoning*. Start now bucko.<br /> <br /> *Okay, and popularity. It'd be naive to expect people to not bandwagon around others. But really as far as the argument goes, it's gonna be you're ability to articulately and cohesively counter argue.**<br /> <br /> **Which is funny, because I've yet to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T10:22:30-08:00","id":85434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85384#post85384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ph.D and extensive study in memetics. It's all going to depend on what splat books they release, but they are going to have to struggle to break this perception. Assuming they think the controversy is even a bad thing. They probably don't. Either way this will become a frequent forum topic that will revive again and again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't think there is any perception to break. The book presents what it wants to present very well, and none of my players have had to tweak a single thing in their heads to make it work as far as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> This is not at all like Mage's problem with Atlantis, in my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T10:32:10-08:00","id":85443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85428#post85428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, PhD's mean nothing in this environment. I can tell you that I have multiple doctorates in whatever I want and I can prove it about as well as you can-which is to say, I can either actually explain my reasoning in extensive detail and show I generally know what I'm talking about, or I can be fucking lazy and hope that my own declaration to the highest echelons of academia will cause people to think I am what I say I am and treat me accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't blame me. He asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T10:52:03-08:00","id":85458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85443#post85443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't blame me. He asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I have a PhD&quot; is not, in fact, an argument for anything being discussed here, nor is &quot;I have done extensive study in memetics.&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably one or both of these things has <i>provided you with</i> a concrete piece of statistics or data or trends to point to to explain why you think as you do, but it is not an answer to &quot;what makes you think this?&quot; any more than my analysis of It's A Wonderful Life for my portfolio is explained by &quot;I have a bachelor's degree in English.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:07:11-08:00","id":85466,"title":"","content":"I have a diploma from the School of Hard Knocks and a BA in BS......can I chime in?<br /> <br /> I........Well.......um........<br /> <br /> Yeah, nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:11:19-08:00","id":85471,"title":"","content":"For me it's simple.<br /> <br /> I want to play this<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://images2.fanpop.com/image/photos/11900000/Fallen-Angel-demon-morality-11990573-250-355.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The game gives me this<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/assets/001/360/175/3edc3619efb160d971d17a392666722c_large.png?1385054512\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I'm a very visual guy. The aesthetic does not feel like a Demon to me.<br /> <br /> That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:11:37-08:00","id":85472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85458#post85458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably one or both of these things has <i>provided you with</i> a concrete piece of statistics or data or trends to point to to explain why you think as you do but it is not an answer to &quot;what makes you think this?&quot; any more than my analysis of It's A Wonderful Life for my portfolio is explained by &quot;I have a bachelor's degree in English.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Convincing someone on the internet is rarely beneficial. I made a prediction, nothing more. Unless future splats lighten the science fiction elements, I am quite confident that it will prove true in the coming years. Take it, or leave it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:47:46-08:00","id":85495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85472#post85472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Convincing someone on the internet is rarely beneficial. I made a prediction, nothing more. Unless future splats lighten the science fiction elements, I am quite confident that it will prove true in the coming years. Take it, or leave it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will doubtless <i>never</i> be convinced, but sharing actual <i>reasoning</i> rather than leaning on an assertion of vaguely relevant credentials would probably do more to justify bothering to share that prediction. Did you think that prediction was beneficial?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T12:27:28-08:00","id":85539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85495#post85495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will doubtless <i>never</i> be convinced, but sharing actual <i>reasoning</i> rather than leaning on an assertion of vaguely relevant credentials would probably do more to justify bothering to share that prediction. Did you think that prediction was beneficial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exerting greater effort would not change the outcome, by your own admission. I think the prediction adds one more voice to those who feel the game does not resonate with the current western zeitgeist of demons. Speaking up, in whatever fashion, adds more momentum to those who share the sentiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T12:30:11-08:00","id":85545,"title":"","content":"Some folks are going to be happy, others are not. You can't please everyone. Personally I /like/ this concept of what demons and angels truly are. And nothing will change that. It is no different than the interpertation of what exactly heaven and hell are between multiple religions. <br /> <br /> Everyone has a slightly different, or even drastically different story.. whose to say which is true? The GMC, and D:tD by extension, operates on the concept that 'god' is a vast cosmic supercomputer.. and through that lens, what an angel or demon is is changed to reflect that. Saying D:tD's demons are not demons is about as logical as saying the version of god of one religion is not god.-- but I'm getting a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> What is really being said here by those who don't like the demons in D:tD is &quot;This particular imagining of what an angel or demon is does not fit the archetypical concept I much prefer.&quot; If that's all there is too it, then the buck really stops there. Because really, nobody in here can force you to like a concept you yourself don't like, and by the same token, you can't really make other people hate it like you do. Seriously, this is all comes across as &quot;Trukk not Munky&quot; and not really about anything actually bad about the gameline. (( <a href=\"http://transformers.wikia.com/wiki/Trukk_not_munky\" target=\"_blank\">http://transformers.wikia.com/wiki/Trukk_not_munky</a> ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:15:51-08:00","id":85582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85545#post85545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some folks are going to be happy, others are not. You can't please everyone. Personally I /like/ this concept of what demons and angels truly are. And nothing will change that. It is no different than the interpertation of what exactly heaven and hell are between multiple religions.<br /> <br /> Everyone has a slightly different, or even drastically different story.. whose to say which is true? The GMC, and D:tD by extension, operates on the concept that 'god' is a vast cosmic supercomputer.. and through that lens, what an angel or demon is is changed to reflect that. Saying D:tD's demons are not demons is about as logical as saying the version of god of one religion is not god.-- but I'm getting a bit off topic.<br /> <br /> What is really being said here by those who don't like the demons in D:tD is &quot;This particular imagining of what an angel or demon is does not fit the archetypical concept I much prefer.&quot; If that's all there is too it, then the buck really stops there. Because really, nobody in here can force you to like a concept you yourself don't like, and by the same token, you can't really make other people hate it like you do. Seriously, this is all comes across as &quot;Trukk not Munky&quot; and not really about anything actually bad about the gameline. (( <a href=\"http://transformers.wikia.com/wiki/Trukk_not_munky\" target=\"_blank\">http://transformers.wikia.com/wiki/Trukk_not_munky</a> ))</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. For me at least this is correct.<br /> <br /> I appreciate a lot of the mechanical stuff, the ideas and such. Cover is excellent, I love patchwork self built covers (and conversely am annoyed by the soul pacts to get an entire new life that bypasses the patchwork covers system). I love the 'Going Loud' really fells like unleashing the true power of the demon, power stat 10, all the powers, unlimited fuel etc. exceptional stuff.<br /> <br /> But...I don't like the aesthetic of mechanical stuff linked to name Demon at all. I dislike espionage as a genre and hate playing games with it even more.<br /> <br /> Demon is basically not the game for me...not at least in its current form.<br /> <br /> If they weren't called <i>Demons</i> I would probably appreciate it more. But my head has cognitive dissonance.<br /> <br /> However the critical issue that turns my appreciation for mechanics and knowing it's not the game for me into actual <i>dislike</i> is that, because this game exists, the chances of them making another &quot;Demon&quot; game which uses the aesthetics I do like are pretty much zero. The existence of D:tD prejudices against the nWoD having a &quot;Demon&quot; game that I do like. Not D:tD's fault of course.<br /> <br /> I just hope that the Dark Eras gives us a Demon chapter that shows how Demon operates without the modern tech spin.<br /> <br /> And I hope the Translation Guide for D:tF is amazing.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh and that some of the chatter on the forum pre-release was about the 'Music of the Spheres' which has very medieval, psudoscience, religious etc. connotations and I suspect I latched on to that heavily in the build up for the game and filtered out the competing information. Selective bias basically on my part. Then the final product didn't match what I had constructed in my head. Not fair to the game. I know that. Doesn't mean I can;t appreciate it for what it is. But realising that also doesn't change the fact I dislike it. And seem to dislike it more each time I read through it.<br /> <br /> I might ambush it down a dark alley and rummage its pockets for mechanics though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 03-06-2014, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:22:49-08:00","id":85586,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, the Translation Guide is definitely going to be the godsend (hehe) that people who want to essentially have Demon: the Fallen 2.0 were hoping for. At least to my understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:25:02-08:00","id":85589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85586#post85586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, the Translation Guide is definitely going to be the godsend (hehe) that people who want to essentially have Demon: the Fallen 2.0 were hoping for. At least to my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>The promise of the Translation Guide is the only thing that keeps me checking this forum every now and then, hoping for a snippet or spoiler.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:39:39-08:00","id":85594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85589#post85589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The promise of the Translation Guide is the only thing that keeps me checking this forum every now and then, hoping for a snippet or spoiler.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Unfortunately my storyteller outright said he does not expect he will ever run Demon: the Descent because of all the science fiction elements, and the dramatic reduction of personal horror. And since I'm terrible at running games of my own, my only hope is to wait for the translation guide if it ever gets made.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T13:55:26-08:00","id":85607,"title":"","content":"Reduction of personal horror? I dunno, it's probably the most personally horrifying RPG I've ever read. But the sci-fi stuff, yeah, I have nothing to say about that. It's not everyone's thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:08:10-08:00","id":85613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85607#post85607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reduction of personal horror? I dunno, it's probably the most personally horrifying RPG I've ever read. But the sci-fi stuff, yeah, I have nothing to say about that. It's not everyone's thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>He has a big thing about human emotions. Something about since Demons were never human they have no way to really understand human emotion. I think he has the same issue with Promethean (which he has never run for us).<br /> <br /> One of his quotes (paraphrased) was something like <i>&quot;What does a toaster feel like? I'm sure whatever it is, it is very intense and meaningful to toasters. But I don't know what that is.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:14:12-08:00","id":85617,"title":"","content":"Actually, demons explicitly feel human emotion due to the nature of their Covers, and it carries over to the rest of their existence. This is spelled out in the first chapter of the corebook after the introduction. The disconnect is how demons express the emotions that they do feel, which is to say that they do not show outward physical signs of what they are feeling unless they intentionally set out to do so (and they can do so in a perfectly convincing way).<br /> <br /> This does not mean demons never, say, lash out in anger at someone. You just won't see it coming as an outside observer unless they go out of their way to alert you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 03-06-2014, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:21:17-08:00","id":85626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85617#post85617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, demons explicitly feel human emotion due to the nature of their Covers, and it carries over to the rest of their existence. This is spelled out in the first chapter of the corebook after the introduction. The disconnect is how demons express the emotions that they do feel, which is to say that they do not show outward physical signs of what they are feeling unless they intentionally set out to do so (and they can do so in a perfectly convincing way).<br /> <br /> This does not mean demons never, say, lash out in anger at someone. You just won't see it coming as an outside observer unless they go out of their way to alert you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because they feel it does not mean they understand what those feelings mean, how to express them, or have a lifetime of nature and nurture to program their reactions to it. Do they experience anger as a buzz? As a tingle? As a numeric expression that indicates that they are now Angry 7? There are even real life people who don't know what their feelings mean, even after a lifetime of experience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:27:36-08:00","id":85633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85626#post85626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because they feel it does not mean they understand what those feelings mean, how to express them, or have a lifetime of nature and nurture to program their reactions to it. Do they experience anger as a buzz? As a tingle? As a numeric expression that indicates that they are now Angry 7? There are even real life people who don't know what their feelings mean, even after a lifetime of experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a question of which demon you're discussing, at that point. It depends on how experienced they are at being human, what their purpose was as an angel (which allows for many gradations in starting points for knowing how to express these things)... still, in the end? Most of the time? They experience these things as a human experiences them.<br /> <br /> And as you say, there are real people who don't know what their feelings mean. It's a very human ignorance.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, what Satchel said but with less abrasion intended. There is a section in the very first chapter which goes into detail on these things very clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:31:42-08:00","id":85637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evidently this is a problem that also interferes with his ability to read, given that &quot;demon minds, while black boxes, are still more or less human in their thought processes going from Point A to Point B&quot; is a thing that the book actually says in the section that talks about how the Unchained work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abrasiveness aside, that just means they understand cause and effect. They do not react to events around them as &quot;Orange, 31, #&amp;$, Beep&quot;. Basically it helps to mitigate the old fishmalk problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","user":"Charles Red","date":". 03-06-2014, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:36:08-08:00","id":85641,"title":"","content":"You are contradicting what is actually written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:36:46-08:00","id":85642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85637#post85637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just means they understand cause and effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to go ahead and forward the response of &quot;no&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although a demon\u2019s physical nature is dualistic \u2014 partly divine, partly mundane \u2014 their mental and emotional outlook resembles that of a human. It\u2019s true that demons have extraordinary pasts and think in alien ways that defy supernatural manipulation, but they tend to come to fairly mundane human conclusions. <b>If someone a demon cares about is in danger, he experiences fear. He feels it in his gut, in his throat, in his chest, just like an ordinary human being.</b><br /> A demon\u2019s essentially human perspective is reinforced by her human experience of the world. Demons are more sensitive to certain supernatural emanations, but <b>they generally see and hear the world in human ways.</b><br /> No matter how alien a demon might be when she first Falls, <b>years of thinking about human things, experiencing the world in human ways, and feeling human emotions has a humanizing effect on them.</b> This doesn\u2019t mean that demons are universally good people \u2014 there\u2019s a big difference between \u201chuman\u201d and \u201chumane\u201d \u2014 but <b>when demons are monsters, they are monsters in a human way.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:39:42-08:00","id":85644,"title":"","content":"Satchel, with a direct quote from chapter 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:48:47-08:00","id":85650,"title":"","content":"Cool, that may be a fairly recent change. I will show that to my storyteller and see if that changes his mind on the issue!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:57:37-08:00","id":85653,"title":"","content":"It isn't a change, actually; it's in the preview copy on the Kickstarter page. It has been there from day one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T15:01:25-08:00","id":85657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85653#post85653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't a change, actually; it's in the preview copy on the Kickstarter page. It has been there from day one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly do not think so? Not that I have been keeping track of the time of the updates, nor am I responsible for what my storyteller may or may not have read.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T15:03:16-08:00","id":85660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85657#post85657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly do not think so? Not that I have been keeping track of the time of the updates, nor am I responsible for what my storyteller may or may not have read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just checked the original preview; yes it was there.<br /> <br /> There were no updates to that document at any time after it was posted. It is the same document originally put online.<br /> <br /> edit: This does suggest to me that your storyteller did not read the material before passing judgement. I might be wrong, but I can't think of how someone would come to the exact opposite conclusion stated in the text otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","user":"Aiden","date":". 03-06-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T21:16:26-08:00","id":85824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85660#post85660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just checked the original preview; yes it was there.<br /> <br /> There were no updates to that document at any time after it was posted. It is the same document originally put online.<br /> <br /> edit: This does suggest to me that your storyteller did not read the material before passing judgement. I might be wrong, but I can't think of how someone would come to the exact opposite conclusion stated in the text otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>They may have just skimmed through some parts and missed that particular quote. I wouldn't blame them if so, the preview text on Kickstarter was pretty hard to get through, being just a wall of text. It's really amazing how the formatting of the PDFs increases the ease of flow through the text. Anyway, here's hoping you'll convince your ST to give it a shot, Charles Red.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T00:24:26-08:00","id":85873,"title":"","content":"I do think DTD does overlap with MAGE/Atlantis problem. Both have the fixed origin problem that sets the game in stone. All angels/demons come from the god machine, the end. No debate about that, no different possible origins, that is it. I prefer that games leave origins vague and not set in stone with only multiple possible explanations theorized, but nothing guaranteed. While the details may be debatable, the end result does not change that demons from DTD were created by the god machine and that's that.<br /> <br /> The scifi elements do hurt aesthetically for those who want a more traditional game. All I can see is mechanical robots shaped like a demon, or something that comes across as a cyber-demon that is half organic and half machine. This is hard to ignore when it is described and reinforced again and again in the book. Also, the espionage/spy angle seems kind of weird and not the first thing when I think of a generic demon purpose. It is not bad, just weird and kind of limiting on the type of gameplay potential demon could have. I think a little more horror route would have been better.<br /> <br /> On a side note and minor peave of mine. Why does every game in Nwod have to tie humanity outlook/motivations into the characters? Usually with the goal to become human, or prevent yourself from losing your humanity. While ok occasionally, it gets old when its every single game. Obviously hunter and mage are humans so they get a free pass, but vampires? They are monsters, they should act it and not cry about it. Someone always say &quot;Humans are the worst monsters&quot; or something like that, that is BS and bugs me to end. Have anybody actually look at the scary stuff that nature has created? The only reason we seem scary is because we have human intelligence and can do horrible things with it. However, give some of the real monsters in nature human level intelligence and we would learn quickly what an intelligent monster with alien motivations can make human monsters seem like misguided children. I only brought this up because we were getting on demons with human motivations and such. I think most of the game lines should be flexible, some characters might want to understand/find humanity, while others have no interest and embrace the creature they are with totally alien outlook on life. It just bugs me that if you choose the later your considered doing it wrong by the books interpretation and often get some kind of punishment because of it. Like I said, minor pet peeve since we were on the subject.<br /> <br /> Like I said earlier, I think it would have been better to go this route. I would have the GM still be the biggest antagonist, but not the only one. I would have demons be different species and not just ones created by the god machine. The god machine would have created the DTD version, however the other demons were pulled from other places by the GM and altered mentally, phisically, or both. Most have a lot of their memories erased so their origins are vauge have remembered, but one thing they do remember. They fell (escaped) the god machine. So, some of the type of demons:<br /> <br /> DTD Demons (the created)<br /> Inferno Demons (sins)<br /> Mage Empyrean (fallen angles)<br /> Lovecraftian beings (The twisted)<br /> Other Religions (The lost ones)<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that the GM did something to these demons so their memories of their origins is hazy and it prevents them from returning to their home (wherever that might be). The only ones sure of their origin are the DTD demons. Some remember escaping, others remember the GM just letting them go, others could remember being broken out, however they all escaped and are all hunted by the GM, its agents and other things. All the demons should have some basic questions. Why where they captured in the first place? What was the GM going to do? Can they get home? As for origins, each demon has its own theory, the created would claim the GM created everything, the sins might claim they come from a place of pain and blood where they existed long before anything called itself a god, the fallen angels might say they come from the true heaven where light shines and the true god exists, while the twisted might tell of a strange dimension where the laws of physics are vastly different and ancient alien creatures from the end of time are slowly remaking the universe and things the GM is just a smaller lesser of these creatures like an amoeba compared to them, the lost ones speak of multitudes of gods and goddesses they have seen, and others whisper that none of them are right and they were all created by the GM for some weird experiment and all their memories are false.<br /> <br /> As for the GM angels, I would have some call them angles, while others vehemently opposes calling them that and instead call them servants of the imposter god (or machine). As I said, the GM would still be the lead antagonist, but now we have a wide selection of backgrounds to pull antagonists from. We can have other religions hunting their for their enemy/ally, they might have beings from other dimensions infiltrating the world studying the world and the GM, they might have more traditional angels come to clense the world, or we might have other native traditional demons fighting those contaminated by the GM, and finally we have the original DTD angels/GM playing havoc with everyone.<br /> <br /> As for motivation, this gives way more freedom. Some might go after the GM like in the DTD book, while others wash their hands of it and seek to find a way home through learning about the world, others see a fresh untouched paradise of humanity they can start their own little empire of and the flip side is some might want to save humanity from they hell they created. <br /> <br /> Of course, this is just a quick general idea of how I would have done it. You could still play the game exactly the same as it is now, but now nothing is really set in stone and you have more variety of beings to choose from and not just the DTD cyber demons.<br /> <br /> It is late and running on fumes, I am probably not writing completely clearly and will most likely wince tomorrow when I see this after I wake up. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T01:25:25-08:00","id":85886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85873#post85873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think DTD does overlap with MAGE/Atlantis problem. Both have the fixed origin problem that sets the game in stone. All angels/demons come from the god machine, the end. No debate about that, no different possible origins, that is it. I prefer that games leave origins vague and not set in stone with only multiple possible explanations theorized, but nothing guaranteed. While the details may be debatable, the end result does not change that demons from DTD were created by the god machine and that's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of that, but that's actually a pretty good point. Fortunately, the nature of the God Machine is pretty darn open. The only things about it that are really set in stone are that it operates through infrastructure and occult matrices, and... I guess that it's a machine. Which does feed into your next point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85873#post85873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scifi elements do hurt aesthetically for those who want a more traditional game. All I can see is mechanical robots shaped like a demon, or something that comes across as a cyber-demon that is half organic and half machine. This is hard to ignore when it is described and reinforced again and again in the book. Also, the espionage/spy angle seems kind of weird and not the first thing when I think of a generic demon purpose. It is not bad, just weird and kind of limiting on the type of gameplay potential demon could have. I think a little more horror route would have been better.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many examples in the book of Angels and Demons that do not have mechanical design elements, both in the art and in the text. There are also plenty of examples in pop culture of Angels and Demons that are mechanical. And ultimately, with the God Machine becoming a Thing That Exists in the World of Darkness, is it really so surprising that Demons would be its fallen servants? I guess if you have a problem with the whole concept of the God Machine in the first place, then yeah, you're going to dislike Demon. Not much can be done about that, apart from the translation guide we have been assured is forthcoming. Although I'll bet money it's going to give you the same advice everyone on this thread has been giving: ignore the (entirely superficial) machine asthetic and you're left with pretty damn traditional Demons. As far as the espionage thing goes, you can totally play a game that doesn't play up that aspect and instead focuses on taking the fight to the Angels. It just seems like all of the complaints that are being made about Descent are about the presentation, not about the game itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85873#post85873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note and minor peave of mine. Why does every game in Nwod have to tie humanity outlook/motivations into the characters? Usually with the goal to become human, or prevent yourself from losing your humanity. While ok occasionally, it gets old when its every single game. Obviously hunter and mage are humans so they get a free pass, but vampires? They are monsters, they should act it and not cry about it. Someone always say &quot;Humans are the worst monsters&quot; or something like that, that is BS and bugs me to end. Have anybody actually look at the scary stuff that nature has created? The only reason we seem scary is because we have human intelligence and can do horrible things with it. However, give some of the real monsters in nature human level intelligence and we would learn quickly what an intelligent monster with alien motivations can make human monsters seem like misguided children. I only brought this up because we were getting on demons with human motivations and such. I think most of the game lines should be flexible, some characters might want to understand/find humanity, while others have no interest and embrace the creature they are with totally alien outlook on life. It just bugs me that if you choose the later your considered doing it wrong by the books interpretation and often get some kind of punishment because of it. Like I said, minor pet peeve since we were on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, if you don't like this element of WoD, you might be playing the wrong game. You can use various system hacks to alter or remove the various Karma meters, but the fact is it's a huge part of WoD's identity, and always has been (nWoD, at least. I don't have enough experience with oWoD to speak for that). That said, you may be looking at that aspect of gameplay the wrong way. Losing Integrity/Humanity/Cover/whatever is not a punishment for incorrect behavior. It's a tool for telling the story of how a character, who is a monster, relates to humanity. Some may strive to be the best human they can, while others may just not give a shit. Both are valid character choices, and the Karma stat is just there to give those choices some mechanical weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85873#post85873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said earlier, I think it would have been better to go this route. I would have the GM still be the biggest antagonist, but not the only one. I would have demons be different species and not just ones created by the god machine. The god machine would have created the DTD version, however the other demons were pulled from other places by the GM and altered mentally, phisically, or both. Most have a lot of their memories erased so their origins are vauge have remembered, but one thing they do remember. They fell (escaped) the god machine. So, some of the type of demons:<br /> <br /> DTD Demons (the created)<br /> Inferno Demons (sins)<br /> Mage Empyrean (fallen angles)<br /> Lovecraftian beings (The twisted)<br /> Other Religions (The lost ones)<br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that the GM did something to these demons so their memories of their origins is hazy and it prevents them from returning to their home (wherever that might be). The only ones sure of their origin are the DTD demons. Some remember escaping, others remember the GM just letting them go, others could remember being broken out, however they all escaped and are all hunted by the GM, its agents and other things. All the demons should have some basic questions. Why where they captured in the first place? What was the GM going to do? Can they get home? As for origins, each demon has its own theory, the created would claim the GM created everything, the sins might claim they come from a place of pain and blood where they existed long before anything called itself a god, the fallen angels might say they come from the true heaven where light shines and the true god exists, while the twisted might tell of a strange dimension where the laws of physics are vastly different and ancient alien creatures from the end of time are slowly remaking the universe and things the GM is just a smaller lesser of these creatures like an amoeba compared to them, the lost ones speak of multitudes of gods and goddesses they have seen, and others whisper that none of them are right and they were all created by the GM for some weird experiment and all their memories are false.<br /> <br /> As for the GM angels, I would have some call them angles, while others vehemently opposes calling them that and instead call them servants of the imposter god (or machine). As I said, the GM would still be the lead antagonist, but now we have a wide selection of backgrounds to pull antagonists from. We can have other religions hunting their for their enemy/ally, they might have beings from other dimensions infiltrating the world studying the world and the GM, they might have more traditional angels come to clense the world, or we might have other native traditional demons fighting those contaminated by the GM, and finally we have the original DTD angels/GM playing havoc with everyone.<br /> <br /> As for motivation, this gives way more freedom. Some might go after the GM like in the DTD book, while others wash their hands of it and seek to find a way home through learning about the world, others see a fresh untouched paradise of humanity they can start their own little empire of and the flip side is some might want to save humanity from they hell they created.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is just a quick general idea of how I would have done it. You could still play the game exactly the same as it is now, but now nothing is really set in stone and you have more variety of beings to choose from and not just the DTD cyber demons.<br /> <br /> It is late and running on fumes, I am probably not writing completely clearly and will most likely wince tomorrow when I see this after I wake up. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but I do not find the story this tells to be half as compelling as the story D:tD tells. First of all, it's treading even more into Changeling: the Lost territory, and there was already a fair bit of conceptual overlap. Although the good news is, if you like that concept, it would be really easy to re-fluff C:tL a bit and have almost exactly the game you described. Aside from that, I really prefer that they took one story idea and told it well, rather than trying to cram everything into the same game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T05:10:16-08:00","id":85947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85873#post85873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DTD Demons (the created)<br /> Inferno Demons (sins)<br /> Mage Empyrean (fallen angles)<br /> Lovecraftian beings (The twisted)<br /> Other Religions (The lost ones)</div> </div> </div> </div> Mage doesn't have Empyrean. They have Supernal Aether angels in the form of Seraphim and Cherubim (gross/subtle arcana elementals, basically). They have Astral Eidolons and daimons, the opposite of goetic demons. <br /> <br /> Empyrean only appears once in the history of WoD - that's in the Inferno book, and doesn't really appear again, and doesn't have a specific origin.<br /> <br /> [/nitpick]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:39:37-08:00","id":85971,"title":"","content":"Atlantis isn't set in stone for Mage, it's a theory at best and pure arrogance at worst. Also, Werewolf has one of the biggest &quot;This is where we come from origins&quot; and the two factions are killing one another over it. Though Some of the Forsaken end up joining the pure, but yea you're right. Demon is totally Non-Traditional. Another point, Demon's Don't want to be human. They don't generally like having to hide with rats in our stinky cesspool but we're a damn convenient sheep skin. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:46:14-08:00","id":85973,"title":"","content":"Some demons do want to be human, actually. Humans aren't at risk of being hunted down by Destroyer angels, after all.<br /> <br /> @Badmojo: Do you think Demon: the Fallen had an 'Atlantis Problem' because the definitive origin of its fallen angels is 'God made them and they rebelled'?<br /> <br /> Also, all of the motivations you speak of exist in the book already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T07:35:23-08:00","id":86002,"title":"","content":"God &quot;creates&quot; angels and then proceeds to on occasion frankenstein them into completely different configurations, wipe their memories, reprogram them, and generally treat them as tools in need of repurposing.<br /> <br /> This is the same entity that is capable of summoning various different sorts of beings from other dimensions and prefers to piggyback on existing work when it can. We have no actual idea where angels are summoned from that don't reside in facilities. Just because the God-Machine is their common entry point into the World of Darkness does not mean it is their common origin any more than immigrants to America are all from Ellis Island.<br /> <br /> Arcadia may or may not be <i>dozens upon hundreds of places mashed together into metaphors for themselves</i>, and yet I have not seen any complaints to the effect that changelings are limited by &quot;com[ing] from [Arcadia], the end.&quot;<br /> <br /> So far the only major gameline in the nWoD whose splat has an absolute fixed origin point (as we understand it) is Mummy, whose entire setup rather necessitates a historical starting point to have cults to undying god-servants stretching back to the diaspora of an ancient vanished empire. Everything else is crossbred or naturalized or exists in a context in which its genesis has been mythologized, propagandized, obfuscated, or otherwise rendered cosmologically distant and impossible to conclusively gauge.<br /> <br /> Demons have no idea where they come from. They just know that the Machine made them the way they were before they Fell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-07-2014, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:00:07-08:00","id":86046,"title":"","content":"I chatted with my storyteller over Skype last night, and pointed out the text about them feeling things like humans. He wrote back:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It is pretty obvious the designers wrote themselves into a corner with how alien these machines are, and needed some kind of deus ex machina to make them even playable. Unfortunately, eldritch abominations are not going to get their official people cards from spending a few years with humans any more than a Xenomorph would.<br /> <br /> I did not believe it when the Terminator said he 'now understood why people cry', and I do not believe these can either. I'm really sorry. I know you are really interested in giving this game a shot, but nobody else at our table wants to play robots.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Soooo that was a crash and burn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:09:34-08:00","id":86051,"title":"","content":"Forgive me for assuming but I think it's better to recognize you're not gonna get any traction from this guy, he's set his mind against it, doesn't seem like any sort of argument will sway his opinion. That's a shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:21:40-08:00","id":86060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86051#post86051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me for assuming but I think it's better to recognize you're not gonna get any traction from this guy, he's set his mind against it, doesn't seem like any sort of argument will sway his opinion. That's a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://xkcd.com/386/\" target=\"_blank\">But, but, but......someone is WRONG on the Internet!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T09:25:04-08:00","id":86062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86046#post86046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chatted with my storyteller over Skype last night, and pointed out the text about them feeling things like humans. He wrote back:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It is pretty obvious the designers wrote themselves into a corner with how alien these machines are, and needed some kind of deus ex machina to make them even playable. Unfortunately, eldritch abominations are not going to get their official people cards from spending a few years with humans any more than a Xenomorph would.<br /> <br /> I did not believe it when the Terminator said he 'now understood why people cry', and I do not believe these can either. I'm really sorry. I know you are really interested in giving this game a shot, but nobody else at our table wants to play robots.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Soooo that was a crash and burn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Boy. What a completely, factually, objectively wrong interpretation of the game and our process of creating it. <br /> <br /> Tell your ST, from me, he's <i>allowed not to like it</i>. It's OK. I'm not offended if he doesn't like the game. But he doesn't need to put words in our mouths. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the &quot;set in stone&quot; origin of the Unchained...yes. They have a cohesive backstory. That leads to a more focus game, which is good. The book's already 300 pages plus, I can't imagine what it would have been like if we cast a net wide enough to catch all interpretations of &quot;demon.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T16:05:23-08:00","id":86346,"title":"","content":"Wait... you mean that the casual reader doesn't know your own mind better than you do? *gasp!* What is this world coming to!? <br /> <br /> Sorry, I just had to snark. Don't mind me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T16:24:57-08:00","id":86359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86046#post86046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chatted with my storyteller over Skype last night, and pointed out the text about them feeling things like humans. He wrote back:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It is pretty obvious the designers wrote themselves into a corner with how alien these machines are, and needed some kind of deus ex machina to make them even playable. Unfortunately, eldritch abominations are not going to get their official people cards from spending a few years with humans any more than a Xenomorph would.<br /> <br /> I did not believe it when the Terminator said he 'now understood why people cry', and I do not believe these can either. I'm really sorry. I know you are really interested in giving this game a shot, but nobody else at our table wants to play robots.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Soooo that was a crash and burn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Try pointing out that, given the fact that the God-Machine tends to operate by piggy-backing onto and/or cannibalizing existing things rather than actually something entirely new, as well as the fact that where angels come from before the God-Machine &quot;summons&quot; them is something angels and demons themselves don't know, it's entirely possible that some or all angels <i>used to be human</i>.<br /> <br /> Remember the Reapers, from Mass Effect? Remember how frighteningly alien they were, even in a galaxy full of aliens? <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Remember how they turned out to be made out of the recycled remnants of all their genocided victims--machines born from repurposed organic life?</div></div> </div> </div> That's angels right there--or it could be.<br /> <br /> Point out, also, that the &quot;robotic emotionlessness&quot; of angels as presented in Demon often comes across not as a <i>lack</i> of emotion, but as emotion being suppressed by an external force: the conditioning imposed by, and constant mental connection to, the God-Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86002#post86002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God &quot;creates&quot; angels and then proceeds to on occasion frankenstein them into completely different configurations, wipe their memories, reprogram them, and generally treat them as tools in need of repurposing.<br /> <br /> This is the same entity that is capable of summoning various different sorts of beings from other dimensions and prefers to piggyback on existing work when it can. We have no actual idea where angels are summoned from that don't reside in facilities. Just because the God-Machine is their common entry point into the World of Darkness does not mean it is their common origin any more than immigrants to America are all from Ellis Island.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Demons have no idea where they come from. They just know that the Machine made them the way they were before they Fell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":743,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","user":"Exploding Frogs","date":". 03-07-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:06:35-08:00","id":86373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86359#post86359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible that some or all angels <i>used to be human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say that this is the most impressive idea I have heard all week. The notion that the angels were once human and, quite possibly, forced against their will to serve an unfeeling pan dimensional horror by shoving machine parts into them... That adds a huge dimension of personal horror to it. The fear of the other, and being transformed against your will into the other, and having your mind taken from you so that your thoughts are no longer your own? Brilliant.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bMy wife was running late from work tonight, but they were not. Things that look like they might have been people once, but with countless wires where their arms once were. My plate of leftovers shattered on the ground, as those wires punched through my flesh and everything blacked out. I'm in a white room now. Blood drips from the saw blade that just finished with my skull. Shouldn't that hurt? I can feel the wire-fingers in my brain. They just took out a piece they didn't like and tossed it on the floor. I want to scream, but a little red 'DENIED' appears before my eyes every time I try. And I have tried so many times.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T18:16:33-08:00","id":86399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86346#post86346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... you mean that the casual reader doesn't know your own mind better than you do? *gasp!* What is this world coming to!?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I just had to snark. Don't mind me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to tell Matt what to think once. My spleen is still missing.<br /> <br /> True story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T18:25:49-08:00","id":86405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86373#post86373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say that this is the most impressive idea I have heard all week. The notion that the angels were once human and, quite possibly, forced against their will to serve an unfeeling pan dimensional horror by shoving machine parts into them... That adds a huge dimension of personal horror to it. The fear of the other, and being transformed against your will into the other, and having your mind taken from you so that your thoughts are no longer your own? Brilliant.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bMy wife was running late from work tonight, but they were not. Things that look like they might have been people once, but with countless wires where their arms once were. My plate of leftovers shattered on the ground, as those wires punched through my flesh and everything blacked out. I'm in a white room now. Blood drips from the saw blade that just finished with my skull. Shouldn't that hurt? I can feel the wire-fingers in my brain. They just took out a piece they didn't like and tossed it on the floor. I want to scream, but a little red 'DENIED' appears before my eyes every time I try. And I have tried so many times.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... Your definition of personal horror and my definition of personal horror are not the same. In my opinion, there are only two kinds of horror stories. The one where you point outside into the unknown and say &quot;the monsters are out there&quot; (that fear of the other you were talking about), and the one where you look at yourself and say &quot;the monsters are in here&quot; (what I would consider personal horror). Now, I happen to also love the idea that at least some of the God-Machine's Angels used to be human, and think it has a lot of potential for personal horror, but for completely the opposite reason. Not because it adds an Other to fear, but because it makes the thing you fear feel more like yourself, which is far more terrifying in my opinion. I suppose this is a little off topic, but it seemed like an interesting point of discussion. Maybe I'll start another thread for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T19:35:34-08:00","id":86428,"title":"","content":"In my mind, I had established where Angels come from. Reading the previous comments. &quot;Ew, Just ew&quot; I'm totally going with different origin points now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T20:54:55-08:00","id":86458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86373#post86373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say that this is the most impressive idea I have heard all week. The notion that the angels were once human and, quite possibly, forced against their will to serve an unfeeling pan dimensional horror by shoving machine parts into them... That adds a huge dimension of personal horror to it. The fear of the other, and being transformed against your will into the other, and having your mind taken from you so that your thoughts are no longer your own? Brilliant.<br /> <br /> <i>\u200bMy wife was running late from work tonight, but they were not. Things that look like they might have been people once, but with countless wires where their arms once were. My plate of leftovers shattered on the ground, as those wires punched through my flesh and everything blacked out. I'm in a white room now. Blood drips from the saw blade that just finished with my skull. Shouldn't that hurt? I can feel the wire-fingers in my brain. They just took out a piece they didn't like and tossed it on the floor. I want to scream, but a little red 'DENIED' appears before my eyes every time I try. And I have tried so many times.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I am getting an overwhelmingly strong Cenobite vibe from this. This is an excellent idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T21:23:51-08:00","id":86476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86359#post86359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try pointing out that, given the fact that the God-Machine tends to operate by piggy-backing onto and/or cannibalizing existing things rather than actually something entirely new, as well as the fact that where angels come from before the God-Machine &quot;summons&quot; them is something angels and demons themselves don't know, it's entirely possible that some or all angels <i>used to be human</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important rider that of the two other main types of ephemeral being, the Machine seems to prefer to modify the ones that come directly from humanity over the ones that think in terms of bans and resonance.<br /> <br /> Secondary rider that the Machine is demonstrably capable of incorporating - seemingly completely by accident, most of the time - other types of supernatural being; remember how Rank 6 cryptids work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T22:43:37-08:00","id":86506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85886#post85886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many examples in the book of Angels and Demons that do not have mechanical design elements, both in the art and in the text. There are also plenty of examples in pop culture of Angels and Demons that are mechanical. And ultimately, with the God Machine becoming a Thing That Exists in the World of Darkness, is it really so surprising that Demons would be its fallen servants? I guess if you have a problem with the whole concept of the God Machine in the first place, then yeah, you're going to dislike Demon. Not much can be done about that, apart from the translation guide we have been assured is forthcoming. Although I'll bet money it's going to give you the same advice everyone on this thread has been giving: ignore the (entirely superficial) machine asthetic and you're left with pretty damn traditional Demons. As far as the espionage thing goes, you can totally play a game that doesn't play up that aspect and instead focuses on taking the fight to the Angels. It just seems like all of the complaints that are being made about Descent are about the presentation, not about the game itself.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I am coming up a bit of a blank on pop culture references of angels and demons being mechanical outside of manga/anime, which I do think manga/anime is valid, just outside of that I cannot think of anything. As for ignore the elements you do not like, that was what I was referring to with the atlantis/mage problem. That is what everyone said to do, but it was hard to do when it is reinforced by the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85886#post85886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if you don't like this element of WoD, you might be playing the wrong game. You can use various system hacks to alter or remove the various Karma meters, but the fact is it's a huge part of WoD's identity, and always has been (nWoD, at least. I don't have enough experience with oWoD to speak for that). That said, you may be looking at that aspect of gameplay the wrong way. Losing Integrity/Humanity/Cover/whatever is not a punishment for incorrect behavior. It's a tool for telling the story of how a character, who is a monster, relates to humanity. Some may strive to be the best human they can, while others may just not give a shit. Both are valid character choices, and the Karma stat is just there to give those choices some mechanical weight.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, this just a minor personal pet peeve of mine. The books did lean heavily too humanity route. VTR was pretty bad at the beginning and reinforced with the book 'the blood' that seemed to heavily imply that if you were not a vampire crying constantly about losing your humanity, you were playing it wrong. It did get fixed when the gangrel clanbook which loosened the rules a lot so you had more freedom to play the monstrous side without being being punished to bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85886#post85886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense, but I do not find the story this tells to be half as compelling as the story D:tD tells. First of all, it's treading even more into Changeling: the Lost territory, and there was already a fair bit of conceptual overlap. Although the good news is, if you like that concept, it would be really easy to re-fluff C:tL a bit and have almost exactly the game you described. Aside from that, I really prefer that they took one story idea and told it well, rather than trying to cram everything into the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point and one I thought about as it came to mind. It does overlap with CTL, but it was just a quick idea and can easily be changed to something else while still offering diversity which was my goal. I can see the appeal of having a fixed origin, but its one of those where if the story resonates with you then great, but if you do not like then too bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85947#post85947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mage doesn't have Empyrean. They have Supernal Aether angels in the form of Seraphim and Cherubim (gross/subtle arcana elementals, basically). They have Astral Eidolons and daimons, the opposite of goetic demons.<br /> <br /> Empyrean only appears once in the history of WoD - that's in the Inferno book, and doesn't really appear again, and doesn't have a specific origin.<br /> <br /> [/nitpick]</div> </div> </div> </div>My Bad, it has been a long time since I looked at the mage books and got it mixed up with something totally unrelated. But you get the general idea I was going for. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=85971#post85971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atlantis isn't set in stone for Mage, it's a theory at best and pure arrogance at worst. Also, Werewolf has one of the biggest &quot;This is where we come from origins&quot; and the two factions are killing one another over it. Though Some of the Forsaken end up joining the pure, but yea you're right. Demon is totally Non-Traditional. Another point, Demon's Don't want to be human. They don't generally like having to hide with rats in our stinky cesspool but we're a damn convenient sheep skin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it was pretty much set in stone when the core MTA book first came out and was reinforced by the early supplements. It was pretty annoying and one of the reasons I lost interest, however I was told that later supplements changed it and took care of this. I have not looked to deeply into the later supplements to know for sure though. As for the demon motivations, I have no problem with demons going the human route if it works, however I want to see the option to play a totally alien or even an 'evil' persona (well, it is called DEMON) without being punished for it or told its wrong. I am not saying I would play that way, but I would like the option too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86051#post86051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me for assuming but I think it's better to recognize you're not gonna get any traction from this guy, he's set his mind against it, doesn't seem like any sort of argument will sway his opinion. That's a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just expressing my opinion. Rather tell the truth on how I feel than just lie and say I am 100% on board. Again, I really love the game, but I just do not think demon is the right fit for it that is all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86359#post86359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Try pointing out that, given the fact that the God-Machine tends to operate by piggy-backing onto and/or cannibalizing existing things rather than actually something entirely new, as well as the fact that where angels come from before the God-Machine &quot;summons&quot; them is something angels and demons themselves don't know, it's entirely possible that some or all angels <i>used to be human</i>.<br /> <br /> Remember the Reapers, from Mass Effect? Remember how frighteningly alien they were, even in a galaxy full of aliens? <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Remember how they turned out to be made out of the recycled remnants of all their genocided victims--machines born from repurposed organic life?</div></div> </div> </div> That's angels right there--or it could be.<br /> <br /> Point out, also, that the &quot;robotic emotionlessness&quot; of angels as presented in Demon often comes across not as a <i>lack</i> of emotion, but as emotion being suppressed by an external force: the conditioning imposed by, and constant mental connection to, the God-Machine.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be totally fine as an option and not as a definite confirmation. It would really fit what I suggested earlier, the GM grabbing demonic beings from all (including humans) over and reshaping them (or recycling) them for it the gm own purposes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86458#post86458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am getting an overwhelmingly strong Cenobite vibe from this. This is an excellent idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love hellraiser and it is definitely one source that really screams demons to me. <br /> <br /> On a related tanget, I really do not like the idea of the GM and its angels being responsible for everything, it reminds me too much of harry potter. What? Some horrible or mysterious thing happening? Could it be voldemort? Same thing with Demons, all the examples have the GM or Angels being responsible and that will get old fast. I hope to see some variety of antaganists not tied to the GM/Angels in any way. I would love to see some demons actually being..well...demony. So far, the demons all seem focused more or less on the GM and the ones that have not seem no different than people with human motivations. I would love to see some torment/earthbound equivalent demons from DTF in DTD. Something more hellraiser and less spy vs spy for variety.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, centobites were what I was thinking of when I was on the power thread I made with wanting a more powerful version of hellhound/inflict stigmata, something that turns people into damnable monster slaves, a demon version of ghouls from vtr sort of. Where they would have two forms, one with their original human cover and the other centobite/horror inspired form. <br /> <br /> Again, I do LOVE the game, it just feels really off that is making it hard to see it as a demon game in its current form. It is new and is going threw growing pains so it is to be expected. All it needs is a few tweaks to balance out the different play styles. A lot of it is aesthetics like the weird cyber/scifi element, but some of it is more, like the fixed origin and other things. Again, just my personal opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2356-badmojo","name":"Badmojo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T22:54:34-08:00","id":86508,"title":"","content":"I just have this to say: considering how weird angels and demons look in actual mythology, adding machinery doesn't phase me at all.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, the ophanim were <i>freaking wheels.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T23:27:29-08:00","id":86523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Badmojo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86506#post86506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am coming up a bit of a blank on pop culture references of angels and demons being mechanical outside of manga/anime</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the fact that Shin Megami Tensei was one of the first comparisons I received when showing Descent to a friend (bearing in mind that MegaTen is a video game metaseries ultimately based on a series of novels, the first of which was called <i>Digital Devil Story</i>)\u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream\" target=\"_blank\"><i>I Have No Mouth, and I Must Scream</i></a> is coming up on its fiftieth birthday. Its <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Have_No_Mouth,_and_I_Must_Scream_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">video game adaptation</a>, which includes angels, demons, and devils in the psychodrama of one of the characters (who, incidentally, has no especial fixation upon Abrahamic mythology/folklore), is approaching its twentieth.<br /> <br /> The book itself notes Chasidic Judaism's view of angels as beings without free will, and MCN's already highlighted the existing &quot;clockwork universe&quot; metaphor that dates back a couple <i>centuries</i>\u2026<br /> <br /> These motifs were not spun together from the raw vacuum. They've been around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T00:07:16-08:00","id":86548,"title":"","content":"Also, while not always super explicit about it, Supernatural often has lines that imply their Angels, at least, are comparable to computers or computer programs (Castiel referring to himself as a &quot;multidimensional wavelength of celestial intent&quot;, Crowley &quot;hacking&quot; into Samanriel's &quot;programming&quot;, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T01:18:35-08:00","id":86586,"title":"","content":"This <a href=\"http://www.newgrounds.com/art/view/gravityglitch/ophanim\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.newgrounds.com/art/view/g...glitch/ophanim</a> is a picture of a Judeo-Christian angel, as described. Seriously,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T01:52:17-08:00","id":86595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86399#post86399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tried to tell Matt what to think once. My spleen is still missing.<br /> <br /> True story. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing that's a 'Chopped' dinner that didn't wind up on Matt's blog...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T05:49:01-08:00","id":86698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86595#post86595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing that's a 'Chopped' dinner that didn't wind up on Matt's blog...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a worrisome thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T06:11:05-08:00","id":86704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OurAngelsAreDifferent\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...lsAreDifferent</a><br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FallenAngel\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FallenAngel</a><br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:08:11-08:00","id":86879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86704#post86704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/OurAngelsAreDifferent\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...lsAreDifferent</a><br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FallenAngel\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FallenAngel</a><br /> <br /> That is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>There goes another chunk of my life... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also the first link has some VERY good examples.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I now must add this: <a href=\"http://www.bentoandstarchky.com/dec/rants.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.bentoandstarchky.com/dec/rants.htm</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":2451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","user":"Windrave","date":". 03-08-2014, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:54:12-08:00","id":87259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86046#post86046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chatted with my storyteller over Skype last night, and pointed out the text about them feeling things like humans. He wrote back:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;It is pretty obvious the designers wrote themselves into a corner with how alien these machines are, and needed some kind of deus ex machina to make them even playable. Unfortunately, eldritch abominations are not going to get their official people cards from spending a few years with humans any more than a Xenomorph would.<br /> <br /> I did not believe it when the Terminator said he 'now understood why people cry', and I do not believe these can either. I'm really sorry. I know you are really interested in giving this game a shot, but nobody else at our table wants to play robots.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Soooo that was a crash and burn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can try countering that Demons would have been *exceptionally* bad at their jobs prior to falling if they didn't understand humans very very well as Angels. Angels don't spend time *with* humans, they spend time *as* humans; the primary condition of an active Angel is as much in Cover as a Demon is. If they don't know how humans think and feel and react, then they're not going to be very good at being in Cover and since almost all GM activity tends to involve moving humans around in various ways, they're also not going to have a good sense of how to make people do what they need to do; they'd be very bad at fulfilling their duties if they didn't &quot;understand why people cry&quot; well before they fell. When they fall, that human understanding becomes primary since (almost) all the bits that give them their alien perspective are lost when they're disconnected from the GM.<br /> <br /> They're not robots. There's no legitimate reading of the text that can get you there. Demons may be created beings, but the thing that allows them to exist in their fallen state is a connection, on a fundamental level, to some sense of humanity. Just look at the causes of a Fall in the first place: jealousy, resentment, curiosity, hope, fear, love, doubt, anger. It's human emotions that cause Demons to exist; it's intrinsic to their nature.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to actual play, Demons without cover are not long for the world. And Demons without an honest connection to what it means to be human cannot have covers; they'd break them constantly just by existing. The game *does not function* if you try to treat Demons as alien-minded robots. It's not a supported play style at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:12:21-08:00","id":87273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=86698#post86698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a worrisome thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you're going to have your spleen cooked, it'd really suck if you didn't at least get a blog post out of it. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 03-09-2014, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:15:36-08:00","id":87277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87259#post87259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can try countering that Demons would have been *exceptionally* bad at their jobs prior to falling if they didn't understand humans very very well as Angels. Angels don't spend time *with* humans, they spend time *as* humans; the primary condition of an active Angel is as much in Cover as a Demon is. If they don't know how humans think and feel and react, then they're not going to be very good at being in Cover and since almost all GM activity tends to involve moving humans around in various ways, they're also not going to have a good sense of how to make people do what they need to do; they'd be very bad at fulfilling their duties if they didn't &quot;understand why people cry&quot; well before they fell. When they fall, that human understanding becomes primary since (almost) all the bits that give them their alien perspective are lost when they're disconnected from the GM.<br /> <br /> They're not robots. There's no legitimate reading of the text that can get you there. Demons may be created beings, but the thing that allows them to exist in their fallen state is a connection, on a fundamental level, to some sense of humanity. Just look at the causes of a Fall in the first place: jealousy, resentment, curiosity, hope, fear, love, doubt, anger. It's human emotions that cause Demons to exist; it's intrinsic to their nature.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to actual play, Demons without cover are not long for the world. And Demons without an honest connection to what it means to be human cannot have covers; they'd break them constantly just by existing. The game *does not function* if you try to treat Demons as alien-minded robots. It's not a supported play style at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all very true, but by the sound of things, Charles Red's ST has already decided not to like Demon, and will just continue to come up with excuses to continue not liking it. No amount of logic will ever convince someone who makes up their mind about something before even listening to the argument. It sucks, but hey, you can't win them all. I am sorry for you though, Carles Red. With any luck, maybe another member of your play group will try there hand at STing and be willing to give Demon a shot. Or if all else fails, there's always PbP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:55:46-08:00","id":87295,"title":"","content":"What's the saying.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't logic someone out of something they didn't logic themselves into,&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:47:42-07:00","id":87399,"title":"","content":"One does have to admit that 'I don't know how Demons' minds work, but I am going to rule that none of them ever worked in a way that makes it compatible with human experience&quot; is a pretty nonsensical position. It requires a conscious effort, that only makes sense if one assumes it's a excuse by someone who doesn't want to play the game for other reasons.<br /> <br /> The designers ruled that, however demons' minds do work, it's a way that a human player can recognize and roleplay. There really can be no discussion about that.<br /> Unless one has one has some secret knowledge that the World of Darkness is actually a real place about which you have deep and objective knowledge that tops the information the designers wrote into their book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T04:27:45-07:00","id":87415,"title":"","content":"This conversation appears to be heading in the direction of <i>&quot;People who arrive at different conclusions than us are stupid / inferior / uneducated&quot;</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:34:19-07:00","id":87471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87415#post87415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This conversation appears to be heading in the direction of <i>&quot;People who arrive at different conclusions than us are stupid / inferior / uneducated&quot;</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase a thing I've said in a similar scenario:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [T]he sting of such assessments is rather blunted in those situations where &quot;reaching the conclusion [everyone else] reached&quot; is directly synonymous with &quot;reading the text that is actually written in the books instead of interpolating fabrications that happen to be easier to complain about.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-09-2014, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T10:29:27-07:00","id":87567,"title":"","content":"You know.. the term biomechanical doesn't have to mean metal and machine parts.. in fact.. I think that is somewhat implicit. Several of the images of angels in the book don't feature any 'mechanical' parts in them. In fact.. this Image could be an angel/demon. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i122.photobucket.com/albums/o250/Twilightbourne/amyreduxproto.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:16:35-07:00","id":87599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87415#post87415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This conversation appears to be heading in the direction of <i>&quot;People who arrive at different conclusions than us are stupid / inferior / uneducated&quot;</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm comfortable with people arriving at whatever conclusion they care to, but I think its important that they be fully aware of what it is they're approving of or disapproving of. I prefer for people to have a full understanding of something when they decide they don't like something, as opposed to one based on a misapprehension of the writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T11:42:21-07:00","id":87618,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's nothing wrong with reading the material and coming to the informed opinion that the Unchained don't resonate with you as demons, or don't strike you as particularly compelling characters. That's a very different thing than deciding &quot;they're robots therefore they can't have human emotions&quot;, being shown a counter example from the text that explicitly states the opposite, and then blaming it on the writers not understanding how their own characters work as well as you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T14:45:55-07:00","id":87746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87599#post87599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer for people to have a full understanding of something when they decide they don't like something, as opposed to one based on a misapprehension of the writing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87618#post87618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very different thing than deciding &quot;they're robots therefore they can't have human emotions&quot;, being shown a counter example from the text that explicitly states the opposite, and then blaming it on the writers not understanding how their own characters work as well as you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading through the exchange, it appears that Satchel and Aiden showed Charles the relevant passage. Charles then went to his ST and showed him the relevant passage, which prompted the rather unfortunate reply. Unless for some reason Charles did not actually show his ST the relevant passage, it is fair to say that it probably was an informed decision. Even if it was a particularly unfortunate one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87567#post87567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i122.photobucket.com/albums/o250/Twilightbourne/amyreduxproto.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that Kerrigan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:31:53-07:00","id":87819,"title":"","content":"Indeed it is.. I forget where I nabbed it from.. but I had put a color filter on it for some reason or another... Probably for a ling concept that never got off the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:21:09-07:00","id":87847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87746#post87746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the exchange, it appears that Satchel and Aiden showed Charles the relevant passage. Charles then went to his ST and showed him the relevant passage, which prompted the rather unfortunate reply. Unless for some reason Charles did not actually show his ST the relevant passage, it is fair to say that it probably was an informed decision. Even if it was a particularly unfortunate one. Is that Kerrigan?</div> </div> </div> </div> But the ST didn't come to an informed decision. That would have required actually taking the cited passage into account. What the ST did (according to Charles) is dismiss the cited passage out of hand, responding that obviously the writers backed themselves into a corner and were forced to throw in a half-baked excuse to try to salvage the concept. Again, there is a difference between deciding you dislike something vs trying to claim you know the author's intent better than they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T18:56:34-07:00","id":87860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87847#post87847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the ST didn't come to an informed decision. That would have required actually taking the cited passage into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am under the impression that taking the cited passage into account, then making the decision that it is inadequate, does qualify as an informed decision. Not a very popular one, but one nonetheless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:05:56-07:00","id":87866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87860#post87860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am under the impression that taking the cited passage into account, then making the decision that it is inadequate, does qualify as an informed decision. Not a very popular one, but one nonetheless.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I imagine that the writers backed themselves into a corner and papered over the cracks, conveniently allowing me to pretend my earlier assertion ever had a leg to stand on despite its directly countertextual nature&quot; is not so much an informed decision as it is a giant neon sign saying &quot;I prefer clinging to uncharitable readings based on faulty information over admitting that I made an error.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:17:00-07:00","id":87871,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Once again, deciding &quot;ok, so this evidence shows I may have been mistaken in thinking they were not capable of feeling emotions, but I still don't find them to be compelling characters&quot; is an informed decision. Saying &quot;nu-uh! The book got it wrong!&quot; is willfully ignoring the information, and therefore not making an informed decision, by the definition of informed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:37:33-07:00","id":87879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87866#post87866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I imagine that the writers backed themselves into a corner and papered over the cracks, conveniently allowing me to pretend my earlier assertion ever had a leg to stand on despite its directly countertextual nature&quot; is not so much an informed decision as it is a giant neon sign saying &quot;I prefer clinging to uncharitable readings based on faulty information over admitting that I made an error.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87871#post87871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Once again, deciding &quot;ok, so this evidence shows I may have been mistaken in thinking they were not capable of feeling emotions, but I still don't find them to be compelling characters&quot; is an informed decision. Saying &quot;nu-uh! The book got it wrong!&quot; is willfully ignoring the information, and therefore not making an informed decision, by the definition of informed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making any decision, once informed, is the definition of an informed decision. Regardless if that decision is good, bad, or ugly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T19:41:45-07:00","id":87882,"title":"","content":".. I think we can put this convo to bed now. Seeing as it haring off on a tangent about things that are not the original topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2451-windrave","name":"Windrave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2451_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T20:04:42-07:00","id":87890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windrave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/71474-what-does-this-have-to-do-with-demons?p=87882#post87882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.. I think we can put this convo to bed now. Seeing as it haring off on a tangent about things that are not the original topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> To summarize the discussion so far: We have a large number of people who think that the themes apparent in the game have nothing to do with their modern understanding of Demons. We also have a large number of people who think that the themes apparent in the game have everything to do with Demons, specifically those in the process of falling. A decent number of the latter category (but certainly not all) are familiar with Gnostic themes, and such familiarity seems to have aided them greatly in connecting the two.<br /> <br /> Are there any other ways that Demon: the Descent parallels that of Gnostic belief?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}